{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes","id":87146,"title":"Solars are Heroes.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-08T18:52:20-08:00","id":87146,"title":"Solars are Heroes.","content":"In the sense that they are good people performing good deeds in order to make the world a better place. Solarness is not about beating down everyone else with your glorious, golden dick.<br /> <br /> Some Solars will not be heroes, but those are exceptions.<br /> <br /> Heroes can have flaws. Heroes can live in complex worlds and have to grapple with difficult decisions. Heroes can have adversaries who are black-hearted villains or who are sympathetic, noble opponents with contrary goals.<br /> <br /> It's fine to look at the ways heroes fail or the ways people with power aren't heroic. I am not saying that playing a Solar who is a hero is better than playing one who is not. The problem is when we start talking about the edge as though it's the center. Exalted is not a game about how humanity is horrible, heroism is a lie, and the PC is just another asshole clawing is way to the top. Rather, Creation is a setting where humans (and non-humans) can be horrible, heroism can be false, and there are many assholes clawing their way to the top.<br /> <br /> That's why it needs Solars. Bringing light to the darkness is only meaningful if it's dark.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":17}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T19:02:13-08:00","id":87152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes#post87146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the sense that they are good people performing good deeds in order to make the world a better place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Better for whom?<br /> <br /> The conquests of Genghis Khan probably made the world a better place for the Mongols, and even various Turkic peoples (who probably actually benefited from it more in the long run; trace it for long enough, and you might get to the Ottoman Turks, who could be argued to have made the world a better place for tens of thousands of exiled Spanish Jewish people).<br /> <br /> That doesn't preclude Genghis Khan from having led/initiated a series of conflicts with something like the fourth largest death toll of any human endeavor in history.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T19:09:27-08:00","id":87154,"title":"","content":"That might be how you play. It is how I play quite a few of my my characters too, but not every solar is a glorious, shining paladin.<br /> <br /> Some of them are tormented beings, cast out for having exalted. Some lash out at the world, becoming the monsters that the world believed them to be.<br /> <br /> Others are quiet, stealthy, dark heroes stalking the world like Batman stalking Gotham.<br /> <br /> Hippokrene, I think you and I would enjoy playing at the same table. But it takes all kinds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1199-mister-lion","name":"Mister Lion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1199_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T19:15:36-08:00","id":87155,"title":"","content":"is this how it is in Ed3, because ed2 drill to me that exalted are great people but not necesary good people","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T19:32:21-08:00","id":87158,"title":"","content":"No, actually, I'm pretty sure the intent of using the archaic definition of 'hero' is exactly so things like this aren't taken as a given. <br /> <br /> Frankly I'd find Creation far more a boring place if a majority of the Exalted were heroes as modern people conceive of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/748-ultrafennec","name":"UltraFennec","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar748_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T19:52:05-08:00","id":87165,"title":"","content":"Sometimes, I feel like playing a Solar Paladin of unwavering principle who shoulders by himself the burdens and sacrifices that lesser heroes would be forced to pass on to their followers. <br /> <br /> Other times, I feel like playing a Guildsman who casually sells his enemies into slavery to the Fair Folk to make a point and corrupts entire kingdoms into shadowlands to sell them to the Deathlords. <br /> <br /> I'm moody that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T20:12:50-08:00","id":87173,"title":"","content":"There's really only one thing that I feel is really obligated of every Solar, and this is purely a preconception that is never really supported anywhere in the books except by implication: It is a universal failure condition for the Solars to succumb to the Great Curse and become like their First Age counterparts, regardless of whether they are paladin figures or thieves or what have you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T20:38:33-08:00","id":87181,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mister Lion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87154#post87154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That might be how you play. It is how I play quite a few of my characters too, but not every solar is a glorious, shining paladin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shining doesn\u2019t have much to do with being heroic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Some of them are tormented beings, cast out for having exalted. Some lash out at the world, becoming the monsters that the world believed them to be. </div> </div> </div>As I said, there are exceptions, but they need to be treated as such.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Others are quiet, stealthy, dark heroes stalking the world like Batman stalking Gotham. </div> </div> </div>Batman could totally be a Solar. He might not shine, but he\u2019s very showy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T20:42:10-08:00","id":87182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>UltraFennec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87158#post87158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, actually, I'm pretty sure the intent of using the archaic definition of 'hero' is exactly so things like this aren't taken as a given.<br /> <br /> Frankly I'd find Creation far more a boring place if a majority of the Exalted were heroes as modern people conceive of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Solars aren't the majority of Exalted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87165#post87165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometimes, I feel like playing a Solar Paladin of unwavering principle who shoulders by himself the burdens and sacrifices that lesser heroes would be forced to pass on to their followers.<br /> <br /> Other times, I feel like playing a Guildsman who casually sells his enemies into slavery to the Fair Folk to make a point and corrupts entire kingdoms into shadowlands to sell them to the Deathlords.<br /> <br /> I'm moody that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can play a vampire who is an animalistic beast, a vampire who is a suave and manipulative bastard, and a vampire who is a compassionate humanitarian who only feeds from animals.<br /> <br /> That the PC can play a large range of characters, some of whom are not heroic, doesn't preclude default statements. And default statements, such as 'Solars are heroes' and 'Vampires have an inner beast' are important.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T20:46:11-08:00","id":87187,"title":"","content":"If I understand correctly, 3e is taking us away from the notion of an Exaltation as an ineffable, autonomous construct that Exalts people for reasons nobody can quite nail down. Instead, each Exalt is literally Chosen by an Incarna. What this implies, if true, is that people who become Solars almost certainly have demonstrated some intent or drive that makes it reasonable to expect they will become a force for good in the world.<br /> <br /> In any case, that's certainly a requirement of player characters in my games. I am not interested in running a game about shameless assholes with world-shaking power. I am interested in a game where the Age of Sorrows is confronted by divinely empowered people who want to do good. Any argument predicated on Solars being generally evil (or even generally assholes) is not useful to any Exalted game I will ever run.<br /> <br /> The archaic definition of &quot;hero&quot; which UltraFennec notes applies to all Exalted. Literally every person who Exalts has at least one Virtue rated high enough to compel some kind of heroic mode of action. Solars are a class above that. Where Dragon-Blooded don't do anything to earn their Exaltations, Sidereals are defined from birth by their Exaltations, and Lunars are offered Exaltation simply for the will to survive, Solars are supposed to be people who are not only great, but <i>good</i>. The Unconquered Sun doesn't Choose people for being selfish assassins, no matter how many Ability dots they have and how high their Conviction is. He doesn't make merchant-princes living the unexamined life into Eclipses, no matter how high their Socialize and Bureaucracy are. He looks into the souls of the great, and once in a while, he says &quot;yes, you are a person who will use My power to make the world a better place&quot;. That's who Solars are.<br /> <br /> And I'd go one further than that. I'd say that characterisation of Solars is what Exalted is <i>for</i>. At least, it's the thing about Exalted that makes it most attractive to me. Because Exalted sets up a world full of existential threats, terrible injustices, and corruption in every court, and then it knocks that world down by saying &quot;except the greatest power in the world is reserved for the good guys&quot;. Exalted is a statement that hope and idealism can triumph. Exalted is a statement that <i>things can get better</i>, even if only through concerted and extraordinary effort and dedication.<br /> <br /> The nature of Exaltation as an irrevocable and unassailable gift means that any Exalt can start out as a good guy and then turn into something else. Exalts are human. But whatever happens to a Solar after their Exaltation, I agree strongly with hippokrene: the default state of a Solar is Person Who Sets Things Right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":19}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2404-chant","name":"Chant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2404_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T20:49:37-08:00","id":87188,"title":"","content":"Last I checked Solars were heroes in the way the ancient Greeks used the term, not the modern definition. And I haven't seen anything saying this is changing in 3E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":16}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T20:50:00-08:00","id":87190,"title":"","content":"That's wonderfully put, Chant. Why didn't you make this thread? It would have saved me so much time! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87173#post87173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's really only one thing that I feel is really obligated of every Solar, and this is purely a preconception that is never really supported anywhere in the books except by implication: It is a universal failure condition for the Solars to succumb to the Great Curse and become like their First Age counterparts, regardless of whether they are paladin figures or thieves or what have you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this.<br /> <br /> The fall of the Solars of the First Age is supposed to be tragic. They were heroes who brought peace and prosperity to the world, but that twisted into something monstrous, and the Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded had to put them down like mad dogs.<br /> <br /> That only works as a tragedy if the Solars didn't start out as a group of amoral assholes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 03-08-2014, 11:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T21:03:26-08:00","id":87195,"title":"","content":"I think there's a widespread meme that Good Is Boring, and that's why people want Solars to be nigh-inescapably disposed toward being shitheads. And I don't agree with that notion.<br /> <br /> The thing about the Unconquered Sun is that he embodies every aspect of good, despite many of those aspects conflicting with each other when applied to the real world. Different Solars will very frequently have different ideas about what it means to be good, and view each other's actions in different moral frameworks. The Eclipse who accumulates power in order to ultimately free the Threshold from the grip of the Guild is good; the Twilight who binds elementals into dangerous servitude to fight the Fair Folk in her quest to protect Creation from dissolution is good; the Zenith who starts a bloody revolution to build a free and equal society is good. All three of these people could think the other two are wasting their time. All three could accuse the other two of doing something outright immoral! Good comes into conflict with good <i>all the time</i>, and that's why it's more interesting to me that Solars are inherently good than that they subvert the bland-good-guy stereotype by actually being inevitably terrible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":19}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2404-chant","name":"Chant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2404_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T21:08:48-08:00","id":87199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87182#post87182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can play a vampire who is an animalistic beast, a vampire who is a suave and manipulative bastard, and a vampire who is a compassionate humanitarian who only feeds from animals.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>A better example of a kind vampire would probably be one who feeds off of blood donated to a blood bank, and then, the blood that's not considered fit for transfusions. Like someone who's just cleaning out the fridge, essentially.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T21:12:24-08:00","id":87200,"title":"","content":"I don't want them to be indisposed toward being shitheads, but neither do I think that the default condition for them should be 'chosen for being good people who want to do good deeds.' That's just as boring as the default condition being 'chosen for being bad people who want to do bad deeds.'<br /> <br /> I don't think the setting is very interesting if the default condition for the Exalted, Solars, Lunars, whichever, is based on the idea that they must have a drive to make the world a better place. Part of what draws me to the game is that not only do I, as a player, have the option to play an anti-hero in truth or even a villainous person given 'righteous' power, but that the setting backs that up as well.<br /> <br /> Default statements ARE important, and at least to me it's very important that that default statement NOT be slanted toward any particular angle except one: the need to be a driven individual willing to use the power they're given. Whether that becomes good, evil (and what are those but defined by people?), or anything in between, whether it's world-shaking or completely self-absorbed, should be up to the people at the table, not the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/748-ultrafennec","name":"UltraFennec","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar748_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T21:14:21-08:00","id":87202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87190#post87190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's wonderfully put, Chant. Why didn't you make this thread? It would have saved me so much time! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Considering my session timed out while I was composing it, I'm afraid your time savings would ultimately have been zero-sum. (That actually happens to me more than half the time I post here.) But thanks! I was honestly pretty surprised to see my posts in this thread accrue Likes so quickly, and being called out with an expressed compliment gives me the warm fuzzies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2404-chant","name":"Chant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2404_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T21:16:28-08:00","id":87203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87195#post87195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there's a widespread meme that Good Is Boring, and that's why people want Solars to be nigh-inescapably disposed toward being shitheads. And I don't agree with that notion.<br /> <br /> The thing about the Unconquered Sun is that he embodies every aspect of good, despite many of those aspects conflicting with each other when applied to the real world. Different Solars will very frequently have different ideas about what it means to be good, and view each other's actions in different moral frameworks. The Eclipse who accumulates power in order to ultimately free the Threshold from the grip of the Guild is good; the Twilight who binds elementals into dangerous servitude to fight the Fair Folk in her quest to protect Creation from dissolution is good; the Zenith who starts a bloody revolution to build a free and equal society is good. All three of these people could think the other two are wasting their time. All three could accuse the other two of doing something outright immoral! Good comes into conflict with good <i>all the time</i>, and that's why it's more interesting to me that Solars are inherently good than that they subvert the bland-good-guy stereotype by actually being inevitably terrible.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What about the one that works to take over the Guild themselves? What about the one that treats with the Fair Folk as useful tools for their aims? What about the one that builds an equal society through bloody empire and conquest?<br /> <br /> My contention is that the folks that *aren't* good folks, and have just as much power as the 'good' folks, are what makes the setting interesting. How is making the default Solar condition 'good guy' (in more words with more nuance, obviously) helping the setting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/748-ultrafennec","name":"UltraFennec","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar748_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T21:22:53-08:00","id":87208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>UltraFennec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87203#post87203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My contention is that the folks that *aren't* good folks, and have just as much power as the 'good' folks, are what makes the setting interesting. How is making the default Solar condition 'good guy' (in more words with more nuance, obviously) helping the setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>By emphatically moving it away from the shitdark approach from previous editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T21:30:29-08:00","id":87212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87199#post87199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A better example of a kind vampire would probably be one who feeds off of blood donated to a blood bank, and then, the blood that's not considered fit for transfusions. Like someone who's just cleaning out the fridge, essentially.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, that is a better example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T21:37:15-08:00","id":87216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>UltraFennec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87203#post87203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My contention is that the folks that *aren't* good folks, and have just as much power as the 'good' folks, are what makes the setting interesting. How is making the default Solar condition 'good guy' (in more words with more nuance, obviously) helping the setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue it's helping the setting by defining the baseline mode of conflict between Solars, and against Solars, as being conflict rooted in moral ambiguity. You don't come into conflict with the Bull of the North because he's evil; you come into conflict with him because you think the good he's invested in, of enriching his people and toppling an evil empire, is outweighed by another good, such as the preservation of life or the allocation of the Realm's resources to fighting Deathlords. Saying &quot;all Solars are good by default&quot; and then describing the ways in which different Solars see different flavors of good in themselves and others is much more interesting to me than saying &quot;Solars are people with the will to be great&quot;. Beings with the will to be great, and the power to achieve greatness, are <i>all over</i> the setting without throwing Solars in the mix. Saying that being Solar has no moral implications, that Solars are simply the greatest of the great and recognised for that, bores me to <i>tears</i>, because it's just a distillation of Creation's status quo premise, which is that life sucks because there are super-powerful entities running around being selfish and amoral. What is the point of the Return Of The Solars if they aren't there to defy the Sorrows that define this Age?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2404-chant","name":"Chant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2404_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T21:38:47-08:00","id":87218,"title":"","content":"I think the issue is if Solar exaltation just comes to those with drive their return doesn't really mean a whole lot. Creation is still screwed it just has 300 more Jackasses running around and fucking things up for everybody. Honestly I have to agree that Solars should (at least when they initially get their Second Breath) have a spark of heroism and a drive to do what they think is right and make the world a better place instead of &quot;Well I got awesome golden sunlight powers now lets go conquer shit and get me some hookers&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon","name":"Calboon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar223_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T21:57:17-08:00","id":87225,"title":"","content":"First off, hippokrene, I love the video in your signature!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes#post87146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the sense that they are good people performing good deeds in order to make the world a better place. Solarness is not about beating down everyone else with your glorious, golden dick.<br /> <br /> Some Solars will not be heroes, but those are exceptions.<br /> <br /> Heroes can have flaws. Heroes can live in complex worlds and have to grapple with difficult decisions. Heroes can have adversaries who are black-hearted villains or who are sympathetic, noble opponents with contrary goals.<br /> <br /> It's fine to look at the ways heroes fail or the ways people with power aren't heroic. I am not saying that playing a Solar who is a hero is better than playing one who is not. The problem is when we start talking about the edge as though it's the center. Exalted is not a game about how humanity is horrible, heroism is a lie, and the PC is just another asshole clawing is way to the top. Rather, Creation is a setting where humans (and non-humans) can be horrible, heroism can be false, and there are many assholes clawing their way to the top.<br /> <br /> That's why it needs Solars. Bringing light to the darkness is only meaningful if it's dark.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I feel the same way about Exalted, specifically Solars in Creations. A little light never hurt anyone.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2475-the-praetorian","name":"The Praetorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2475_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T21:58:44-08:00","id":87226,"title":"","content":"What is good? Calling solars good just confuses what their heroism is. Saying that all solars are good is muddling the thematic inspirations exalted draws from.Hitler Gahndi, and Churchill all were trying to do good, and are likely exaltion candidates. You could argue that everyone is trying to be good but we differ in the understanding of that. Would your goodmean that all solars have a minimum compassion rating?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2239-lyre","name":"lyre","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T22:00:04-08:00","id":87228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Calboon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87218#post87218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the issue is if Solar exaltation just comes to those with drive their return doesn't really mean a whole lot. Creation is still screwed it just has 300 more Jackasses running around and fucking things up for everybody. Honestly I have to agree that Solars should (at least when they initially get their Second Breath) have a spark of heroism and a drive to do what they think is right and make the world a better place instead of &quot;Well I got awesome golden sunlight powers now lets go conquer shit and get me some hookers&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Power corrupts, and absolute power corrupts absolutely, but I agree a Solar's origin should begin as something righteous and noble, where it goes from there though is up to them. This is why I really dislike the entire concept of the great curse, sure it makes for a great plot device to explain why the Solars have been gone for so long, but it also looms over the setting making it so even the most noble character will eventually tear down all they created. I feel like the great curse should have only effected those first age Solars who fought in the primordial war, instead of every person who gets the exaltation for the rest of time. I also don't see why some solar hasn't perceived the great curse and found a way to break it, I mean they can kill and bind primordials, but its impossible for some elder twilight to shatter the curse?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T22:01:32-08:00","id":87229,"title":"","content":"Solars are agents of change who oppose the status quo; if they were totally happy and satisfied with how things things were going, they probably wouldn't have ever Exalted. <br /> <br /> Fortunately, there's a lot of things that are wrong with the current state of Creation. The Guild, the Realm and most nations are various forms and degree of corrupt and evil. And so the Solars, as people who often want to change the world, find themselves in a position where it's very easy to make things better. Or make them worse.<br /> <br /> The Bull of the North is the classic example. He's great for the Icewalkers; he's leading them to a new era, he's helping to change their lifestyle, he's helping to form them into a civilization. Awesome. To them, the Bull is a great man and a &quot;good&quot; person. But to the many of the people he's conquered and the nations he's invaded or slaughtered he's viewed as a dangerous monster.<br /> <br /> The comparison to Genghis Khan was quite apt. <br /> <br /> The Solar's aren't &quot;good.&quot;But they are heroes. They will change the world. Ideally for the better, but possibly for the worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T22:01:56-08:00","id":87231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87216#post87216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd argue it's helping the setting by defining the baseline mode of conflict between Solars, and against Solars, as being conflict rooted in moral ambiguity. You don't come into conflict with the Bull of the North because he's evil; you come into conflict with him because you think the good he's invested in, of enriching his people and toppling an evil empire, is outweighed by another good, such as the preservation of life or the allocation of the Realm's resources to fighting Deathlords. Saying &quot;all Solars are good by default&quot; and then describing the ways in which different Solars see different flavors of good in themselves and others is much more interesting to me than saying &quot;Solars are people with the will to be great&quot;. Beings with the will to be great, and the power to achieve greatness, are <i>all over</i> the setting without throwing Solars in the mix. Saying that being Solar has no moral implications, that Solars are simply the greatest of the great and recognised for that, bores me to <i>tears</i>, because it's just a distillation of Creation's status quo premise, which is that life sucks because there are super-powerful entities running around being selfish and amoral. What is the point of the Return Of The Solars if they aren't there to defy the Sorrows that define this Age?</div> </div> </div> </div>The point is that they're the mightiest of the Exalted Host, and nobody can ignore them, whether they do good or do ill. What you find boring to tears is, essentially, the greater part of what I find compelling and interesting about them. <br /> <br /> Why *should* they be any different than the rest of the powerful folks that have screwed over the world? Just because they have one type of power versus another shouldn't make that difference. That should come from the person who gained the power, not the power itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/748-ultrafennec","name":"UltraFennec","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar748_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T22:07:57-08:00","id":87234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>UltraFennec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87231#post87231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why *should* they be any different than the rest of the powerful folks that have screwed over the world?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Being hand-selected by a Compassion 5 ubergod&quot; seems ample reason to me. Sol probably isn't picking out a lot of people who would make better Abyssals than Solars, and if he is then something is terribly wrong with EX3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T22:20:54-08:00","id":87236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87234#post87234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Being hand-selected by a Compassion 5 ubergod&quot; seems ample reason to me. Sol probably isn't picking out a lot of people who would make better Abyssals than Solars, and if he is then something is terribly wrong with EX3.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well for one, pretty sure the Glories characterization of UCS as a compassion 5 ubergod is going away. Now he's a mighty and flawed perfection, he's the goddamn Sun, once the shield and weapon against the Wyld and is now the guy on top. How he's actually depicted varies, his form is ambiguous and varies from culture to culture. Very similar to his 1E characterization.<br /> <br /> This speaks volumes about the Solar Exalted. They're power, they're flawed perfection, and they were once a weapon to kill an immensely powerful thing that was put in charge. They are not good, they are not evil. The Solar Exalted are chosen because they have the drive and motivation to use the power, and come out on top. The Solar Exaltation is a metaphysical gun, but you only get it if you're going to pull the trigger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T22:24:00-08:00","id":87237,"title":"","content":"Except Sol is also Temperance, Conviction, and Valor 5. He's either in perfect balance, or constantly being pulled in multiple directions if we use the mechanics as a guide. <br /> <br /> Again, I'm not advocating for Solars all being 'people who would make better Abyssals.'<br /> <br /> I'm advocating that for the purposes of the setting and making the game unique, that making the Solars inherently 'good' in some way detracts from the experience.<br /> <br /> Are most players going to default to that? Probably, it's very natural in RPGs.<br /> <br /> But saying that it being otherwise is wrong is just...it rankles. It goes against the things that inspired the game. It puts a worldview into Creation that has no realistic hope of existing in that kind of world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/748-ultrafennec","name":"UltraFennec","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar748_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T22:29:24-08:00","id":87241,"title":"","content":"Disclaimer: If you want to interpret or adapt the setting such that, in your game, Solars have no defining pattern of goodness, I have no interest in stopping you. I'm aware of the folly of badwrongfun. But I hope that any Storyteller who wants to base their game in that interpretation is careful to clarify that to their players. Be aware that a person who picks up the Exalted corebook and goes &quot;whoa, awesome, I want to play this&quot; very well may have that reaction because they understand it to pose the Solar condition as &quot;you are a good guy, so the Sun made you awesome&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2404-chant","name":"Chant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2404_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T22:29:38-08:00","id":87242,"title":"","content":"evil or not good doesnt mean that they are assholes. A man whos family was ruined by a guild merchant prince and everyone but him ended up dead or sold to slavery exalts as a nigth caste and now he wants to kill all the high ranking people in the guild and their families as revenge. Thats a not asshole not good exalt, and his actions will change the world, for good or bad depends on what others do to fill the void of the guild starting to crumble, but there will be a change and from his point of view is a righteous cause.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1351,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","user":"Sakii","date":". 09-13-2020, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T22:31:04-08:00","id":87243,"title":"","content":"I generally agree with this, and the reason I'm constantly irritated at the Great Curse as a setting element is how it's a slap in the face to that idea. Though even if Solars aren't meant to be People Who Set Things Right and are instead people who make human mistakes with superhuman power, it would still go against that thesis by absolving them of guilt for their mistakes. All it takes for people to make mistakes is to give them any situation that's not black and white, there doesn't need to be any supernatural force pushing you to make mistakes.<br /> <br /> Whatever the tone, I just hope it's consistent. 2E had a presentation of Solars who were arrogant douchebags, right down to their Charm text constantly singing their praises about everything, but you had to tolerate them because they were the only ones capable of fixing anything. Thankfully the 3E previewed charms for Solars majorly toned this down, so I have hope that the rest of the Solar presentation will do a lot to help alleviate my distaste for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T22:31:33-08:00","id":87244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>UltraFennec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87237#post87237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except Sol is also Temperance, Conviction, and Valor 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>I strongly believe this won't be the case anymore come Ex3, and I don't believe this was the case until Glories.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T22:34:22-08:00","id":87247,"title":"","content":"No.<br /> The biggest problem is most people see themselves are 'good/heroic', so either the statement is meaningless, or you inject objective morality into the mix, which together with a statement about the goodness of Solars will just descend to farce, where the letter of the law becomes an objective measure of goodness, upheld as a ridiculous setting conceit (which is something I doubt any of the devs would put their names on).<br /> <br /> What's more, it's lazy. If all Solars are good, what was the Usurpation? If it was merely those particular Solar had fallen form grace, why the Jade Prison? Why hunt down and kill those that remain? Ultimately it's either going to end in a boring &quot;Color-Coded for Your Convenience&quot; world where some splats are purely villainous to counter-balance the purely heroic Solars<br /> <br /> Honestly though, if youwant to houserule that all second Age Solars are heroic good in your game, more power to you. But don't waltz in and say this is somehow the proper or better way to play the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":726,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/726-amine-hsu","user":"Amine Hsu","date":". 03-09-2014, 03:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/726-amine-hsu","name":"Amine Hsu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar726_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T22:36:22-08:00","id":87248,"title":"","content":"I think people are getting a bit hung up on Solars = heros = paladins. Batman for example is the quintessential Night Caste, and a very powerful force for good. However he's also obsessive, paranoid, distrustful and occasionally treats his close friends and adopted family with something that often resembles abuse. He's a good guy and a hero, but a lot more nuanced than &quot;superhero = good = paladin&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T22:44:20-08:00","id":87251,"title":"","content":"the Usurpation happened because the sidreals had a prophesy that the solar were going to destroy the world, not those specific solars bot the solars in general, killing the current 300 will just make another 300 who will destroy the world, so Jade Prision. And the main reason was the Great Curse that everyone thinks is the solar fault, you turn into a solar you will go mad with power no mater how virtuous he was at the start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T22:46:34-08:00","id":87254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes#post87146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the sense that they are good people performing good deeds in order to make the world a better place. Solarness is not about beating down everyone else with your glorious, golden dick.</div> </div> </div> </div>This has never been the definition of hero envoked for Exalted in its history. Nor is it the term as applied ot a great deal of inspirational sources for Solar Exalted. Being a Solar Exalt is about being a larger than life person who does great deeds. Those deeds can be good or horrible. Or either based on the eye of the beholder. Or the Solar, like any potentially great person, can squander their glory as well.<br /> <br /> This isn't the fucking superfriends.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes#post87146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some Solars will not be heroes, but those are exceptions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on your definition of heroic. I find it juevenille and more or less tossing out a thesis the game is built on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes#post87146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heroes can have flaws. Heroes can live in complex worlds and have to grapple with difficult decisions. Heroes can have adversaries who are black-hearted villains or who are sympathetic, noble opponents with contrary goals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hero is not the antithesis of villain. Heroes simply need to be great people by the definitions that the gameline has used, rather than your definition laid-out normatively becuase...you say so I guess?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes#post87146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's fine to look at the ways heroes fail or the ways people with power aren't heroic. I am not saying that playing a Solar who is a hero is better than playing one who is not. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Just aberrant apparently. And implicatively evil, whatever that means.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes#post87146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... The problem is when we start talking about the edge as though it's the center. Exalted is not a game about how humanity is horrible, heroism is a lie, and the PC is just another asshole clawing is way to the top. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a game where there is no objective morality, the world does run on economics and sociology as we undeerstand it on Earth, and the main characters are larger than life legendary individuals. Though that does include a little bit of human selfishness and greed as a default. Sorry. Humans have a good trackrecord of indeed sucking. Good stories come from that anyhow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes#post87146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Rather, Creation is a setting where humans (and non-humans) can be horrible, heroism can be false, and there are many assholes clawing their way to the top.</div> </div> </div> </div>What does &quot;Heroism can be false&quot; even mean?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes#post87146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's why it needs Solars. Bringing light to the darkness is only meaningful if it's dark.</div> </div> </div> </div>Solars are a deconstruction of the glories hero returns. Solars are likely to be your next Caesar or Augustus as much as they're going to be your Cincinnatus. This isn't a game of Color Coded For Your Convenience Good Heroes versus Evil Scoundrals. Any declarations that it is, especially someone around as long as you have been, seems kind of hopefully naive or willfully rejecting of the game as its source material and original presentation have been presented.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T22:58:58-08:00","id":87265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87251#post87251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Usurpation happened because the sidreals had a prophesy that the solar were going to destroy the world, not those specific solars bot the solars in general, killing the current 300 will just make another 300 who will destroy the world, so Jade Prision. And the main reason was the Great Curse that everyone thinks is the solar fault, you turn into a solar you will go mad with power no mater how virtuous he was at the start.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically this. The Usurpation was a thing, because Solars were God-King Nukes waiting to go off. These beings were weapons. They were powerful, and power corrupted. They had no boundaries, they like their patron, defined the edge of Creation by burning away with twisted chaos. There was no restraint, they did as they pleased, and none could tell them different. That course is ultimately very destructive. Sidereals saw this, created the Jade Prison, and amassed all the forces they could to kill these mighty corrupted godkings and seal them away before they destroyed everything.<br /> <br /> Fast forward to the Second Age, Time of tumult. The ancient terrible things are coming back slowly, same Exaltations, same potential for power, but this time they have an example. They have a boundary, they have restraint because of their nature of newly made, and legends of what happened before.<br /> <br /> The tragedy is that history may be doomed to repeat itself, but this time there's a chance for it not to turn out they way it did, not a return to the First Age, but a rise of a new age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T23:00:28-08:00","id":87268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87181#post87181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shining doesn\u2019t have much to do with being heroic.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue I think Levi is noting here is that apparently shining gold means you are expected to be a &quot;good guy&quot; in the modern media sense. Instead of a &quot;great guy&quot; in the historic Big Name History or classicla sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87181#post87181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I said, there are exceptions, but they need to be treated as such.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why precisely? You've said they should, but not why that should be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87181#post87181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Batman could totally be a Solar. He might not shine, but he\u2019s very showy.</div> </div> </div> </div>So are Conan, Sindbad, Zorayas, Zirak, Mosis, Gilgamesh, Heracles, Musashi, or Ezio. They are also a list of murderers, conquerers, comitters of genocide or wreckless idiots. Sindbad never did a damned thing becuase it was &quot;right&quot; as far as I gather, but because he didn't want to die. Moses led a religion but killed nations in God's name. And these are people that inspire Solar Exalted. And to some extant, are monsters to us at times and still great.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87182#post87182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars aren't the majority of Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why should Solars be special good guy Exalted? This hasn't been said and it relegates your anima to a morality, which is blatently lazy on one hand and against a lot of the game's founding thesis on the other. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87181#post87181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can play a vampire who is an animalistic beast, a vampire who is a suave and manipulative bastard, and a vampire who is a compassionate humanitarian who only feeds from animals.<br /> <br /> That the PC can play a large range of characters, some of whom are not heroic, doesn't preclude default statements. And default statements, such as 'Solars are heroes' and 'Vampires have an inner beast' are important.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are not really as comparable though. One is a statement on the nature of the beast ot create a conflict between Man and the descent into monstrosity. The other is &quot;Give a man the power of the Most High to do what he will with and a mandate to use it. What legends will they tell of his deeds?&quot; The first is a vehilce of personal horror. The latter is a more rhetorical question. All that is required is you make legends. You can be the Savior of the Jews, the Butcher of the Caanenites or both. You could be the rich merchant who sailed Seven Seas or the man who doomed seven voyages and got rich off of it. <br /> <br /> So I restate. Glowing gold doesn't make you suddenly a saint. Not being saint doesn't make you an aberrant Solar. All that matters most in the end is being great. Greatness is not goodness in Exalted's history, and even with less shitdark of 2e's presentation, should not be the goal now.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T23:08:22-08:00","id":87270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87208#post87208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By emphatically moving it away from the shitdark approach from previous editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>All this does is imply everyone else is not so inherently prone to &quot;goodness&quot; and so if it weren't for Solars were going to fuck everything up and still will. It takes their motives and makes them less inherently &quot;good&quot; than the Solars. Everyone else is morally inept <i>by default</i> if Solars are the good ones by default. It doesn't avoid shitdark. It makes things cartoonish.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T23:08:57-08:00","id":87271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>UltraFennec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87237#post87237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm advocating that for the purposes of the setting and making the game unique, that making the Solars inherently 'good' in some way detracts from the experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunars, as a group, are driven to protect Creation. Some do that by fighting Wyld-spawn, some do it by striving to strengthen societies, some do it by trying to put the Solars back in charge, etc.<br /> Sidereals, as a group, are driven to uphold Creation. Some think that's best done by keeping Solars from fucking it up, some think that's best done by supporting the Solars and making Creation a place of virtue and strength, and some think that's best done by addressing threats to Creation directly.<br /> <br /> Do these default group characterisations detract from the setting, or from Lunar and Sidereal gameplay? Neither of these types of Exalt is Chosen for their &quot;goodness&quot;, and yet both seem to have a predisposition toward altruistic behavior. If that doesn't detract from the experience, I don't see why it should be a problem for Solars to also take the &quot;good by default&quot; characterisation.<br /> <br /> Come to think of it, how could the original Exalted Host possibly have beaten the Primordials if they weren't &quot;good&quot; in some sense the Incarnae understand? There is zero reference to Celestials of the Primordial War era defecting to the Primordials' side. Why? Surely there was some opportunity presented to them. If free will is encoded into Exaltation, and the Incarnae wanted the Exalted to fight for their side only, then wouldn't it be an intrinsic part of the process of Exaltation that it's only awarded to people who are at least initially motivated to bring about the vision the Incarnae had for Creation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2404-chant","name":"Chant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2404_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T23:16:48-08:00","id":87278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87271#post87271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lunars, as a group, are driven to protect Creation. Some do that by fighting Wyld-spawn, some do it by striving to strengthen societies, some do it by trying to put the Solars back in charge, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Citing MoEP: Lunars fluff doesn't make for a good argument. It's effectively compromised by being the actual shitdark in this conversation. Insurgent werewolves are much more workable than the mess in between the silver and blue covers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 03-09-2014, 03:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T23:18:42-08:00","id":87280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87271#post87271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Come to think of it, how could the original Exalted Host possibly have beaten the Primordials if they weren't &quot;good&quot; in some sense the Incarnae understand? There is zero reference to Celestials of the Primordial War era defecting to the Primordials' side. Why? Surely there was some opportunity presented to them. If free will is encoded into Exaltation, and the Incarnae wanted the Exalted to fight for their side only, then wouldn't it be an intrinsic part of the process of Exaltation that it's only awarded to people who are at least initially motivated to bring about the vision the Incarnae had for Creation?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is because it wasn't a matter of good and evil, but simply a coup with the Exalted as the weapons. Also how insignificant most Primordials actually regarded mortals. Think of yourself as a Primordial, and common gnats mortals, Beneath your notice. Now suddenly the gnats have guns that really hurt, but they're still gnats. Would you bargain with a gnat?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T23:31:31-08:00","id":87286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87270#post87270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All this does is imply everyone else is not so inherently prone to &quot;goodness&quot; and so if it weren't for Solars were going to fuck everything up and still will. It takes their motives and makes them less inherently &quot;good&quot; than the Solars. Everyone else is morally inept <i>by default</i> if Solars are the good ones by default. It doesn't avoid shitdark. It makes things cartoonish.<br /> <br /> And stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really do not understand this. &quot;Good&quot; isn't a resource Solars do not get a monopoly on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon","name":"Calboon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar223_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T23:37:19-08:00","id":87288,"title":"","content":"also its impossible to be good in a world were your morals can contradict the morals of everybody else.<br /> i mean in the thread about who is prince diamond they say that there is a culture were they can kill you in the spot if you address with the wrong gender, and thats rigth, it was the fault of the dead guy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T23:43:53-08:00","id":87291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87288#post87288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">also its impossible to be good in a world were your morals can contradict the morals of everybody else.<br /> i mean in the thread about who is prince diamond they say that there is a culture were they can kill you in the spot if you address with the wrong gender, and thats rigth, it was the fault of the dead guy.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why saying Solars have some special requirement to be &quot;heroic in teh sense of good guy&quot; is incoherent. If Solars are assumed to, by default, be good guys, this creates a weird situation whereby the dint of Solar Exaltation is morally &quot;good&quot;. Or it implies that Solars have a unique claim to &quot;good guyness&quot; that other Exalts have. Which coupled with other parts of the OP's post, indicates that villainness or at least not having to &quot;live up&quot; to some lofty view of goodness unique to Solars somehow.<br /> <br /> It's not about monopolies on goodness. It's about assuming that Solars somehow have to go about being &quot;heroes as modern good guys&quot; as a normative is nonsense. As well as how such a view has never been, and I dbout canonically, ever should be, the original intent of Exalted's setting presentation, nor it going forward.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T23:46:13-08:00","id":87292,"title":"","content":"Might want to notify the playerbase of that, then. <br /> <br /> I have seen good and bad Lunars, good and bad Sidereals, good and bad DBs, predominantly good Alchemicals... I have seen a total of one Solar that wasn't in some way a jerk with an all too high opinion of himself and a &quot;my way or the highway&quot; attitude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T23:59:30-08:00","id":87297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amine Hsu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87247#post87247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No.<br /> The biggest problem is most people see themselves are 'good/heroic', so either the statement is meaningless, or you inject objective morality into the mix, which together with a statement about the goodness of Solars will just descend to farce, where the letter of the law becomes an objective measure of goodness, upheld as a ridiculous setting conceit (which is something I doubt any of the devs would put their names on).<br /> <br /> What's more, it's lazy. If all Solars are good, what was the Usurpation? If it was merely those particular Solar had fallen form grace, why the Jade Prison? Why hunt down and kill those that remain? Ultimately it's either going to end in a boring &quot;Color-Coded for Your Convenience&quot; world where some splats are purely villainous to counter-balance the purely heroic Solars<br /> <br /> Honestly though, if youwant to houserule that all second Age Solars are heroic good in your game, more power to you. But don't waltz in and say this is somehow the proper or better way to play the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's lazy is a monolithic conception of good.<br /> <br /> Your first paragraph is predicated on a false dichotomy: either the concept of good is objective, or it's meaningless. Exalted is, to a huge extent, about the fact that people see themselves as good/heroic, for good reasons, and yet come into conflict with other people who see themselves as good/heroic. The Great Curse is about how people who are invested in their own sense of good can, with the best of intentions, start working to the detriment of the world they think they're enriching. Does that make &quot;good&quot; meaningless? Way no.<br /> <br /> Your second paragraph seems to be predicated on the notion that good can't come into conflict with good. When I look at Exalted, I see a setting based heavily on the notion that good very often <i>does</i> come into conflict with good. Every Sidereal at the Great Prophecy wanted to bring about the best outcome for Creation, and yet they separated into factions, and one faction butchered the other. Lunars want to protect Creation just as much as Sidereals do, but the general mood between the two groups (insofar as they interact as groups) is hostility. Solars who are building armies to fight off the Deathlords are working for the good of Creation, and Sidereals who are trying to murder Solars to prevent a prophesised catastrophe are working for the good of Creation. Enemy Of Good Guys does not mean Evil Guy.<br /> <br /> I am running a game right now where I am requiring every player character to be &quot;good&quot; in some sense. And you know what I got out of that condition? A Twilight working for the Silver Prince, a Night ex-agent of the All-Seeing Eye, and a Zenith who wants to scourge the sea of pirates but is probably okay with tossing people into volcanoes. These three characters have many, many points of contention between them, and yet they all satisfy my condition that they be good. That's not a stage set to descend into farce, that's a stage set for a dramatic treatise on the nature of morality itself.<br /> <br /> As for your last line, okay, nobody should be calling badwrongfun. But please recognise that this thread arose because those of us in the camp that believes Solars should be treated as avatars of goodness rather than just awesomeness feel like <i>our</i> interpretation is being broadly treated as invalid or unfaithful to the setting. As evidenced by your use of the term &quot;houserule&quot;, implying that your interpretation of the setting should be considered the canonical and default one.<br /> <br /> This actually feels kind of analogous to the brony scene. There are a lot of people who want to take My Little Pony at face value and enjoy its uplifting message, and then there's a contingent of the fandom which unabashedly turns it into porn because that's what people do on the Internet. And people can enjoy whatever porn they want, but face-value-enjoyment-as-if-we-were-nine-year-old-girls bronies end up feeling like it's difficult for them to create a space where they can celebrate the show their way without seeing clop. Similarly, for a person who delights in Exalted as a setting where the omnibenevolent god of virtue gives people divine sparks to go fix the world, having the discussion spaces we associate with that setting dominated and defined by people who interpret it as having WoD-level bleakness can be demoralising.<br /> <br /> Maybe this thread should have begun with a different tone. Maybe the real underlying argument is not &quot;this is the way Exalted is supposed to be&quot; but &quot;some of us feel squelched when we try to work within the conception of Exalted that appeals to us&quot;. Maybe we all need to explicitly acknowledge this difference of opinion as one that is based in a fictional setting explicitly designed for flexibility of presentation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2404-chant","name":"Chant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2404_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T00:14:46-08:00","id":87305,"title":"","content":"Maybe, but if you frame your point that way, I think you just end up arguing about two entirely different things. You'd have one side saying &quot;some of us feel squelched when we try to work within the conception of Exalted that appeals to us&quot; and the other side would be saying, fundamentally, &quot;fine, changing that is the definition of a houserule, but still the game is not, by default, suggesting a moral stance for Solars.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/926-yishten","name":"Yishten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar926_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T00:14:50-08:00","id":87306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87280#post87280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is because it wasn't a matter of good and evil, but simply a coup with the Exalted as the weapons. Also how insignificant most Primordials actually regarded mortals. Think of yourself as a Primordial, and common gnats mortals, Beneath your notice. Now suddenly the gnats have guns that really hurt, but they're still gnats. Would you bargain with a gnat?</div> </div> </div> </div>I absolutely would, if they proved themselves an existential threat to me. I would &quot;bargain&quot; as I would try to figure out what kinds of chemicals were used to get the gnats-with-guns to focus on attacking me, and see if I could use those same chemicals to make my true aggressor their target. Obviously, gnats do not understand &quot;bargaining&quot; in the same way as I do, but they are still open to various forms of influence that are within my power.<br /> <br /> Before the Primordial War, no Exalt would have been able to get a Primordial's attention, but once they evidenced that they were threats, do you really think that no Primordial or Third Circle Demon ever thought to make a compelling offer for some of the Exalted to switch sides? In a sense, the Exalted were weapons, but they are inextricably free-willed humans, and as much as the Incarnae and Primordials might have thought of them as non-entities, the Incarnae were well aware of the concept of free will, and its implications. Otherwise they wouldn't have made Exaltations irrevocable and resistant to mental influence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2404-chant","name":"Chant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2404_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T00:25:15-08:00","id":87313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87271#post87271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lunars, as a group, are driven to protect Creation. Some do that by fighting Wyld-spawn, some do it by striving to strengthen societies, some do it by trying to put the Solars back in charge, etc.<br /> Sidereals, as a group, are driven to uphold Creation. Some think that's best done by keeping Solars from fucking it up, some think that's best done by supporting the Solars and making Creation a place of virtue and strength, and some think that's best done by addressing threats to Creation directly.<br /> <br /> Do these default group characterisations detract from the setting, or from Lunar and Sidereal gameplay? Neither of these types of Exalt is Chosen for their &quot;goodness&quot;, and yet both seem to have a predisposition toward altruistic behavior. If that doesn't detract from the experience, I don't see why it should be a problem for Solars to also take the &quot;good by default&quot; characterisation.<br /> <br /> Come to think of it, how could the original Exalted Host possibly have beaten the Primordials if they weren't &quot;good&quot; in some sense the Incarnae understand? There is zero reference to Celestials of the Primordial War era defecting to the Primordials' side. Why? Surely there was some opportunity presented to them. If free will is encoded into Exaltation, and the Incarnae wanted the Exalted to fight for their side only, then wouldn't it be an intrinsic part of the process of Exaltation that it's only awarded to people who are at least initially motivated to bring about the vision the Incarnae had for Creation?</div> </div> </div> </div>One side was full of asshole creator beings that wouldn't be out of place in a Lovecraft work, the other side gives you super powers and promises not to be such massive dicks as the last guys were. Which side do you pick?<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, there were still people who defected even then. It was noted, for example, that the original holder of Desus and Swan's exaltation attempted to betray the rebels to the Primordials.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 03-09-2014, 04:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T00:35:40-08:00","id":87316,"title":"","content":"No, no, no, no, no!<br /> Solars are, and always have been, deliberately written to deconstruct the idea of shining heroes. The Solars <i>look</i> like heroes. They shine, they're appointed by the king of the gods, etc. And many of them are good guys. And many of them are not. Look at the 1st ed Caste books. There's your guys who go round protecting the weak, your doctors, your crafters who want to improve people's lives. And then there are the dicks. Characters like Lyta and Havesh were specifically written to ram down your throat the idea that yes, many Solars are good guys, but others are huge colossal dicks, don't fall into the trap of believing Solars are the good guys, because the whole point is that looking like the good guys and having the divine right of kings does not make you the good guy. Just because you are the King does not mean you deserve to rule. (Lyta of course <i>believes</i> herself to be good, but I think we'd all agree she's not)<br /> The Solars were chosen to be ultimate weapons, to kill the titans. They were chosen to be great, to be ambitious, to not back down and go back to a life of stultified mediocrity. They were not chosen to be &quot;good&quot; by our 21st century ideal.<br /> You are a Nietschian Ubermensch, you create your own morality. You don't have to follow what is objectively good (you might well follow what is subjectively good, but I assume the premise of this thread is that most Solars are objectively good, since saying they're all subjectively good is a meaningless statement).<br /> <br /> You can play Julius Caesar, you can play Genghis Khan, you can play Lui Bei or you can play Cao Cao. That's the whole point. You play the <i>great</i> heroes of history, not the good ones (you can play the good ones if you like, you just don't have to).<br /> Why should the setting tell you that playing an evil Solar is badwrongfun? I wouldn't want it to tell you that playing a good Solar is badwrongfun either, I want you to have the choice.<br /> Why do we want to curtail people's character concepts, or for that matter NPC concepts? Why can't we have a wide variety of concepts? Good, bad, ambiguous (ambiguous are generally the most interesting to me).<br /> <br /> This isn't DnD, there is no &quot;good&quot; alignment. You can act in ways players consider good, or not. There is no metaphysical objectivity. And without a setting-enforced objective good, how can Solars be objectively good?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 03-09-2014, 04:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T00:45:37-08:00","id":87320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87268#post87268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why should Solars be special good guy Exalted? This hasn't been said and it relegates your anima to a morality, which is blatently lazy on one hand and against a lot of the game's founding thesis on the other.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's an aspect that you, and many others, are reading into our arguments. Namely, that &quot;Solars are good by default&quot; = &quot;Solars are metaphysically forced to be good&quot;. Or &quot;Solars define by their actions what is good, rendering the concept of good meaningless&quot;. Both of those are straw man positions.<br /> <br /> The Unconquered Sun didn't wage war against the Primordials purely because he wanted to play the Games of Divinity. He did it because he saw the Primordial's order of things as an unjust one. When the war was won, Yu-Shan didn't become the City of the Incarnae; it became the City of the Gods. The Essence of Ignis Divine is not &quot;I get what I want&quot;, but &quot;I subscribe to principles of virtue which empower my perfection&quot;. When Solars undergo Limit Break, and their unconquerable greatness gets out of hand, the Unconquered Sun doesn't pat them on the back and go &quot;way to express your Virtues! I'm proud of you.&quot; He turns his face in disgust. In light of everything the source material says about TUC, I have a really hard time believing that he would grant Exaltation to people who he can see are likely to use it to become tyrants to their people in the way that Primordials were tyrants to the gods.<br /> <br /> That explicitly does <i>not </i>mean Solars can never become tyrants. People change. People attain perspectives that allow them to contextualise their actions as good even when others almost uniformly see them as evil. The Solar Anima does not mean &quot;I will always be good, and my actions will define what is good&quot;. It means &quot;I was awarded irrevocable, supreme power by a being which believed I would use it for good&quot;. And I think it's that capacity for change and corruption which underscores Exalted's moral ambiguity and complexity, far more than &quot;Solars are just people who will put power to use&quot; ever could. The Old Realm <i>did</i> start as a utopia, and the Sun turned his face from his Exalted when they fell victim to that corruption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2404-chant","name":"Chant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2404_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T00:55:16-08:00","id":87325,"title":"","content":"I see Solars as a whole as being Flawed Heroes, like those portrayed in Ancient Myths. The Solars have deep Flaws, but overcoming these Flaws is what makes them Heroes. Sure, there are other heroes in the 2nd Age, Mortal and non-Solar Exalted alike<i>, </i>but the very Solar Exaltation itself seeks out People with a Great Destiny and I think many of these People have a great potential to be Heroes -- and ultimately I believe that many of them will step forward into the Light and try to be Heroes. If they can overcome their Flaws, then they will be the Heroes the 2nd Age needs. If they fail to overcome their Flaws <i>(or if a non-Heroic Person receives the Solar Exaltation...)</i>, then they may be it's Doom.<br /> <br /> I don't see Solars, or any Exalted, as being flat 2d Characters -- nor do I want them to be. I want them to be complex People with motivations and desires that help shape how they interact with and view the world, replete with Flaws that go beyond the &quot;Limit Break.&quot; I want them to be larger than life, and whether they are Heroes or Villains, I want them to always be memorable. Ultimately they should be greater than the Sum of the Dots on the Character Sheet.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> A question: If the Solars were freed of -- or had never been victims of -- the Great Curse, would the Solars fall <i>(have fallen)</i> from grace? Would the Solars abuse <i>(have abused)</i> their power, and if so, would they fall <i>(have fallen)</i> as far as if they were under the influence of the Great Curse? Ultimately, is the Great Curse needed to portray the Fall of the Solars, or are they Doomed to Fall even without it?<br /> <br /> <br /> Peace.<br /> <br /> <br /> ~ N","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is timing in everything. Timing in strategy cannot be mastered without a great deal of practice. There is also timing in the Void. You win battles with the timing in the Void born of the timing of cunning by knowing the enemies' timing, and thus using a timing which the enemy does not expect.&quot; <i>Shinmen Musashi no Kami Fujiwara no Genshin, Go Rin No Sho (The Book of the Five Rings)</i>","edited":{"userid":2141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2141-nadrakas","user":"Nadrakas","date":". 03-09-2014, 05:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2141-nadrakas","name":"Nadrakas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T00:55:58-08:00","id":87326,"title":"","content":"Exaltation happening to great people instead of good people is one of the major aspects of what makes Exalted interesting to me. I would likely avoid playing with anyone that made it so Solar or any other form of Exaltation happened primarily to people we in the modern world would consider heroes. Of course some of them will be veritable saints and budhas, but because saints and budhas are great too, not because Solars have a particular tendency for goodness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T00:59:10-08:00","id":87327,"title":"","content":"I don't regard an non-heroic PC as inherently worse than a heroic one. I don't think non-heroic PCs and NPCs contradict 'Solars are heroes' as a default statement. I simply regard them as exceptions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yishten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87305#post87305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe, but if you frame your point that way, I think you just end up arguing about two entirely different things. You'd have one side saying &quot;some of us feel squelched when we try to work within the conception of Exalted that appeals to us&quot; and the other side would be saying, fundamentally, &quot;fine, changing that is the definition of a houserule, but still the game is not, by default, suggesting a moral stance for Solars.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Houserule is a bizarre word to use when discussing interpretations of creative works.<br /> <br /> &quot;Fight Club is a movie that criticizes the violence and emotional alienation of modern masculinity.&quot;<br /> &quot;That might have been the intent, but it ultimately glorifies those very things.&quot;<br /> &quot;That's just your houserule of the film.&quot;<br /> <br /> And Exalted isn't passive media. We create it whenever we sit down and game.<br /> <br /> Unless you specifically mean Chant saying that PCs all have to be good in some way. That is a houserule and he seems to label it as such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 03-09-2014, 05:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T01:02:47-08:00","id":87333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87316#post87316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Lyta of course <i>believes</i> herself to be good, but I think we'd all agree she's not)<br /> The Solars were chosen to be ultimate weapons, to kill the titans. They were chosen to be great, to be ambitious, to not back down and go back to a life of stultified mediocrity. They were not chosen to be &quot;good&quot; by our 21st century ideal.<br /> You are a Nietschian Ubermensch, you create your own morality. You don't have to follow what is objectively good (you might well follow what is subjectively good, but I assume the premise of this thread is that most Solars are objectively good, since saying they're all subjectively good is a meaningless statement).</div> </div> </div> </div>Can I bat your &quot;No, no, no, no, no!&quot; right back at you?<br /> <br /> &quot;Subjectively good&quot; isn't meaningless! It's the entire premise of Exalted's many factions, where you have Bronze Faction good guys, Gold Faction good guys, Silver Pact good guys, etc. etc. Good comes into conflict with good, precisely <i>because</i> good is not something you can objectively measure and define!<br /> <br /> Here is my thesis statement: Every person who receives Solar Exaltation is a person who believes that they are working to create the right order in the world. Every person who receives Solar Exaltation believes that they are good and working to effect good. The Unconquered Sun is a being who cannot reconcile one good against another, believing in every good with his whole heart. Therefore, all those he Exalts are good, and yet there is no single governing principle of good which defines his Chosen.<br /> <br /> Corollary: A Solar does not accumulate power and influence simply in order to gratify themselves. Instead, a Solar wields power to bring about the order they see as best.<br /> <br /> That ideal order that every Solar wishes to bring about for Creation, that individual conception of good, is where the term &quot;Lawgiver&quot; comes from. Not from their position as ordained by the Creation-Ruling Mandate, but because that is the essence of what it is to be Solar: to believe in what is right, and cause the world to conform to that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2404-chant","name":"Chant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2404_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T01:05:53-08:00","id":87335,"title":"","content":"Firstly, you're equating the 4 virtues with goodness. A heap of Deathlords have Conviction 5. Conviction includes stuff like torturing people because you feel you have to. Similar arguments could be made about Valor and maybe Temperance (though not so much as Valor or Conviction).<br /> The Unconquered Sun is the <i>king</i> of the Gods. Ie he's a dictator. They don't get votes or anything. He's supposed to be more like Zeus or Odin (or, and this may be a contraversial statement, the God of the Old Testament) than Jesus. He's the God who sends plagues to slay his enemies. He's the guy who started a war against his own parents, and butchered their supporters. He partly did this, yes, because he felt they were evil, but he's not a simply good figure.<br /> People generally assume he's good, because, you know, he's the King of the Gods. But some question that. Like the way most Greeks went &quot;yeah, of course Zeus is a good guy, he's King of the Gods, he decides what's good&quot; but then Socrates went &quot;no, that's stupid, you shouldn't worship Zeus... oh wait I seem to have been forced to drink poison&quot;.<br /> If you want to play a Getimian waging war against an unjust Heaven, you can, because the UCS isn't inherently perfect.<br /> <br /> Secondly, Grabowski deliberately made the fact that Solars are not inherently good a core part of the game. That's more fundamental to the game than the way Solars are made. If the writers then wrote a system for where Solars come from that might imply they're good guys, this was bad writing. The very point of the game is that when you play a Solar, you can play the great hero (in the classical sense of the word) that you want. Not be told &quot;you're playing a good guy&quot;. Or for that matter, &quot;you're playing a bad guy&quot;. Your actions in the game will determine if you're good or bad.<br /> And honestly, it doesn't matter. Because it's a game, no-one's coming to judge your morality from what you played in the game. All that matters is what the characters in the game think is good, ie subjective good.<br /> I know it's fallen out of favour with the devs for being too mechanistic, but the reason in 2nd ed exaltation didn't involve you being specifically chosen by the Gods was to make sure no-one said &quot;well surely the UCS would only choose good people&quot;.<br /> In 1st ed, that didn't occur to them, they just wove Lyta, Havesh, etc at you to make sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 03-09-2014, 05:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T01:19:35-08:00","id":87348,"title":"","content":"To me, one of the most important elements of the setting is that your heroism (modern meaning) does not come from anything you can write on your character sheet. That includes what type of Exalted you are. There are no alignements, tied to splats or otherwise. Morality exists in YOUR OWN DECISIONS and YOUR OWN ACTIONS, and no where else. Some Solars are wandering selfless mendicants, some are righteous avengers, some are visionary conquerers - with all the brutality that entails. It's the individual's choices that matters, not their splat.<br /> <br /> If your view of Solars precludes a Solar conquerer, or Solar mad scientist, or Solar assassin (all of whom view themselves as righteous and making the world a better place) being a villainous antagonist for a Solar campaign - you are doing it wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 03-09-2014, 05:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T01:25:36-08:00","id":87351,"title":"","content":"Another point I'd like to make: much more than any other type of Exalted, Solars are a blank slate. If you play a Lunar, you're playing a shapeshifter. If you're playing an Abyssal, you've got this whole death-orientated scheme going on. The thematics are tighter.<br /> For Solars, you can pick pretty much any human fantasy concept. You can be a soldier, a priest, a smith, a farmboy, an aged martial artist, a genius doctor, a knight, a samurai, a courtesan, a diplomat, etc, etc, etc, etc, etc. That's their virtue over say, Lunars, or Sidereals.<br /> There's not much baggage.<br /> So while I dislike saying &quot;Solars are the good guys&quot; for its own sake, as already mentioned, it would be a huge change to the setting (and one I feel would be very bad for the game) I also dislike it because I don't want to get too much extra baggage attached to Solars anyway, because it reduces the amount of concepts you can play.<br /> If my concept is &quot;world's greatest assassin&quot; (a very suitable Night caste concept I feel), that's kind of hard when I'm supposed to start as a good guy. I don't want to have to find some excuse to explain why my guy who kills people for money is actually a good guy, I want to keep the concept pure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T01:29:07-08:00","id":87352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Calboon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87286#post87286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really do not understand this. &quot;Good&quot; isn't a resource Solars do not get a monopoly on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good is a qualifier though, if Solars are all mostly good, what does that say about the moral quality of exalt types that AREN'T all mostly good?<br /> <br /> (( and if everyone is all mostly good... ))","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/726-amine-hsu","name":"Amine Hsu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar726_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T01:41:47-08:00","id":87361,"title":"","content":"It seems like everyone who is arguing against me is trying to trap me in concepts of &quot;good&quot; that they themselves are bringing to the table. At no point have I expressed that I think every Solar is &quot;good&quot; in the sense that we might call an altruistic, even-tempered, upstanding citizen in a Western democratic republic &quot;good&quot;, and I now explicitly disclaim that belief.<br /> <br /> When I say every Solar is &quot;good&quot; at the moment of Exaltation, what I mean is that every person who receives Solar Exaltation is a person who believes in some state of affairs as ideal beyond their own involvement in it, and who endeavors to bring that state of affairs about. Freedom. Democracy. Literacy. Longevity. Piety. Justice. Any number of things, many of which may come into conflict with each other. A Solar is never just a person who is really good at what they do, nor a person who has great personal ambitions. A Solar is a person who endeavors to create the world they think is best.<br /> <br /> If Solar Exaltation were simply about the potential to be <i>personally</i> great, simply about having an impact on the world, regardless of why, then you wouldn't have Yurgen Kaneko wandering out into the frozen wastes to die and coming back Exalted instead, nor Panther getting Exalted for noticing he's living a live of debauchery. You wouldn't have every Zenith getting told to spread righteousness in their own idiomatic way.<br /> <br /> I love Exalted for not nailing down what individual behaviors and perspectives and methods constitute &quot;good&quot;, nor requiring a Storyteller or Player to do so. I think that's precisely why the Solars can all be &quot;good&quot; and also all be different and interesting and at odds with each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2404-chant","name":"Chant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2404_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T01:43:33-08:00","id":87365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87348#post87348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your view of Solars precludes a Solar conquerer, or Solar mad scientist, or Solar assassin (all of whom view themselves as righteous and making the world a better place) being a villainous antagonist for a Solar campaign - you are doing it wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;<b>(all of whom view themselves as righteous and making the world a better place)</b>&quot;<br /> <br /> You and I are on the same page.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2404-chant","name":"Chant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2404_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T01:46:14-08:00","id":87371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87327#post87327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think non-heroic PCs and NPCs contradict 'Solars are heroes' as a default statement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course they do. Not on an individual 'look, I caught you out' sort of basis, but each Solar that doesn't conform to the modern sense of heroism reduces the degree to which your 'default' is an accurate description of the Solars. If there are enough of them, and there are a healthy crowd, even in the first edition material from before X2 took it's weird tonal dive, then your statement stops being an accurate statement about the Solars as a whole, and the idea of it as a default of any sort becomes ridiculous.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't regard an non-heroic PC as inherently worse than a heroic one. </div> </div> </div>Then why bother with a default? Why not stick with everything that's been written in and about the game, all of which supports the idea that there is no default moral or ethical directive, gravity, inclination or default applied to the Solars, or any other Exalted. Clearly this is your preferred interpretation, but just as clearly from the responses in this threat that's far from universally shared. Everyone interprets the moral standing of the Exalted slightly differently and thus far none of the published material, which is really the only way to judge what the 'defaults' of the game are, has steered clear of publishing anything that says otherwise.<br /> <br /> Given that the material the new writing team has pointed us to as a guide for where they're going with the tone of the new edition prominently includes both heroic and non-heroic (in the modern sense) Solars, I doubt that your statement on heroism will be well supported in the materials. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T01:48:28-08:00","id":87373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87351#post87351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another point I'd like to make: much more than any other type of Exalted, Solars are a blank slate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you sure?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Plague of Hats</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's never really been true in the way lots of people complain about that Solars don't &quot;have a theme.&quot; I think when people try to sell them as &quot;the blank-slate Exalted&quot;, it really just damages fan perceptions of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2404-chant","name":"Chant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2404_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T01:52:54-08:00","id":87379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuddenThunder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87371#post87371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Of course they do. Not on an individual 'look, I caught you out' sort of basis, but each Solar that doesn't conform to the modern sense of heroism reduces the degree to which your 'default' is an accurate description of the Solars. If there are enough of them, and there are a healthy crowd, even in the first edition material from before X2 took it's weird tonal dive, then your statement stops being an accurate statement about the Solars as a whole, and the idea of it as a default of any sort becomes ridiculous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you believe that the scenario in your statement is the case and we've reached a critical mass of non-heroic Solars, such that my statement is ridiculous?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then why bother with a default? </div> </div> </div>The same reason the default Lunar is 'a monster with a human inside or a human with a monster inside.' It informs the themes and mood of the setting and the splat.<br /> <br /> 'Humans are selfish' is another default statement, which probably tell you something about how I perceive humanity as a whole. It doesn't preclude selfless acts or people, nor does it suppose selfish humans are better humans than non-selfish ones.<br /> <br /> The idea that default statements exist as a metric to see how well your PC measures up to them reduces players to children hoping to get gold stars on their homework.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 03-09-2014, 05:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T03:18:19-07:00","id":87392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>chant</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems like everyone who is arguing against me is trying to trap me in concepts of &quot;good&quot; that they themselves are bringing to the table. At no point have I expressed that I think every Solar is &quot;good&quot; in the sense that we might call an altruistic, even-tempered, upstanding citizen in a Western democratic republic &quot;good&quot;, and I now explicitly disclaim that belief.<br /> <br /> When I say every Solar is &quot;good&quot; at the moment of Exaltation, what I mean is that every person who receives Solar Exaltation is a person who believes in some state of affairs as ideal beyond their own involvement in it, and who endeavors to bring that state of affairs about. Freedom. Democracy. Literacy. Longevity. Piety. Justice. Any number of things, many of which may come into conflict with each other. A Solar is never just a person who is really good at what they do, nor a person who has great personal ambitions. A Solar is a person who endeavors to create the world they think is best.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I wasn't really arguing with you, but rather the whole side who are supporting &quot;Solars are good guys&quot;. I object a lot less to your idea because it's more nuanced, and doesn't include forcing characters to a default of objectively good.<br /> I would say, however, that while I'm happy for a large portion of Solars to be good from a certain point of view, which seems to be your point, and I agree these are generally the most interesting characters, I still don't think I want it as a <i>default</i> for Solar.<br /> If my character concept is greatest assassin or greatest conqueror, your idea still means I have to play &quot;greatest assassin who wants to make the world better by his own standards&quot; and I don't see the point of the game telling me to do that.<br /> I still can't play Alexander the Great, whose primary goal is to shake the world and write his name in history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 03-09-2014, 06:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T03:25:32-07:00","id":87394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>chant</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you sure?</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say they were entirely a blank slate, just that they were more than anyone else. They have themes like leadership, great skill, being mythic heroes. Light, the sun, royalty. But those themes are a lot less restrictive than being a tattooed shapeshifter, or a secret master fate ninja.<br /> Perhaps that seems like a weak-ass refutation of your point. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But anyway, I think they always were more of a blank slate than anyone else. If Plague disagrees, well he wasn't a Dev then.<br /> Of course, he is now, so maybe they'll be less of a blank slate in the new book (I hope not, but there it is).<br /> I'll still argue that a moral default is definitely not a theme they should have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T03:29:15-07:00","id":87395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hippokrene</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you believe that the scenario in your statement is the case and we've reached a critical mass of non-heroic Solars, such that my statement is ridiculous?</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, Hippokrene, what sort of percentage of Solars do you think should be good? Do you mean 99% of them should be good, or 80%, or 60%?<br /> I suspect some of the arguments here are because we don't all know exactly what the other people mean. If we can define precisely what we're talking about, that might help us understand each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 03-09-2014, 06:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T03:35:27-07:00","id":87396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87379#post87379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you believe that the scenario in your statement is the case and we've reached a critical mass of non-heroic Solars, such that my statement is ridiculous?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I've only done a swift survey, not a thorough accounting, but running through the caste books it looks like you've got about 25%-35% of the Solars featured that I'd say don't qualify as heroic in the modern sense. So, no, ridiculous would probably be a bit strong. I wouldn't say it's a particularly strong or accurate description of the Solars as a group though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87379#post87379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The same reason the default Lunar is 'a monster with a human inside or a human with a monster inside.' It informs the themes and mood of the setting and the splat.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does rather help that that's a statement that's been made by the people who will be writing the game, so we can expect that it will be probably be reflected in the published material. The heroism statement, on the other hand, goes directly against the stated assumptions and published support for two editions here, and without any indication that the new edition will be changing that. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87379#post87379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea that default statements exist as a metric to see how well your PC measures up to them reduces players to children hoping to get gold stars on their homework.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, default statements exist to inform players what the norms and assumptions are in the setting. If you make heroic solars the default you tell players that they should expect the strong majority of Solars they make and encounter will be heroes. You likewise tell people that Solars who aren't heroes are unusual, rare, and going against the nature of their character type. You change player behaviour, and steer it in particular directions. The current default of the setting is that Solars aren't a group of people you can make broad moral or motivational generalisations about. I really haven't seen any reason given to change that or support for the idea that it's true. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T03:49:39-07:00","id":87401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars are myth-heroes. It is a myth-hero's purpose to subvert mythos and thereby define it. Solars fight, destroy, and ultimately recreate the status-quo, doing so by conquering the obliquely magical through acts of sheer will, force, and skill writ-large, like every myth-hero in literature.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think, from this quote, we can infer that the intent for Solars is not that they have any default moral characteristic, as much as I want that to be the case. Instead, John intends to draw on heroes like Odysseus and Beowulf whose moral character is not central or even relevant to their stories.<br /> <br /> I like Exalted better my way, but the weight of the evidence has crushed me. I concede Solars-as-intended don't have to be &quot;good&quot;, even in the permissive definition of &quot;good&quot; I've given in this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2404-chant","name":"Chant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2404_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T04:19:56-07:00","id":87409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87361#post87361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I say every Solar is &quot;good&quot; at the moment of Exaltation, what I mean is that every person who receives Solar Exaltation is a person who believes in some state of affairs as ideal beyond their own involvement in it, and who endeavors to bring that state of affairs about. Freedom. Democracy. Literacy. Longevity. Piety. Justice.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about Control, Vengeance, Tyranny, Conquest, Anarchy, Dogma or Bloodlust? Because really I see those as equally Exalt-able ideals. And throughout history they've been considered &quot;good&quot; by various peoples. Note that I actually am curious about your opinion on this, I'm not trying to snipe or anything.<br /> <br /> On an unrelated note, when has it been mentioned that all Solars in third edition are going to be handpicked by the Unconquered Sun? I could swear the Devs mentioned that they were planning on making the criteria for Exaltation more mysterious, not less.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T04:22:04-07:00","id":87410,"title":"","content":"One interesting thing about Odysseus, is that while he's a mythic hero and what-not, you actually couldn't really play him in 2nd ed. He doesn't have a heroic motivation. He really just wants to get home and live in peace in his minor, fairly poor kingdom. Events force him to be a hero. Which is a common trope for heroes. Consider also the aged but skilled guy who doesn't want to come out of retirement but has to be convinced (ie 7 Samurai).<br /> Now third ed won't have the requirement of an epic motivation, as it won't have motivations at all, which makes me wonder what the requirements for Solar (or any) Exaltation will be. Perhaps it'll just be potential for greatness. Which would be fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T05:12:26-07:00","id":87432,"title":"","content":"To a large extent, Good is a &quot;Point of View.&quot; So is &quot;Evil.&quot; If you are on one side, then you are doing &quot;Good;&quot; if you are on the receiving end then the other side is &quot;Evil.&quot; Yes...this is a &quot;Simplistic&quot; explanation, but that is how things have been broken down throughout History; even today.<br /> <br /> As has been mentioned, many things that we view as &quot;Evil&quot; today were, at one time-or-another, viewed as being &quot;Good.&quot;<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">- Forcing people to Convert to a Particular Religion in order to Save their Souls. If they didn't, then execute them as Heretics. Not too long ago that was considered &quot;Good.&quot; Nowadays, we see that as &quot;Evil&quot; and call it Terrorism.<br /> <br /> - Sacrificing People, pulling out and burning their Hearts: The Aztecs saw this as &quot;Good&quot; because they were keeping the world Alive. The Europeans saw it as &quot;Evil&quot; and did everything they could to put a stop to it. Of course, the fact that the Aztecs had lots of Gold had nothing to do with it.</div> <br /> In the 2nd Age, a Solar may oppose the above because they see them as &quot;Evil.&quot; Or, they may go forth and Vanquish their enemies in the name of the Unconquered Sun, putting to the sword or sacrificing any who fail to venerate Ignis Divine. Meanwhile, other Solars may oppose this desecration of the worship to the Unconquered Sun, defending the Mortals and rallying them against this Heresy. Both sides would see themselves as &quot;Good&quot; and the other as &quot;Evil.&quot;<br /> <br /> Being a Hero does not mean that others see you as &quot;Good,&quot; even if you see yourself as &quot;Good.&quot;<br /> <br /> Peace.<br /> <br /> <br /> ~ N","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is timing in everything. Timing in strategy cannot be mastered without a great deal of practice. There is also timing in the Void. You win battles with the timing in the Void born of the timing of cunning by knowing the enemies' timing, and thus using a timing which the enemy does not expect.&quot; <i>Shinmen Musashi no Kami Fujiwara no Genshin, Go Rin No Sho (The Book of the Five Rings)</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2141-nadrakas","name":"Nadrakas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T05:19:10-07:00","id":87434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kunoichi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87409#post87409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On an unrelated note, when has it been mentioned that all Solars in third edition are going to be handpicked by the Unconquered Sun? I could swear the Devs mentioned that they were planning on making the criteria for Exaltation more mysterious, not less.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the Devs (I forget which one) said, in refutation to someone talking about the automatic nature of Exaltation, that it was going back to you being chosen by the Gods. Nothing on what criteria they choose though.<br /> Maybe it's mysterious as to how they choose their candidates.<br /> That does run into the problems the automatic nature was written to avoid though, namely what happens if you kill an Incarnae, who chooses the new ones? Or if the Yozis forced the Gods to choose stupid people as Exalts? Or whatever.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T05:28:13-07:00","id":87436,"title":"","content":"The fall of the First Age is definitely supposed to be a tragedy, but as one gets more hints and flashes of it one might start to suspect that it's more a tragedy in the detached literary sense than in the human toll sense.<br /> <br /> The First Age could be a time in which grand armies, vast beyond measure, equipped with the arsenals of heaven and led by the greatest of heroes clashed against one another in warfare where people could win amazing glories. That's lost now, but it was primarily a thing that people could live and tell amazing stories about; it wasn't necessarily to the good of people.<br /> <br /> I'd say that's what Holden means when he makes a point about how Creation has never had lasting prosperity or central unification, or what John means when he says that there are social problems that have plagued humanity throughout the Ages of their dominance.<br /> <br /> It is of course going too far to say that the First Age became a time of wall to wall atrocity and mind control, but it hurts the thesis of the game to say that, prior to the blooming of the Great Curse, it was a time in which the issues of the human condition were solved.<br /> <br /> To the extent that people had peace, I'd say it should be the peace of Rome, of Britain, of the Mongols; the people in the interior live without fear, but there can still be a lot of violence at the edges. There are societies that view themselves as peaceful because they don't perceive a threat of war that could actually destroy their civilisation, or that impacts upon their everyday life; historically, many such societies have felt very comfortable with bringing war to other people.<br /> <br /> So the Old Realm is liable to have had that.<br /> <br /> This should be primarily subtextual.<br /> <br /> That said, I think that Solars should lack the essential motifs that would be widely seen as marks of villainy (like the usual interpretation of their compelling presence as insidious mind control); that's not to say that Solars are always or even necessarily often &quot;good&quot; people, but at least not necessarily people who would readily come across as... I don't know, something a bit mustache twirling.<br /> <br /> It should generally be plausible that <i>somebody</i> would look on a Solar as a venerable hero, even if it's largely because the Solar is impressive (or, if everybody is looking at them with dread, at least with a mind to that everyone coming from a questionable hierarchy).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T05:36:37-07:00","id":87438,"title":"","content":"I like to think of the Solar exalted primarily as Chosen by the Sun. TUC is a god, a personification of different concepts attributed to him. Concepts like perfection, greatness, heroism, goodness or light-conquers-dark. TUC isn't human, and I also like to think that he has a very poor understanding of humans, considering his domains. Where humans are nuanced he is the extreme in every case, and his nature forces him not to accept anything that is less than the extreme.<br /> <br /> When TUC chooses his champions, or when he sets the principles for Solar exaltation, he looks for people who <i>he likes</i>. I.e. humans who somehow embodies the same concepts that he does, that strive for perfection, acts heroic or does good, in the same way that he understands these concepts.<br /> <br /> This means that at first most Solars will seem like heroes and champions of all that is good and holy. But just as concepts like perfection and good vs. evil breaks apart in a complex context without a objective scale of measure, so will the Solars stray from what is expected of them. In the early days of the First Age the Solars still had guidance, the Sun still tried to influence their morals and actions. But as TUC can't stand things that conflicts with his concepts, and because of a growing addiction to the Games of Divinity, he turned away and suddenly the Solars had no one who told them what to do. They had no boundaries. And as the Solars grew thousands of years old and gained power beyond the gods, they lost touch with reality and the rest of creations inhabitants. The way the elder Solars acted then became the norm for younger Solars, and that is what I like to think caused the Solars collective madness and decent in the First age, not primarily the Great Curse.<br /> <br /> The Solars of the second age are still chosen by the same standards as those in the first age, they are somehow great and/or good and all in the moment of exaltation. But then they change, as all humans do (which is a strange concept to TUC) and they may become something entirely opposed to what TUC had in mind.<br /> <br /> So, to tie this to the topic, in my head the Solars can be exalted because the are good in a way TUC recognizes. But they could also be exalted just because they strive for perfection, greatness or a heroic legacy. Goodness (the way TUC understands and defines it) is not a requirement for exaltation, but it is one of the things looked at.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2355-ratatosk","name":"Ratatosk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2355_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T07:09:07-07:00","id":87459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87327#post87327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't regard an non-heroic PC as inherently worse than a heroic one. I don't think non-heroic PCs and NPCs contradict 'Solars are heroes' as a default statement. I simply regard them as exceptions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Houserule is a bizarre word to use when discussing interpretations of creative works.<br /> <br /> &quot;Fight Club is a movie that criticizes the violence and emotional alienation of modern masculinity.&quot;<br /> &quot;That might have been the intent, but it ultimately glorifies those very things.&quot;<br /> &quot;That's just your houserule of the film.&quot;<br /> <br /> And Exalted isn't passive media. We create it whenever we sit down and game.<br /> <br /> Unless you specifically mean Chant saying that PCs all have to be good in some way. That is a houserule and he seems to label it as such.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm really just using Chant's own terminology from his or her prior post. The passivity or lack thereof of the media isn't really relevant, though. I don't see the pro-Hero group framing their argument that, when they play, ultimately their Solars end up being portrayed as heroes; I see them framing the argument that Solars default to being heroes. This suggests to me that we're talking about the status of the game, as presented, prior to anyone picking up the dice.<br /> <br /> And from that perspective, though I personally have little commitment to any interpretation, it seems to me that those who argue against interpreting Solars are, as I believe Chant put, working to make the world a better place by default, have a stronger argument, between the explicit deconstruction of the shining hero concept inherent to Solars, that I don't think I've seen much to cause me to interpret the gods rebelling out of any sense of justice (unless it was the notion that it was unjust that they have to manage Creation while the Primordials do not), and that Solars are just people (and people don't default to heroism). Though, emotionally, I am certainly sympathetic to the pro-hero argument.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/926-yishten","name":"Yishten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar926_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T07:46:04-07:00","id":87478,"title":"","content":"Chant, the definition of 'good' you are using in this thread is completely indistinguishable from heroic in the greek sense. When being 'good' simply means doing what you believe is right, then even Hitler is a hero and the closest you get to evil is a couch potato.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T07:53:43-07:00","id":87480,"title":"","content":"Yes, the solars are heroes, but not in the modern sense, rather, they are the heroes in the way the Ancient Greeks used them.<br /> To the greeks, a hero was someone who was strong, powerful or influential, and who was willing to use his power.<br /> <br /> The best example of this is probably Achilles. Really goodlooking and an absolute monster on the battlefield, men want to be him and women want to be with him, son of a nymph, almost completely invincible, all-in-all. But at the same time, he was also a gloryhound, loved combat for it's own sake (not something you can say about most modern heroes), and the whole &quot;Dragging Hector behind his chariot just to humiliate him&quot; business is also a very douchebaggy thing to do.<br /> <br /> But yeah, most Greek heroes are assholes to a greater or lesser extend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T07:57:12-07:00","id":87482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the definition of 'good' you are using in this thread is completely indistinguishable from heroic in the greek sense. </div> </div> </div>At the risk of stepping on another poster's toes, not exactly. As he pointed out, Odysseys doesn't fit his idea. Hitler does because he was trying to change the world for (what he thought was) the better* but Odysseus doesn't. Odysseus wasn't trying to change the world for the better, he just wanted to get home. He was faced with great adversity and found the strength, wits and leadership to overcome it, thus becoming a hero. But he wasn't trying to make the world a better place really, for anyone but him and his family.<br /> Same with Beowulf really.<br /> <br /> *This is kind of a simplification of Hitler's desires, but that's not really important right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T08:04:05-07:00","id":87485,"title":"","content":"So this is just a rehash of the &quot;Solars are people with grand motivations&quot; thread from before?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/926-yishten","name":"Yishten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar926_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T08:06:42-07:00","id":87488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yishten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87485#post87485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So this is just a rehash of the &quot;Solars are people with grand motivations&quot; thread from before?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, we know the grand motivation thing is being scrapped in Ex3, as far as I know because it's super-restrictive on character concepts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T08:13:26-07:00","id":87491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87365#post87365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;<b>(all of whom view themselves as righteous and making the world a better place)</b>&quot;<br /> <br /> You and I are on the same page.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, we're now at the point where Solar Hitler qualifies for your definition of good. I think this discussion has become completely meaningless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/726-amine-hsu","name":"Amine Hsu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar726_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T08:16:10-07:00","id":87494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87488#post87488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, we know the grand motivation thing is being scrapped in Ex3, as far as I know because it's super-restrictive on character concepts.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a mechanic, it's being taken out. As a concept, you will still be able to use it, but it won't be a forced thing anymore.<br /> To celebrate this, my first 3e character shall be a Swordsman whose school get destroyed and he has the simple motivation of &quot;Killing the man who destroyed his school in an honorable, one-on-one duel.&quot;<br /> <br /> Basically Inigo Montoya with a katana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T08:18:57-07:00","id":87496,"title":"","content":"Odysseus was a hero during the war against Troy, even if a reluctant one. Its after the torjan war, during the odyssey, that he is trying to get home.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2245-quimeradc","name":"Quimeradc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T08:37:46-07:00","id":87502,"title":"","content":"The exaltation has to be autonomous; this goes back to the side-stepping things like the Primordials commanding the gods to stop exalting people. <br /> <br /> I think the most important thing is that the Solar is someone willing, able, and capable of using the power he is given at the time of exaltation. The exaltation itself has very little in the way of a deep psychological understanding of the individual it empowers. It's a pre-programmed drone seeking out some specific surface traits. A Night Caste exaltation (of which we assume there were 60 at its peak) has to choose an individual out of the hundreds of millions (or more) people in Creation in the span of a single moment; at some point, you're going to get Havesh the Vanisher instead of Batman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/994-heroicantagonist","name":"heroicantagonist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar994_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T08:39:03-07:00","id":87503,"title":"","content":"I think that there's more to Solar heroism than just being larger-than-life, but that it's also important to understand that it's primarily a thematic for them rather than a moral statement.<br /> <br /> Basically, as a Solar, you get to be an Exalt by believing in the hero within you and summoning him or her forth by an act of will. Alternately, you could merge your soul with a demon and hope for the best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 03-09-2014, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T08:52:19-07:00","id":87510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yishten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87485#post87485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So this is just a rehash of the &quot;Solars are people with grand motivations&quot; thread from before?</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> *******","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T08:54:10-07:00","id":87511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heroicantagonist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87502#post87502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The exaltation has to be autonomous; this goes back to the side-stepping things like the Primordials commanding the gods to stop exalting people.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's so unnecessary to get into such excessive intricacy in how a distant background element played out.<br /> <br /> It's just another form of punchy statement that doesn't actually hold up to scrutiny anyway: &quot;oh, the Exaltation had to be autonomous because otherwise the Primordials could just order gods to stop doing it, and then when they realised that wouldn't work they didn't just order the gods to start killing the Exalted because BRRRRRRRMMMMMMM&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heroicantagonist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the most important thing is that the Solar is someone willing, able, and capable of using the power he is given at the time of exaltation. The exaltation itself has very little in the way of a deep psychological understanding of the individual it empowers. It's a pre-programmed drone seeking out some specific surface traits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah let's totally strip out anything wondrous or miraculous out of this central focus of setting mythology; that's tone immersive.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T09:08:16-07:00","id":87514,"title":"","content":"I'm inclined to think of Solars as defaulting to &quot;hero&quot; too, though in the sense that they are inherently &quot;righteous&quot; rather than either &quot;great&quot; (oft-cited as the classical sense of the word) or &quot;good&quot; (the more modern sense), though in practice I think it hews pretty close to what the OP meant by the latter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T09:15:42-07:00","id":87521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87320#post87320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there's an aspect that you, and many others, are reading into our arguments. Namely, that &quot;Solars are good by default&quot; = &quot;Solars are metaphysically forced to be good&quot;. Or &quot;Solars define by their actions what is good, rendering the concept of good meaningless&quot;. Both of those are straw man positions.</div> </div> </div> </div>My position is that 'If Solars are the good guy Exalted&quot; as described, and emphasized as such, the other Exalted become not the good guys. Which has a consequence of giving Solars more inherent moral weight. By defining a splat by something that is often given moral qualities, you give that splat moral weight. Which is what avoiding defining any Exalt sort as good is mean to prevent.<br /> <br /> Baron Acton (the guy who coined the &quot;power corrupts&quot; motto as we know it) has another quote I quite like:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The danger is not that a particular class is unfit to govern. Every class is unfit to govern. </div> </div> </div>Solar Exalted get no more moral &quot;weight&quot; than anyone else. They're no more &quot;good&quot; than anyone else. They are good and heroic as any great human can be good and heroic. But again, greatness =/= greatness. Trying to say it is and say &quot;Solars are good heroes&quot; is wanting your Exaltation to have moral weight and your try to influence the world as a Solar an act of moral good in itself. Which is what the game's initial thesis is outright against.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87320#post87320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Unconquered Sun didn't wage war against the Primordials purely because he wanted to play the Games of Divinity. He did it because he saw the Primordial's order of things as an unjust one. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>As the god who decides what's just and not based on his personal beliefs (which are apparently incompatable with Primordial ones), how is this good, per se? Humans and gods got a lot out of it. That's good for them. But remember that the UCS's actions are not inherently good or right. What he did was still a coup. &quot;I can do it better&quot; is what many such people have done for centuries.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87320#post87320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... When the war was won, Yu-Shan didn't become the City of the Incarnae; it became the City of the Gods. The Essence of Ignis Divine is not &quot;I get what I want&quot;, but &quot;I subscribe to principles of virtue which empower my perfection&quot;. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems fairly based on the <i>Glories</i> interpretation of the Sun. Which you note, is meant to also lead the Sun into acts of stupidity, blatent contrarian action due to the nature of his Virtues themselves not being compatable and so on. Virtueous in Exalted is also not good. Virtueous is just Virtueous. And in the Unconqured Sun's case in <i>Glories</i> (which we know is not necessarily his case in 3e) is not able to be all things at once. He has to pick and choose and live with what he chose.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87320#post87320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... When Solars undergo Limit Break, and their unconquerable greatness gets out of hand, the Unconquered Sun doesn't pat them on the back and go &quot;way to express your Virtues! I'm proud of you.&quot; ...</div> </div> </div> </div>This assumes that the Great Curse is all that had Solars fall. It seems to me it's more folks who don't even have in the mechanized 2e the Curse to be bad in the ways he turned his face do that. The Hierophant said things in the Sun's name to get what he wanted. He had Heart of Tears. His actions were his own: greed, the purported Voice of God and a want to use the latter to push for the former. This is human nature. The Sun turned his back due to that. Saying Solars are good save for the Great Curse if anything shows how shittily the Great Curse has been implemented, as it take sthe mroal weight of one's predecessors off of them and onto the Curse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87320#post87320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... He turns his face in disgust. In light of everything the source material says about TUC, I have a really hard time believing that he would grant Exaltation to people who he can see are likely to use it to become tyrants to their people in the way that Primordials were tyrants to the gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tyrany is not what he gives a shit about. Greatness is. And what &quot;in light of everything&quot;? He Exalted Lyta, Havesh the Vanisher, Fehim, Nimiun Snow Eyes, and Mirror Flag. He Exalted people who would become Larquen Quen or the Hierophant. The Sun is either one who doesn't hold standards as we see them, or is capable of fucking up and misjudging people enough that he gives people you might not like Exaltations. That's the way of the world. People who get power might not be people you want to have it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87320#post87320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That explicitly does <i>not </i>mean Solars can never become tyrants. People change. People attain perspectives that allow them to contextualise their actions as good even when others almost uniformly see them as evil. The Solar Anima does not mean &quot;I will always be good, and my actions will define what is good&quot;. It means &quot;I was awarded irrevocable, supreme power by a being which believed I would use it for good&quot;. And I think it's that capacity for change and corruption which underscores Exalted's moral ambiguity and complexity, far more than &quot;Solars are just people who will put power to use&quot; ever could. The Old Realm <i>did</i> start as a utopia, and the Sun turned his face from his Exalted when they fell victim to that corruption.</div> </div> </div> </div>And again, the Sun might of just fucked-up and thought better of you than you actually were. The big change that made you an asswhole may well of been the very Exaltation that let you suddenly go and be a prick instead of what good your situation had potential to let you do.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T09:18:39-07:00","id":87523,"title":"","content":"Addendum: the overarching Drama of the Solars is, at least in significant part, &quot;how do we get 150 demigods chosen for the righteousness in their hearts to see the big picture and work together&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T09:19:58-07:00","id":87525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87510#post87510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> No. *******</div> </div> </div> </div> I'd not have assumed. But if Chants arguments are being understood by others correctly, it seems to be leaning that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/926-yishten","name":"Yishten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar926_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T09:33:26-07:00","id":87538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87521#post87521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The danger is not that a particular class is unfit to govern. Every class is unfit to govern.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, this perfectly encapsulates my feelings on Exalted and the question of rule it poses. I like this quote!<br /> <br /> Just chipping in to point out that Exalted has <i>always </i>been about that question. It just does so in a way that puts the player in a position of power and lets them live with the consequences of their decisions. The Solar Exalted are presented in the manner they are so that these Utopian-Objectivist Richard Rahl's are seemingly sympathetic on purpose. It can be a game of pure power fantasy, or it can be <i>about </i>power in a fantasy setting, and it works on both levels.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1564-shinjo","name":"Shinjo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T09:43:18-07:00","id":87540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87394#post87394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If Plague disagrees, well he wasn't a Dev then. Of course, he is now</div> </div> </div> </div>Just as clarification, Plague has never been a developer and, if I recall correctly, is not even working on Exalted anymore.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T09:45:31-07:00","id":87541,"title":"","content":"Righteous is as ambiguous a term as &quot;good&quot; in my view. The term itself more or less means &quot;Does actions which are right&quot;. Quick look at the Goolge definition, it is even outright said as, &quot;(of a person or conduct) morally right or justifiable; virtuous&quot;. No one gets to decide this in Creation. Even when the Unconqured Sun decides it, it's his view of it. We seem to give weight to him on that choice, rather than just assume his choice is arbitrary and he gets to press it because he's king. <br /> <br /> Virtueousness is also a poor criteria for selecting Solar Exalted. Virtue is not an inherent good as the Virtues lead to contradictory and at their extremes, not especially liked behavior. Compassion makes you unable to commit harm against some who might need it, or do harm to those who you mean to help based on your biases. Conviction makes you monofocused monster. Temperance makes you detached from the world for order. Valor makes you a gallavanting asshole. Virtueousness is not goodness either then.<br /> <br /> Greatness is something that, by contrast, has less ambiguity. The Sun seems not so much caring with what sort of person you are with power. It's that you are someone who can be great wtiht hat power. Great doesn't mean you aren't going to always be good.<br /> <br /> Note in all of this it also sort of ignores the fact that great as applied to other Chosen. Luna still Exalts people who can be great, simply in her view of greatness (which is monstrosity to some extent). Sidereals are chosen form great potential destiinies. We'll likely see other bits about. But all Exalted are great. They are all heroes in the classical sense. <br /> <br /> Hippokreme's defintiion of heroic as pertains to Solars ignores other Exalts in its definition and in a way takes that heroism from other Exalted. Exalted's main premise of all sorts, the tagline lost in 2e has been &quot;What legends will they tell of your deeds?&quot; Not how you'll save the world. How they'll make it a better place. But what you will do to become history. Solar Exalted are Chosen not for their goodness or heroicness. They're chosen because they are exemplars of skill and people able to use power as the Sun might think works out. THey might fail in actually implementing that power in a way the Sun wanted, but that's on them entirely. And if legends are told of that failure, than the game works out. If you are remembered as Cao Cao, Vlad Tepes or Hassan-i Sabbah, you left your mark just as much as anyone else. Whether or not it was for what you thought was right for the world, or right for you to have more control of the world.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T10:19:59-07:00","id":87555,"title":"","content":"At what point did I say &quot;righteousness&quot; was completely objective? Why this insistence that these words (good, hero, righteous) can't be somewhat subjective without being meaningless? And why can't the Sun's personal opinion of what is right inform what sort of person his power Exalts? Why can't Exaltation take more into consideration than a count of your Ability dots? And while I'm at it, why exactly can't this mystical, metaphysical process be a little ambiguous?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 03-09-2014, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T10:33:33-07:00","id":87569,"title":"","content":"((Was totally off topic, so I removed it.))","signature":"","edited":{"userid":748,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/748-ultrafennec","user":"UltraFennec","date":". 03-09-2014, 02:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/748-ultrafennec","name":"UltraFennec","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar748_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T10:37:34-07:00","id":87571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87208#post87208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By emphatically moving it away from the shitdark approach from previous editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're confusing 'somewhat dark and savage' with shitdark. Shitdark means there's no hope and nothing's ever going to change. It means the setting has essentially *zero* lighter or remotely hopeful elements in it. It means that it's essentially a playground for crazy sadistic, masochistic people who want nothing more than to inflict and receive harm upon everyone.<br /> <br /> Shitdark is something you find in like, Warhammer 40K. Exalted is so far from that as a setting that your assertion is laughable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/748-ultrafennec","name":"UltraFennec","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar748_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T10:59:35-07:00","id":87577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>UltraFennec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87569#post87569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would strongly argue against any interpretation of Bruce Wayne being a good guy, or a good person, because of pretty much all the traits you just listed. Those are not the traits of a good person, they're the traits of someone that's every bit as psychotic and obsessive as the people he hunts down. The only real difference between Batman and his rogue's gallery is that Batman happens to be on the side that helps the general populace, and has a hang-up about killing people.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's important to bear in mind there are many different Batmans in different sources and storylines. Some of them easily qualify for a good guy (if a troubled one), others, not so much. It's the issue with legacy characters - every author has a different vision of the character, leading to inconsistent characterization across different sources. Hell, I can't find it now, but I've seen a D&amp;D alignment grid where every alignment from Lawful Good to Chaotic Evil was represented by a different interpretation of Batman, that's how blurry it got over the decades and tens of authors leaving their own print on the character.<br /> <br /> But I think the most basic idea of Batman is still that of a good guy, though certainly not a paladin type. At least, those renditions of Batman where I can still see the good guy in him are the ones I enjoy the most.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T11:00:47-07:00","id":87578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87555#post87555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At what point did I say &quot;righteousness&quot; was completely objective? Why this insistence that these words (good, hero, righteous) can't be somewhat subjective without being meaningless? And why can't the Sun's personal opinion of what is right inform what sort of person his power Exalts? Why can't Exaltation take more into consideration than a count of your Ability dots? And while I'm at it, why exactly can't this mystical, metaphysical process be a little ambiguous?</div> </div> </div> </div>Righteousness is as arbitrary a term in this case as goodness to me. It says someone has moral weight. The very term itself means &quot;what's morally right&quot; in a way. It's still in Creation simply an opinion, sure, but it creates a sort of moral imperative on the Exaltation (you were Chosen for your righteousness) which implies you have some moral authority, as it also assumes the Sun has moral authority.<br /> <br /> Or you could just say the Sun wants greatness. Which seems to me something folks can generally agree on more: bigness, ability to stand out, things like that. Which would fit the Solar magic thematics as well (which are about making you a great swordsman, businessman, assassin, survivor, whatever).<br /> <br /> For righteousness to be a criteria of Exaltation, it would result in righteousness (or goodness or whatever), things which we tend to put moral weight to, meaning shit. Because the Exalt himself is not impelled in any fashion to actually act righteous, good or whatever hwen they Exalt. It means the Sun's views are naive, since the person himself might not live up to his views. And it creates this idea that the person getting the Exaltation was morally more upright htan someone who got another Exaltation or didn't get one at all, because you're obviously more <i>righteous</i> than other candidates due to you know, haivng the Exaltation.<br /> <br /> I guess in moral argument form, look at it like this:<br /> <br /> P1: Solar Exalted are chosen from righteous people (whatever that is).<br /> P2: Solar Exalted therefore are righteous people.<br /> P3: Other Exaltations or sources of power are not necessarily chosen from righteous people.<br /> P4: From P3, this means there can be sources of power with no righteous people.<br /> P5: Righteousness by definition means moral weight.<br /> P6: Because Solars have a minimum of all being righteous, while other sources of power have a possibilty of no righteous people, there is an assumption that more Solars are righteous than other sources of power.<br /> C: Because of P5 and P6, Solar Exalted have more moral weight than other sources of power.<br /> <br /> Replace righteous with good. Or hippokreme's definition of heroic (which is good but co-opting other stuff). It leads to the same weight. Solars are either more good, more moral, or more whatever, inherently, than other Exalted. Something the game works to avoid. And something that isn't even what Solars are really meant to be more of. <br /> <br /> Solars are meant to be more <i>powerful</i> than other Exalted. They are chosen by paragons of skill. Solars are chosen about what they <i>can </i><i>do</i>, not how morally upright they are. Solars are chosen because they'll make good Solars. It's somewhat tautological, but putting qualitative statements to things which often have moral or societal preferences involved is a route of folly and more or less a rejection of the game's premises.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T11:03:34-07:00","id":87580,"title":"","content":"((Quoted post was removed by OP for being off topic, this one was likewise removed))","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T11:05:35-07:00","id":87582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87361#post87361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I say every Solar is &quot;good&quot; at the moment of Exaltation, what I mean is that every person who receives Solar Exaltation is a person who believes in some state of affairs as ideal beyond their own involvement in it, and who endeavors to bring that state of affairs about. Freedom. Democracy. Literacy. Longevity. Piety. Justice.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kunoichi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87409#post87409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about Control, Vengeance, Tyranny, Conquest, Anarchy, Dogma or Bloodlust?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, for that matter, what about Wealth, Beauty, Enlightenment, Indulgence, Love, or Peace of Mind? All are essentially noble, but also self-centered, and some are really easy to achieve.<br /> <br /> (By the way the &quot; not\u00b4an upstanding citizen in a Western democratic republic&quot; thing probably shouldn't be a followed by a bunch of ideals associated with precisely that.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T11:06:08-07:00","id":87584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87401#post87401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think, from this quote, we can infer that the intent for Solars is not that they have any default moral characteristic, as much as I want that to be the case. Instead, John intends to draw on heroes like Odysseus and Beowulf whose moral character is not central or even relevant to their stories.<br /> <br /> I like Exalted better my way, but the weight of the evidence has crushed me. I concede Solars-as-intended don't have to be &quot;good&quot;, even in the permissive definition of &quot;good&quot; I've given in this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea John proposes is what allows your idea of subjective good to really come into play when you want it to do so, in my reckoning. And I must say I was misjudging your stance somewhat, your ideas are more similar to mine than I thought and perhaps than I presented myself as.<br /> <br /> <br /> I do still find the OP to be...more objective than is good for the setting and tone of Exalted. It just doesn't sound like a subjective, workable definition to me, but an objective, high-view one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/748-ultrafennec","name":"UltraFennec","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar748_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T11:10:57-07:00","id":87590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>UltraFennec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87569#post87569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I would strongly argue against any interpretation of Bruce Wayne being a good guy, or a good person, because of pretty much all the traits you just listed. Those are not the traits of a good person, they're the traits of someone that's every bit as psychotic and obsessive as the people he hunts down. The only real difference between Batman and his rogue's gallery is that Batman happens to be on the side that helps the general populace, and has a hang-up about killing people.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is exactly my point about righteousness. It's a less loaded term, in that sense. People have trouble with &quot;good but also crazy&quot;, or more generally using &quot;good&quot; as an adjective to describe someone who anything less than unambiguously good (and that much moreso when morality is accepted as inherently subjective). And this is part of the appeal of the savage world of Creation; virtually no one is completely good. But it's hard not to frame Batman as righteous, and it's equally hard to put the vast majority of his rogues' gallery in that frame. Righteousness is intrinsically linked to the perspective and values system of the actor. This dovetails with the tragedy of the Solars, which is that when you give someone with righteousness in their heart Infinite Cosmic Power, sometimes it warps their perspective enough and they become monstrous, or, more subtly, both their good qualities AND their bad ones get magnified equally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T11:13:00-07:00","id":87593,"title":"","content":"*lots of people saying &quot;solars should have good intentions&quot; = boring*<br /> <br /> Really? I mean seriously, unless i've jumped into another universe while I've slept, and my experiences are thus invalid, my impression is that 99% of people want to do &quot;good&quot;... by their own biased, limited, twisted understanding of what &quot;good&quot; is, and with limited willpower and perseverance and temperance.<br /> <br /> So yeah, by all means, have the Ignis Divine inbue his exaltations with some &quot;good&quot; qualification in the people they seek out. The result really shouldn't change much at all. People are people. The road to hell is paved with good intentions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2438-satori","name":"Satori","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T11:18:30-07:00","id":87603,"title":"","content":"I do belive all solars are heroes, but i think heroism is in the eye of the beholder. After all Hitler is the hero of arians and neo nazis.<br /> <br /> But i do not believe such extreme examples of twisted heroism should be played, unless its part of a story of redemption. I think those cases are great way to avoid black and white morals in the game, to remember the PC that their heroes journey might be look upon as villany by other parties.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2245-quimeradc","name":"Quimeradc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T11:35:29-07:00","id":87614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satori</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87593#post87593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*lots of people saying &quot;solars should have good intentions&quot; = boring*</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there are also some of us who simply think that &quot;Solars should have good intentions&quot; is fundementally problematic for other reasons (mainly making other Exalts not have such a qualification leads to bad conclusions). This is in addition to being boring.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satori</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87593#post87593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? I mean seriously, unless i've jumped into another universe while I've slept, and my experiences are thus invalid, my impression is that 99% of people want to do &quot;good&quot;... by their own biased, limited, twisted understanding of what &quot;good&quot; is, and with limited willpower and perseverance and temperance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly feel that folks don't always do things because it's &quot;good&quot;. They do things becuase it's safe, it leads to good results, and people generally don't like to hurt other people due to guilt or consequences. Exaltation removes a lot of the consequences part, which warps how people act really quickly as has been seen with general human studies on power dynamics. Exaltation shouldn't really be expected to do anything to stop that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satori</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87593#post87593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So yeah, by all means, have the Ignis Divine inbue his exaltations with some &quot;good&quot; qualification in the people they seek out. The result really shouldn't change much at all. People are people. The road to hell is paved with good intentions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then why should the Solar Exaltations be specially made for good intentions, which is not shown in the power set? Why should it have any real imbuement besides granting the ability to act on whatever intention you want?<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T11:49:36-07:00","id":87623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>UltraFennec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87571#post87571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you're confusing 'somewhat dark and savage' with shitdark. Shitdark means there's no hope and nothing's ever going to change. It means the setting has essentially *zero* lighter or remotely hopeful elements in it. It means that it's essentially a playground for crazy sadistic, masochistic people who want nothing more than to inflict and receive harm upon everyone.<br /> <br /> Shitdark is something you find in like, Warhammer 40K. Exalted is so far from that as a setting that your assertion is laughable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not confusing anything, perhaps you just have a more optimistic outlook on the whole Thousand Dooms situation than I do.<br /> <br /> As it stands, 1E is canonically doomed no matter what the Exalted do. 2E <i>not</i> being like this is entirely unsupported by the books when there's an apocalyptic threat lurking under every rock and everyone who might be able to do something about them is either gearing up for a civil war, too busy doing celestial paperwork, or invariably being driven crazy by the Great Curse because they have no ability to resist it (setting aside the Infernals, who are probably the best bet for the whole saving the world thing on account of Torment having a release valve packaged with it).<br /> <br /> It really isn't that much different from 40K -- the main difference is that Exalted has player characters who matter and can influence things, but even they have limit tracks and no ability to resist when the game decides to take away their character sheets for a few scenes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":834,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","user":"HK-87","date":". 03-09-2014, 02:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T11:56:52-07:00","id":87632,"title":"","content":"Man, this is a tough conversation to participate in from my phone! I apologize for the terrible lack of line breaks but try as I might they don't seem to take. @Blaque: Your postulates and conclusion above all seem to point to two hidden postulates: P1) the perspective Solars, the Exaltations, and the Unconquered Sun are all unambiguously *consistent and correct* in their judgments. P2) Moral weight is a thing that exists outside an individual's own value system. I'm suggesting neither of these things. A prospective Exalt can be righteous (from their own perspective and within the strictures of an Exaltation) and still do awful things in the name of their own sense of right (e.g. Lyta). And to the point of Solars vs other Exalts, if there isn't any objective morality, the most you can really conclude is that Solars as a group are somewhat more likely to *act like* they have moral authority than other Exalts, which is definitely consistent with their history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T12:01:21-07:00","id":87635,"title":"","content":"Re: &quot;99% of people want to do good&quot;, well, yes most people would rather do &quot;good&quot; than &quot;evil&quot;. <br /> <br /> But most people aren't actually that motivated by wanting to do good. <br /> <br /> People generally are motivated by sex, love, friendship, loyalty, power, money, achievements, ego, threats, knowledge, revenge, delusions and madness, etc.<br /> <br /> A shifting mix of those is closer to most people's real motivations than a general desire to &quot;do good&quot; or &quot;change the world for the better&quot; or a statement like &quot;Free all the slaves in the North&quot; or whatever.<br /> <br /> Now, most people will, if they have power and they are put into a situation, try to do the right thing rather than the evil thing - they'll try to prevent exploitation, murder, theft. <br /> <br /> But that's not what motivates them. It's not their mission in life or their purpose. That's just what comes of being an average person confronted with the morally unacceptable.<br /> <br /> And the Solars are true to this, I think.<br /> <br /> You could come up with good dramas from lots of people who all have a mission to &quot;make the world a better place&quot; coming into conflict. Solars don't seem written like that. They're generally all sorts of people who wield talent and determination to overcome larger than life obstacles (and, like, Chant pretty much admitted as much a few pages ago).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T12:11:34-07:00","id":87643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87635#post87635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: &quot;99% of people want to do good&quot;, well, yes most people would rather do &quot;good&quot; than &quot;evil&quot;. But most people aren't actually that motivated by wanting to do good. People generally are motivated by sex, love, friendship, loyalty, power, money, achievements, ego, threats, knowledge, revenge, delusions and madness, etc. A shifting mix of those is closer to most people's real motivations than a general desire to &quot;do good&quot; or &quot;change the world for the better&quot; or a statement like &quot;Free all the slaves in the North&quot; or whatever. Now, most people will, if they have power and they are put into a situation, try to do the right thing rather than the evil thing - they'll try to prevent exploitation, murder, theft. But that's not what motivates them. It's not their mission in life or their purpose. That's just what comes of being an average person confronted with the morally unacceptable. And the Solars are true to this, I think. You could come up with good dramas from lots of people who all have a mission to &quot;make the world a better place&quot; coming into conflict. Solars don't seem written like that. They're generally all sorts of people who wield talent and determination to overcome larger than life obstacles (and, like, Chant pretty much admitted as much a few pages ago).</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually, most (all?) Solars seem to have some strongly held belief about something that's wrong with the world that they want to make better at the core of their character. Even Havesh, the go-to for an &quot;unheroic&quot; Solar exemplar, is rooted in a deep hatred for the injustice of the Varangian caste system (and is strongly implied to be on a path to using his powers to combat it, once he gets past using them primarily to live above his station).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T12:13:07-07:00","id":87644,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting that in 1e contained a &quot;Nature&quot; mechanic like that of the oWoD games to describe and define the core of your character's personality, and the list of possible Natures for your PC included such things as &quot;Hedonist&quot; and &quot;Thrillseeker.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T12:16:25-07:00","id":87648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87632#post87632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... @Blaque: Your postulates and conclusion above all seem to point to two hidden postulates: P1) the perspective Solars, the Exaltations, and the Unconquered Sun are all unambiguously *consistent and correct* in their judgments. P2) Moral weight is a thing that exists outside an individual's own value system. I'm suggesting neither of these things. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue here then is that if righteousness is arbitrary, then is it righteousness? You hit the Euthyphro dilema if you do that don't you? If all good is what you think it is, and all that makes you Chosen is the Sun thought you are good, is it good because the Sun's views are good ones, or because he has the power to say they're good ones? The moment that somoene like the OP tries to say that Exalted of a certain sort are some quantifiable value term, it feels to hit this. And since Creation has no objective good as a known fact, all it is is arbitrarily &quot;God thinks so&quot; and it's not relaly important to whether you got your Exaltation or not.<br /> <br /> Or in other words, if the righteous can be wrong, what is it exaclty besides personal motivation and self-confidence? Why give it flowery weighted terms like righteous when in the end it is how sure you are of your actions?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87632#post87632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... A prospective Exalt can be righteous (from their own perspective and within the strictures of an Exaltation) and still do awful things in the name of their own sense of right (e.g. Lyta). ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Or feel entitled to just do stuff that takes lots of balls to do. Like Hevash and Fehim. Neither have ever been presented in thinking themselves as righteous. They think they were fucked. And act more or less in response to this view. Likewise many inspirational figures in Exalted tend to not be so good either. Conan, Sindbad, Zorayas or Cao Cao don't come accross as people doing stuff because they thought htey were righteous. They often seem to be doing stuff because they want stuff, and think they can get it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87632#post87632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... And to the point of Solars vs other Exalts, if there isn't any objective morality, the most you can really conclude is that Solars as a group are somewhat more likely to *act like* they have moral authority than other Exalts, which is definitely consistent with their history.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you need to do it by introducing what accounts to fake objective morality though? Could this not be done through general external political justification, ad hoc, rather than something programmed into the Exaltation? The former seems more going with the realpolitk and your behavior being on your head more than it being something that qualified you to get the golden shining in the first place.<br /> <br /> As I feel, even fake moral weight shouldn't be in the Exaltation. This is in part due to poor consequences on how it represents other Exalts in-setting and how players often will ride these to often stupid conclusions as an addition.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T12:22:53-07:00","id":87654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87643#post87643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Actually, most (all?) Solars seem to have some strongly held belief about something that's wrong with the world that they want to make better at the core of their character. Even Havesh, the go-to for an &quot;unheroic&quot; Solar exemplar, is rooted in a deep hatred for the injustice of the Varangian caste system (and is strongly implied to be on a path to using his powers to combat it, once he gets past using them primarily to live above his station).</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you want to run through some more examples? Havesh doesn't seem motivated, at his core, by a desire to make the world better or any sort of altruism. He seems motivated by revenge (yes, against the Varangian caste system) and hedonism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T12:25:03-07:00","id":87655,"title":"","content":"For me, &quot;Solars are heroes&quot; doesn't undermine the heroism of other splats, just like &quot;Lunars are barbarians and shamans&quot; doesn't invalidate a dragon-blooded Conan or an Abyssal witch doctor. It provides a starting place for understanding the Exalt and their themes.<br /> <br /> I find it difficult to think of a better one. &quot;Solars are whatever you want&quot; makes it sound like GURPS. I suppose &quot;Solars are superhumans&quot; works, though I don't find it very evocative.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87648#post87648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue here then is that if righteousness is arbitrary, then is it righteousness?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have an issue with arbitrary words. Superman believes in &quot;Truth, justice, and the American Way.&quot; Those are all highly arbitrary, but it's still a meaningful statement.<br /> <br /> I'd suggest that most meaningful words - love, truth, hope, compassion, bravery, duty, friendship - are likewise arbitrary. What they mean to you is likely not exactly what they mean to me.<br /> <br /> That doesn't invalidate them as concepts. That just means they're not simple and easy.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 03-09-2014, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T12:34:20-07:00","id":87660,"title":"","content":"This whole thread has made me think of the portrayal of superheroes in Garth Ennis' <b>The Boys</b> and now I kind of want to run a Wyld Hunt game in which the players are basically the Boys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T12:58:40-07:00","id":87676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87478#post87478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chant, the definition of 'good' you are using in this thread is completely indistinguishable from heroic in the greek sense. When being 'good' simply means doing what you believe is right, then even Hitler is a hero and the closest you get to evil is a couch potato.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Yes!</i> And no.<br /> <br /> Not every Great person is doing something they think is Good. Wizard of Oz offered a good example of Alexander the Great, who conquered for the sake of conquest, self-aggrandisement, and self-enrichment. Not because he wanted to reshape the societies of those conquered, not because he wanted to set the world in some state of affairs that he thought was best, but simply because he had a drive to be great. And, as Wizard of Oz pointed out, that doesn't fit with even my lax definition of &quot;good&quot;.<br /> <br /> That's why Solars are interesting. Exalted is not a setting where there is some Plane of Cupcakes whose inherent properties can objectively judge the moral character of your actions. It's a setting where, to the extent that good exists, it is there to be examined and questioned and argued about. And even though I've conceded the point of what the writers intend to convey about the setting, I will always be much more interested in the notion that Solars are good but now they have to grapple with what that <i>means</i> (which the Unconquered Sun won't do) than the notion that Solars are just as statistically amoral as everything that makes up the setting's status quo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2404-chant","name":"Chant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2404_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T13:06:53-07:00","id":87680,"title":"","content":"And yet, Alexander the Great was a textbook Solar, Survival Charms and all<sup>1</sup>.<br /> <br /> <sup>1: They say he tamed a horse that could not be tamed</sup><sup>, and that this prompted his father to declare that he should conquer himself a kingdom worthy of him than Macedon.</sup>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T13:25:02-07:00","id":87693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87644#post87644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's worth noting that in 1e contained a &quot;Nature&quot; mechanic like that of the oWoD games to describe and define the core of your character's personality, and the list of possible Natures for your PC included such things as &quot;Hedonist&quot; and &quot;Thrillseeker.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh man, good times. I remember games where nearly everybody would take Thrillseeker and we'd have long Nobilis-style philosophical discussions about whether a given thing was risky enough to qualify for WP regen, given that you were a Solar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T13:38:54-07:00","id":87704,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><i>(Momentary thread diversion for the sake of Humor...)</i></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87676#post87676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exalted is not a setting where there is some <b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Plane of Cupcakes</span></b> whose inherent properties can objectively judge the moral character of your actions</div> </div> </div> </div>Step away from the Cupcakes Chant!!!<br /> <br /> If there is one thing in the world we don't pick on, it is Cupcakes...along with Kitties and Puppies. But mostly Cupcakes...especially with Chocolate Icing. Or Vanilla Icing...or Banana Cream...or...well, most any Icing on Cupcakes will do, as long as they are moist and taste good. Mmmmmm...Cupcakes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And I for one would like to see a Plane of Cupcakes!!! Can we have a Solar Spell that takes us there??? Huh? Well Devs??? This would go well with the Chef Thread from a while back.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">(I now return you to you're regularly scheduled Thread).</span><br /> <br /> Peace.<br /> <br /> <br /> ~ N<br /> <br /> <br /> Ni, Peng and Neee-Wom!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is timing in everything. Timing in strategy cannot be mastered without a great deal of practice. There is also timing in the Void. You win battles with the timing in the Void born of the timing of cunning by knowing the enemies' timing, and thus using a timing which the enemy does not expect.&quot; <i>Shinmen Musashi no Kami Fujiwara no Genshin, Go Rin No Sho (The Book of the Five Rings)</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2141-nadrakas","name":"Nadrakas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T13:44:57-07:00","id":87706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87655#post87655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...I don't have an issue with arbitrary words. Superman believes in &quot;Truth, justice, and the American Way.&quot; Those are all highly arbitrary, but it's still a meaningful statement.<br /> <br /> I'd suggest that most meaningful words - love, truth, hope, compassion, bravery, duty, friendship - are likewise arbitrary. What they mean to you is likely not exactly what they mean to me.<br /> <br /> That doesn't invalidate them as concepts. That just means they're not simple and easy.</div> </div> </div> </div>That being said, they are also so subjective and prone to contradictory defintiions that then going and saying an Exalt sort is defined by such people having this apparently unpinnable quality leads either to pointless pixel-bitching as to waht the term is (as this thread shows) or in wrost cases, some people thinking it does mean something and pressing that it should be that for all presentations of tha thing (as you seem to be doing in the onset of this thread).<br /> <br /> Words can be broad and hard to pin down, sure. Normatives and why they should be as you say them are a different beast. In rejecting your entire opening premise as mostly &quot;It should be this because I say so&quot; so far, I have yet to be convinced that &quot;heroism&quot; as you define it should be either a necessary condition of Solarness or a sufficient conditon of &quot;being Solar enough&quot;.<br /> <br /> Heroism as Exalted has used it is now how you define it. And making it a necessary condition of Solar Exaltation appears to have demeaning results for it not needing to be there or defined differently for other Exalted.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":353,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","user":"Blaque","date":". 03-09-2014, 04:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T13:53:39-07:00","id":87714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokreme</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, &quot;Solars are heroes&quot; doesn't undermine the heroism of other splats, just like &quot;Lunars are barbarians and shamans&quot; doesn't invalidate a dragon-blooded Conan or an Abyssal witch doctor. It provides a starting place for understanding the Exalt and their themes.<br /> <br /> I find it difficult to think of a better one. &quot;Solars are whatever you want&quot; makes it sound like GURPS. I suppose &quot;Solars are superhumans&quot; works, though I don't find it very evocative....</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for two posts. Things got weird in trying to edit things here. <br /> <br /> The thing though you seem to dismiss is that being a hero means you don't have to be good. Sindbad, Odysseus, and Achilles wanted things and did stuff to get to those things. Alexander the Great conquered for conquering's sake. Conan did a boatload of things more out of pride and thrill-seeking more than he did out of altruism. Zorayas went and reconquered Zojad <i>because it was her's and she fucking could</i>. These are great heroic and legendary people. I thintk hat's more itneresting than the detailed minutia bullshit of how in the end it was a right thing. Sometimes people do what might be seen as wrong by others and instead of justifying it as some act of righteousness, they can be honest; they wanted something and they did it. What moral weight to things after that is often post hoc. Not every story gets a nice bow of &quot;It was the right thing in the end.&quot; This is not hisotry, which Exalted draws a lot on, nor the source material that Exalted also draws a lot on often give a shit about.<br /> <br /> Solars aren't superhuman, they're iconically human. That's what's interesting about them. Stories of intristicaly good people in a bad world are a dime a dozen. People who are people in their world who do things as relates to the expectations fo that world, be it to buck the trends or to push them to their logical results is more interesting to me. But note I dont' also go starting threads declaring that a word in a context mean what I say it is because I say it does.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T14:17:57-07:00","id":87722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87706#post87706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That being said, they are also so subjective and prone to contradictory defintiions that then going and saying an Exalt sort is defined by such people having this apparently unpinnable quality leads either to pointless pixel-bitching as to waht the term is (as this thread shows) or in wrost cases, some people thinking it does mean something and pressing that it should be that for all presentations of tha thing (as you seem to be doing in the onset of this thread).<br /> <br /> Words can be broad and hard to pin down, sure. Normatives and why they should be as you say them are a different beast. In rejecting your entire opening premise as mostly &quot;It should be this because I say so&quot; so far, I have yet to be convinced that &quot;heroism&quot; as you define it should be either a necessary condition of Solarness or a sufficient conditon of &quot;being Solar enough&quot;.<br /> <br /> Heroism as Exalted has used it is now how you define it. And making it a necessary condition of Solar Exaltation appears to have demeaning results for it not needing to be there or defined differently for other Exalted.<br /> <br /> And stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>(Nod)...like the word is. Who knew that it would be difficult to define: <a href=\"http://www.slate.com/articles/news_and_politics/chatterbox/1998/09/bill_clinton_and_the_meaning_of_is.html\" target=\"_blank\">Is</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://youtu.be/j4XT-l-_3y0\" data-code=\"j4XT-l-_3y0\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/j4XT-l-_3y0/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Is, defined: &quot;3rd person singular present indicative of be.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> ...pinning words down, as you said Blaque, is very subjective. If &quot;is&quot; was so difficult to pin down, it is not so difficult to understand how this discussion has so many differing opinions on Heroism and what makes a Solar a Solar. <i>(Shrug)</i> Which in the end, is the point -- there are no two Solars that are the same, each one is an individual, and each one is a &quot;Hero&quot; in their own right. Here is an excerpt from 2E on Exaltation:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">-- &quot;<b>The Exaltation demands heroes:</b> Exaltation is a fundamental alteration of destiny, turn a mortal into a semi-divine weapon. To be capable of benefiting from the Exaltation\u2019s power, the Exalt-to-be must already have an important destiny. No Exalt is unwilling to wield his power. The Exaltation is not a rational or moral force, though. It simply seeks out beings who can and will wield divine power. It could descend on the most pious of hermits or the most immoral of rascals, so long as the chosen one is of consequence to history and will put its might to use.&quot; <i>(Exalted Core, Page 32)</i></div> <br /> By this definition of Hero, they are not &quot;Good&quot; by any stretch of the mind.<br /> <br /> As Chant posted earlier... <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Originally posted by [B</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">John M\u00f8rke[/B]]<br /> Solars are myth-heroes. It is a myth-hero's purpose to subvert mythos and thereby define it. Solars fight, destroy, and ultimately recreate the status-quo, doing so by conquering the obliquely magical through acts of sheer will, force, and skill writ-large, like every myth-hero in literature.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is a better description, and it doesn't have Solars as inherently being &quot;Good.&quot; They are people who go forth and change the world. They are Heroes, in the Ancient meaning of the word as opposed to the modern definition.<br /> <br /> Peace.<br /> <br /> <br /> ~ N<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is timing in everything. Timing in strategy cannot be mastered without a great deal of practice. There is also timing in the Void. You win battles with the timing in the Void born of the timing of cunning by knowing the enemies' timing, and thus using a timing which the enemy does not expect.&quot; <i>Shinmen Musashi no Kami Fujiwara no Genshin, Go Rin No Sho (The Book of the Five Rings)</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2141-nadrakas","name":"Nadrakas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T14:21:48-07:00","id":87725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87706#post87706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And making it a necessary condition of Solar Exaltation appears to have demeaning results for it not needing to be there or defined differently for other Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've come back to this idea several times. Let me see if I understand it correctly.<br /> <br /> If: All Solars are Chosen for being good<br /> Then: Non-Solars, as a group, are not good.<br /> <br /> That's ... very confusing to me. It's like saying &quot;if NASA only picks smart people to be astronauts, that constitutes an insult to all doctors.&quot; It sounds like you're equating &quot;all members of set A have trait X&quot; with &quot;<b>only</b> members of set A have trait X&quot;, which is ... flatly illogical. So I hope I've simply misunderstood your position.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2404-chant","name":"Chant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2404_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T14:44:27-07:00","id":87744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87725#post87725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You've come back to this idea several times. Let me see if I understand it correctly.<br /> <br /> If: All Solars are Chosen for being good<br /> Then: Non-Solars, as a group, are not good.<br /> <br /> That's ... very confusing to me. It's like saying &quot;if NASA only picks smart people to be astronauts, that constitutes an insult to all doctors.&quot; It sounds like you're equating &quot;all members of set A have trait X&quot; with &quot;<b>only</b> members of set A have trait X&quot;, which is ... flatly illogical. So I hope I've simply misunderstood your position.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is being said is there's a case where all of x, where x is a Solar, than x is good. Or in predicate logic:<br /> <br /> (x)(Solar(x) \u2192 Good(x)) In this case x is an individual person.<br /> <br /> Now it is true that due to how this works, Good(x) can be true even if Solar(x) is not. But note that it it's not the other case around. If you aren't at some level somewhere good, you can't be a Solar by this way it has been laid out.<br /> <br /> This then leads to a situation where all Solar Exalted are good to some level at some time to get their Exaltation. No other Exalt has this mandate. This means any Solar you meet, even if you don't agree with them, is at least &quot;good&quot; in their mind (since hippokreme, who I am criticizing in this thread, conflates heroism with goodness). But any other Exalt is not so necessitated as to being good. And in fact, as there's no necessity of goodness from the other Exalt, there's no real real restriction on making all non-Solars blackhats. Yes, that's an extreme position. Surely there are good non-Solars out there. But there's no minimum like with Solars (universal) to there being good of other Exalts. While every Solar you run into has to be a good person, there's nothing apparently there to makes it so every Dragon-Blooded isn't an entitled fucker or that every Abyssal is a murderous psychopath.<br /> <br /> In the end it both chokes-off Solar story options (by apparently making Solars at some level, even if they change, &quot;good people&quot; inherently), and it also makes it so every non-Solar is at a state where they ahve to prove their goodness, something Solars apparently get for free.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T15:05:58-07:00","id":87762,"title":"","content":"I think the real problem with defining Solars as good in the context of Exalted is, it takes some of the punch off the idea that consequences are important. In my experience, people tend to go easy on those who make mistakes or take crazy risks when the intent behind their action is judged as good, downplaying the possible or actual negative consequences of failure, because it doesn't sound like a good idea to dissuade people from attempting to do good, even if the effort is less than perfect.<br /> <br /> Exalted, it seems, likes to take a more cynical view of that - no, it doesn't matter how noble your intents were. The road to hell is paved with good intentions; what really matters are results. If you screwed up, it's all on you, and nobody will ask why you tried in the first place. If you succeed, nobody will argue morals with a winner. I think this outlook is much more appropriate for the genres Exalted is supposed to emulate - many myths and pulp stories tell of the exploits of heroes of relatively low morals, and morality plays are way more interesting when it's not predetermined who holds the moral high ground in the particular conflict.<br /> <br /> Note that it doesn't preclude the idea of particular Solars, or any other heroes of Creation, trying their best to be good people - it just makes it more challenging and complicated for them, but when have challenges and complications ever stopped a Big Damn Hero?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T15:13:37-07:00","id":87766,"title":"","content":"Again, brevity owed to mobile device. But @Blaque, given your formal logic, can't it be the case that Lunar, Sidereal, and even Alchemical Exaltations consider &quot;heroism&quot; (goodness, righteousness, whatever) as a criteria, just not with the same priority that Solar Exaltations do? I mean considering the &quot;typical&quot; inhabitant of the Creation, the sort of world it is and the sort of person you'd probably be to become an overachieving paragon of skill in it, isn't it kind of conspicuous that of the Solars we do have, so *few* of them are outright assholes, and fewer still immediately go full genocidal megalomaniac when blessed with Amoral Solar Cosmic Power? Doesn't that alone suggest some bias toward &quot;good&quot; and away from &quot;evil&quot; people on the part of Solar Exaltation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T15:24:43-07:00","id":87770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87744#post87744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, that's an extreme position. Surely there are good non-Solars out there. But there's no minimum like with Solars (universal) to there being good of other Exalts. While every Solar you run into has to be a good person, there's nothing apparently there to makes it so every Dragon-Blooded isn't an entitled fucker or that every Abyssal is a murderous psychopath.<br /> <br /> In the end it both chokes-off Solar story options (by apparently making Solars at some level, even if they change, &quot;good people&quot; inherently), and it also makes it so every non-Solar is at a state where they ahve to prove their goodness, something Solars apparently get for free.<br /> <br /> And stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're posing a problem to which the solution is &quot;don't run a game full of black and white morality&quot;. Yes, you <i>can</i> depict non-Solars as broadly evil or degenerate, but there's no reason you have to, or even that you should. The situation is analogous to the Virtue system at character creation. Every Exalted character has at least one Virtue of at least 3. That statement is entirely focused on the Exalted, and it doesn't mean that normal mortals seldom have high Virtues. It doesn't mean the setting is designed so that the Storyteller should play all non-Exalted NPCs as having Virtues of 1 or 2 across the board.<br /> <br /> It's not useful to say that a setting proposition chokes off story options. Literally everything about a setting constitutes a constraint to story options. Creation is flat? You can't do a story about being the first person to circumnavigate it. Whitewall is landlocked? You can't do a story about a naval blockade there. Solars are always great people and have some minimum of 5 Willpower? You can't do a story about a self-effacing genius with imposter syndrome.<br /> <br /> Sometimes you have to dispense with parts of the setting to make the story work, and that's okay. We shouldn't be shy of defining a setting in the first place just because it constrains our possibilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2404-chant","name":"Chant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2404_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T15:51:33-07:00","id":87783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87766#post87766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, brevity owed to mobile device. But @Blaque, given your formal logic, can't it be the case that Lunar, Sidereal, and even Alchemical Exaltations consider &quot;heroism&quot; (goodness, righteousness, whatever) as a criteria, just not with the same priority that Solar Exaltations do? ...</div> </div> </div> </div>You could. But then you hit a different issue where it still is a case in which Solars are presented as &quot;more heroic&quot; than other Exalted, whcih then gets into some of 2e's issues where it felt like the whole gamew as built as Solar Exalted and the Supporting Cast, mainly through some fo the same bits of my argument earlier. I would rather Exaltation be an enabler to heroic deeds as flavored for the Exalt type, rather than different heroic deeds being the reason you are Exalted emphasized as much (as defined classically and not modern daily).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87766#post87766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... I mean considering the &quot;typical&quot; inhabitant of the Creation, the sort of world it is and the sort of person you'd probably be to become an overachieving paragon of skill in it, isn't it kind of conspicuous that of the Solars we do have, so *few* of them are outright assholes, and fewer still immediately go full genocidal megalomaniac when blessed with Amoral Solar Cosmic Power? Doesn't that alone suggest some bias toward &quot;good&quot; and away from &quot;evil&quot; people on the part of Solar Exaltation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. It might just suggest that authors are more optimistic about writing characters than people might think. And a few of the guys we might think are good, it should be noted, still do some things we might not like. I love Jalith from Castebook: Dawn, but she did kind of just straight-up rob a jade shipment in one story. And Wind kind of does flaunt in an insulting fashion the previous objects of his position of a monk in a way that surprisingly doens't upset people. And even beyond all that, it is also a fact that this is in the end a ficitonal world with fictional characters who are categorized good or bad in their writing by the author/player. What they do or don't do that's good or evil should be that indivdiual creator's reasons fo rwhat's good fo the story, rather than a presciptive of the nature of their magic.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T16:05:53-07:00","id":87787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87770#post87770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're posing a problem to which the solution is &quot;don't run a game full of black and white morality&quot;. Yes, you <i>can</i> depict non-Solars as broadly evil or degenerate, but there's no reason you have to, or even that you should. The situation is analogous to the Virtue system at character creation. Every Exalted character has at least one Virtue of at least 3. That statement is entirely focused on the Exalted, and it doesn't mean that normal mortals seldom have high Virtues. It doesn't mean the setting is designed so that the Storyteller should play all non-Exalted NPCs as having Virtues of 1 or 2 across the board.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not depict Solars as a range of individuals with their own motivations, goals and such, without some prescripts towards some specific view of heroism though? Note I'm mostly rejecting the defintion in the OP. Since that hasn't been how Exalted has been defined ever. Heroes are not &quot;good people with good intentions.&quot; They are &quot;people who do great actions.&quot; Defining an Exalt type by the first implies they have a special inherent bit of being the white in a world that has no reason not to be black. This in part is what fueled 2e's stupidity at times. It assumed PCs were the good guys and the world itself was total shit for them tof ix. I would rather no assumption of &quot;good guy or bad guy&quot; be anywhere, even the protagnosit splat. If you end up with a team of sociopaths that's another story to tell. A flawed Virtue helps at least though add a chink to that, but I have just as often seen characters embrace it and go whole hog. Rather than being a &quot;good guy&quot; a person might well want their character to indeed go and conquer seventeen nations, use the Demon Lord to become inhumanely beautiful, and steal a manse's awesome diamonds via guile and seduction, all mainly becuase the world is there, you have the power and you want ot use it. That the brother more or less blowing you up out of revenge helped the world by destroying your sorcerer demon-army using empire is just a nice side effect, not his goal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87770#post87770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not useful to say that a setting proposition chokes off story options. Literally everything about a setting constitutes a constraint to story options. Creation is flat? You can't do a story about being the first person to circumnavigate it. Whitewall is landlocked? You can't do a story about a naval blockade there. Solars are always great people and have some minimum of 5 Willpower? You can't do a story about a self-effacing genius with imposter syndrome.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a false equivicacy though. As presented, some archetypical Solars aren't actually Solars based on the OP's post because they aren't &quot;good people doing good things&quot; or &quot;righteous people&quot; or &quot;people trying to change the world.&quot; Sindbad and Odysseus want to go home. That's it. Full stop. Zorayas in <i>Night's Master</i> gets power, and wants to use it. That's it. Conan as I gather more or less became a king because he could. That he was a good king is a nice side effect, but not his goal in life up to that point, which was pretty solidly heroic by then (which included a threat to a princess that if he and his mercenaries weren't paid they were going ot loot the city).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87770#post87770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometimes you have to dispense with parts of the setting to make the story work, and that's okay. We shouldn't be shy of defining a setting in the first place just because it constrains our possibilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>That as it may be, part of those intial constraints whas there is no good or evil as can as defined objectively. Then going and saying that an Exalt sort has to be a good guy (for realz even if they aren't) by default is one of those things that have never been in the setting's foundation and something I find surprsing to see people want to shove in.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T18:12:20-07:00","id":87843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87766#post87766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean considering the &quot;typical&quot; inhabitant of the Creation, the sort of world it is and the sort of person you'd probably be to become an overachieving paragon of skill in it, isn't it kind of conspicuous that of the Solars we do have, so *few* of them are outright assholes, and fewer still immediately go full genocidal megalomaniac when blessed with Amoral Solar Cosmic Power? Doesn't that alone suggest some bias toward &quot;good&quot; and away from &quot;evil&quot; people on the part of Solar Exaltation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Meeting the bare minimum qualities for not being an utter tool says amazingly little about somebody's moral character.<br /> <br /> I mean, seriously? &quot;Oh, hey, I never used my overwhelming power to completely wreck other people up, even though I totally could have&quot;. Well frickin' done, your cookies are in the mail.<br /> <br /> There's Petting the Dog, and then there's &quot;every dog that passes you by without getting a wallop is a testament to your bias towards good&quot;.<br /> <br /> A hell of a lot of the time, Solars are going to be people where their character and intentions can be analogous to &quot;I'm going to hunt down a ravenous dragon and pull its head off to mount in a trophy room, because I'm totally powerful enough to do that now&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T18:43:35-07:00","id":87853,"title":"","content":"I could say, at least, that the mythic narrative that culminates in Solar Exaltation is one that doesn't really include acts of arbitrary horror and cruelty.<br /> <br /> That's not to say that there won't be Solars who, before or after their Second Breath, weren't kind of monsters, but you're at least not likely to be Chosen <i>because</i> you had monstrous qualities. That's not to say that the Sun happened to catch you at a time where he could be tricked into thinking you weren't one, just that, for the purposes of Exalting you, he's looking at you in terms of an atomic, holistic version of who you are and who you can be, a vision that sees you as pointed towards an idealized version of yourself; a shining and glorious testament to human will and audacity.<br /> <br /> That's a vision that kind of fails to include your capacity for shifts in mood and priority, or your social and personal context, mind.<br /> <br /> You know, people focus a lot on Lyta and Havesh, because the former is pretty extreme and the latter is a bit crass, and both of them have book-length attention, but I'd personally be more saddened by what a proscription on being &quot;good people with good intentions&quot; would do to Ophilis Ses, who is hardly a good man, but is still probably a fair few steps up from being an especially terrible one. Ses is a criminal, and not likely to be a reluctant one, but he's a criminal largely because that was what was available to his person as a persecuted minority, and he rose high in his syndicate because he had the talents that makes one good at crime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T19:49:41-07:00","id":87887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87853#post87853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could say, at least, that the mythic narrative that culminates in Solar Exaltation is one that doesn't really include acts of arbitrary horror and cruelty.</div> </div> </div> </div>It <i>can</i> include plenty of non-arbitrary horror and cruelty, though, like David going out to kill one hundred Philistines to win Michal's hand in marriage, and returning with two hundred because he's just that cool.<br /> <br /> It's all in the presentation, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T22:01:36-07:00","id":87948,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?719650-Never-played-Exalted-Ask-the-Developer&amp;p=17702917#post17702917\" target=\"_blank\">hatewheel</a><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You would be playing one of the legendary Solar Exalted: <b>heroic</b> women and men chosen by the greatest of all gods, the Unconquered Sun, to go forth and bring the world back from the brink of death. As one of the Lawgivers, you are nigh-immortal, living thousands of years and seeing your power and legacy reincarnated again and again through various lifetimes. You have the powers of a divinity and as you develop the Essence of your character, his / her proclivities grow beyond all measure. A Solar can literally contend with gods: in the theater of the mind and the theater of drama, and in single combat. You will be playing a god king returned from death to reclaim your status as one of Creation's mightiest <b>heroes.</b> </div> </div> </div>Shit just got real, yo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T22:05:13-07:00","id":87954,"title":"","content":"Did I ever say Solars weren't heroes? I don't think anyone here has said that. I mainly have, and continue to, reject your specific definition of hero presented at the beginning of this thread.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T22:07:04-07:00","id":87957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87954#post87954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did I ever say Solars weren't heroes? I don't think anyone here has said that. I mainly have, and continue to, reject your specific definition of hero presented at the beginning of this thread.<br /> <br /> And stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>I posted that because it has something to do with the thread. It wasn't aimed at you specifically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T22:13:16-07:00","id":87963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87957#post87957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I posted that because it has something to do with the thread. It wasn't aimed at you specifically.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't assuming that. What I'm mostly pointing out is that the use of hero in a pitch isn't surprising. Your definition of hero in the thread's first paragraph, however, has yet to be defended as an alternative to how it is defined in usef for Exalted. Seems like a good idea to do that otherwise it seems like a non sequitur to me.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T23:00:02-07:00","id":87987,"title":"","content":"Solars will be heroes to some and villains to others. Just like most real life &quot;heroes.&quot;<br /> <br /> General Custer was viewed as a hero and martyr by many United States citizens. But ask the Native Americans who he slaughtered what they thought of him. Pancho Villa is revered by many as a revolutionary hero, but lots of people consider him nothing more than a murders bandit. Genghis Khan is a hero to the Mongolian people, but few non-Mongolians view him in nearly that much of a positive light. Hannibal was a hero and legend of Carthage but reviled as a demon and destroyer by the people of Rome. Achilles was the hero of the Trojan War, but the people of Troy didn't exactly love the guy.<br /> <br /> Being a hero doesn't mean being good. It doesn't mean being kung-fu-Gandhi. Being a hero in Exalted simply means being a person who does amazing things that can and will change the world. Some Solars will be generally nice dudes and try to do their best to bring good to the greatest number of people. Others will be like the Bull of the North and have a more narrow set of people they plan to bring &quot;good&quot; to. And some like Havesh will bring good to themselves and damn everybody else. They're all Solars, they're all heroes, they're just not all sunshine and rainbows.<br /> <br /> *EDIT* Ultimately the Solars are human, just like every other Exalt, and no more prone to be paladins than any other Exalt is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 03-10-2014, 04:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T23:15:06-07:00","id":87992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87623#post87623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not confusing anything, perhaps you just have a more optimistic outlook on the whole Thousand Dooms situation than I do.<br /> <br /> As it stands, 1E is canonically doomed no matter what the Exalted do. 2E <i>not</i> being like this is entirely unsupported by the books when there's an apocalyptic threat lurking under every rock and everyone who might be able to do something about them is either gearing up for a civil war, too busy doing celestial paperwork, or invariably being driven crazy by the Great Curse because they have no ability to resist it (setting aside the Infernals, who are probably the best bet for the whole saving the world thing on account of Torment having a release valve packaged with it).<br /> <br /> It really isn't that much different from 40K -- the main difference is that Exalted has player characters who matter and can influence things, but even they have limit tracks and no ability to resist when the game decides to take away their character sheets for a few scenes.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not true. 1st ed. assumed that there was a chance you could do everything right and still lose, but it never said that was a certainty by any means. From what I recall, 1st ed. hated saying things with certainty so your assertion is a very strange one to make. 2nd ed. liked to create plot hooks with apocalyptic overtones because people seemed to really latch onto those. That doesn't mean everyone is doomed, it just means the supplement writers thought that writing for Exalted meant turning things up to eleven for the sake of a crap definition of epic-ness (I have no doubt a lot of the blame for this is on the internet echo chamber bullshit that surrounded/surrounds Exalted). The Great Curse is an easy target for 'everything is awful', but once again, it's not a guarantee everything will be awful forever. It just means that there is a guarantee that something bad will happen occasionally/eventually given time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chant</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not every Great person is doing something they think is Good. Wizard of Oz offered a good example of Alexander the Great, who conquered for the sake of conquest, self-aggrandisement, and self-enrichment. Not because he wanted to reshape the societies of those conquered, not because he wanted to set the world in some state of affairs that he thought was best, but simply because he had a drive to be great. And, as Wizard of Oz pointed out, that doesn't fit with even my lax definition of &quot;good&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alexander was going well into megalomaniac territory and may have been planning on creating a one-world-one-empire situation. He took steps to integrate the Greek and Persian peoples and a lot of his generals hated him because he was trying to fuse the two cultures into one*. When you get down to it, Alexander killed a shitload of Greeks. Whether mercenaries in the service of Persia, rebels fighting against him, or casualties of his ambition plenty of the people he was trying to &quot;help&quot; died as a result. It's just that Alexander's version of Good was wrecking that place next door and taking all their stuff and giving it to his men. Which is a big thing in Exalted and why we're all here today I bet. We look at stuff through a set of beliefs that would be laughable to people from Alexander's era when it was commonly held that &quot;It is the right of the strong to rule the weak&quot; and &quot;It may have been wrong to take our empire, but we have no choice except to hold onto it now&quot;. Not a lot of credence given to Christian ideals such as universal forgiveness, meekness, or martyrdom.<br /> <br /> *That being said, Alexander's integration attempts were probably motivated by realpolitik and creating a counter-balance to the Macedonian military that he was reliant upon and thus subject to, as was amply demonstrated past the Indus river. However, the mythological Alexander was a visionary god-king that wanted to unite the people of Earth under one empire with one culture (namely, his culture plus the parts he liked from other cultures).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":407,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/407-ithle","user":"Ithle","date":". 03-10-2014, 02:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/407-ithle","name":"Ithle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T02:11:28-07:00","id":88034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87887#post87887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It <i>can</i> include plenty of non-arbitrary horror and cruelty, though, like David going out to kill one hundred Philistines to win Michal's hand in marriage, and returning with two hundred because he's just that cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>David's Exaltation narrative is where a prophet goes to his father's house, finds all of his brothers wanting, and then has his father call him in from the fields where God tells the prophet &quot;this is the one, anoint him&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T02:40:08-07:00","id":88038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87987#post87987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being a hero doesn't mean being good. <b>It doesn't mean being kung-fu-Gandhi</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gandhi is also an object of several controversies that make his life more ambiguous than some would like it to be.<br /> <br /> Which only adds to your point, mind you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T03:40:23-07:00","id":88050,"title":"","content":"Man, I'd really, really hate Exalted if the Solar Exaltation would immediately change a person's alignment to &quot;Lawful Good&quot;.<br /> <br /> Thankfully, that isn't the case. Exalted is a better game because of characters like Lyta or the Vanisher or Mirror Flag.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T03:44:35-07:00","id":88052,"title":"","content":"This has nothing to do with the conversation, but I really like Mirror Flag. She's easily my favorite Exalted character. I really hope she shows up some in 3rd edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T04:27:33-07:00","id":88062,"title":"","content":"I should be quite put out if Solars were heroes in the sense Hippokrene suggests. It is, in my opinion, a shallow treatment of heroism that does not interest me in the slightest, nor what draw me to Exalted. Fortunately, I have seen neither the developers nor the writers suggest such will be the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are no problems, only plothooks.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1P2AuLM6D1Et9mWQVJp-ugWujFJhTi2VwQBtOazOW1Mg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Terrifying Argent Witches Hub</a><br /> <i>Originally posted by </i><b><i>Dex Davican</i></b><br /> I need them for my collection: <i>Enormous Gonads of 2012: A Retrospective.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/920-imrix","name":"Imrix","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T04:33:59-07:00","id":88064,"title":"","content":"You know, there's this really goofy anime called Nobunagun going on at the moment, about an alien bunny who collected the DNA/souls from various famed historical figures so that, when a hostile alien race came to Earth, their reincarnations could be empowered to save the world.<br /> <br /> They're not all especially pleasant figures, and the main character is the return of Oda Nobunaga in his &quot;virtual demon lord&quot; anime phase, but they're all basically supposed to be people that can be relied on to fight for the survival of the human race.<br /> <br /> So that might help in seeing the Solar Exalted, considering John's comments in that RPG.Net thread; they're not necessarily good people, or have good intentions, but the Unconquered Sun at least sees them as likely to reverse the death spiral that the world is currently on (even if that means Genghis Khan imposing the Pax Mongolia on a huge swath of a continent, because stable and contiguous standards of law and trade are something that helps ward off the Wyld). This is not a thing Essential to Solars; it is not what they are categorically <i>for</i>. But it's what the world needs at the moment, and it's the standard the Unconquered Sun is holding his Chosen to (and hey, once it's reasonably considered to have been fulfilled, we can start talking about that whole &quot;King of Heaven provides divine assistance to the greatest civilisation on Earth).<br /> <br /> Contrast with the Abyssal Exalted, the Solar seen as the final nail in the coffin of a dying world, as interpreted by ghosts who've had a thousand years to brood over their deaths and decide that the Sidereals were <i>right</i> about how Solars can't be trusted for the sake of empowering themselves (emotionally, that is) and who, having died and lost the reason to live, hate the living world, and assume that all their Chosen need is to have the same losses and they'll hate it too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T04:57:36-07:00","id":88069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88064#post88064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, there's this really goofy anime called Nobunagun going on at the moment, about an alien bunny who collected the DNA/souls from various famed historical figures so that, when a hostile alien race came to Earth, their reincarnations could be empowered to save the world.<br /> <br /> They're not all especially pleasant figures, and the main character is the return of Oda Nobunaga in his &quot;virtual demon lord&quot; anime phase, but they're all basically supposed to be people that can be relied on to fight for the survival of the human race.</div> </div> </div> </div>That reminds me of an online webcomic, Saturday Morning Breakfast Cereal.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://www.smbc-comics.com/comics/20140212.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> *EDIT* I put it in spoiler tags since it's a fairly big comic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 03-10-2014, 08:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T05:05:41-07:00","id":88074,"title":"","content":"I would like to advocate for spoiler bars being prefaced by where the spoiler is coming from, as there could be references to stuff in things I have not yet seen or read but would like to, and I wouldn't know unless I opened it and then got spoiled, or there could be something referring to what is already within the range of what I've seen, or just plain don't care about, and can look at it comfortably.<br /> <br /> A format similar to what I present here (spoiler for last episode of first season of Dexter)<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The Ice Truck Killer is Dexter's brother.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It would be at least my personal preference, and I feel like it would make more effective use of concealing spoilers.<br /> <br /> (Apologies for prior petulant version of this post)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 03-10-2014, 08:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T05:24:01-07:00","id":88081,"title":"","content":"In this specific case, the spoiler was included to avoid taking up space with a huge image; it does not include spoilers for anything I know of. You're still right in that you can't know that unless the poster conveys that information.<br /> <br /> I also accidentally clicked open <i>your </i>spoiler box ARGH CURSES ETERNAL","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T05:44:55-07:00","id":88089,"title":"","content":"Dammit, I knew I should have put in some shit that nobody would care about purely for the sake of example.<br /> <br /> Well, it's fixed know, even if I can never fix the other transgression.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T05:50:39-07:00","id":88092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88089#post88089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, it's fixed know, even if I can never fix the other transgression.</div> </div> </div> </div> You SON OF A BITCH!<br /> <br /> No, I agree. No one cares about Dexter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/926-yishten","name":"Yishten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar926_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T07:58:03-07:00","id":88162,"title":"","content":"<i>Nobunagun</i> is surprisingly neat for some of the idea of Exalted incarnations too. Mainly how Nobunaga himself is Shion's Obi-Wan more through flashbacks of specific events useful for her at the time that might be relevant at that time. She's never actually talked to Nobunaga himself, just sort of acted based on residual memory.<br /> <br /> And while Nobunaga is generally a big bad guy in history and anime, it's kind of itneresting how he's a great example of mixed reputation. Much of what he did that made him lambasted at his time is stuff that actually to me seems pretty forward-thinking: pressed for a secular government, open markets, broke-up guilds, promoted based on competence for a major upward mobility setup, utilized modern warfare and administrative techniques. It's just that this was all spitting in the eye of folks in his day and that kind of stuck. And you can't go and make him a good guy either, since by dint of being a daimyo gunning to become shogun, he was actually a pretty ruthless bastard.<br /> <br /> Honestly a lot of Sengoku Era characters and how many times they're re-interpretted in modern Japanese fiction would show to me how much you get out of people in real life with nuance. Since it allows a neat cross section for a hero or villain as needed, especialy in what amounts to a dark age for the country from my gathering with all the fighting and things.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T08:20:29-07:00","id":88181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yishten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88092#post88092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, I agree. No one cares about Dexter.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> [sniff]<br /> <br /> Dex<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T08:25:33-07:00","id":88187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ithle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87992#post87992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not true. 1st ed. assumed that there was a chance you could do everything right and still lose, but it never said that was a certainty by any means. From what I recall, 1st ed. hated saying things with certainty so your assertion is a very strange one to make. 2nd ed. liked to create plot hooks with apocalyptic overtones because people seemed to really latch onto those. That doesn't mean everyone is doomed, it just means the supplement writers thought that writing for Exalted meant turning things up to eleven for the sake of a crap definition of epic-ness (I have no doubt a lot of the blame for this is on the internet echo chamber bullshit that surrounded/surrounds Exalted). The Great Curse is an easy target for 'everything is awful', but once again, it's not a guarantee everything will be awful forever. It just means that there is a guarantee that something bad will happen occasionally/eventually given time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that that actually IS true. My google fu is weak, but someone better than I can find the quote where Grabowski explicitly tells us how the canonical ending for (1E) Exalted is that all the factions pointlessly fight amongst each other until the sky falls down atop them all. He even urges you to reread the first paragraph of the Corebook if you don't believe it! (barring PC intervention, of course)<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T08:32:29-07:00","id":88190,"title":"","content":"To be fair, when Exalted 1st edition was released it was till being pushed as the pre-history to the World of Darkness. So things went wrong, everyone failed, the Wheel of Ages turned slowly, Creation decayed and became more boring, and we ended up with the world of the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Exalted also drew heavily from pulp fiction, much of which took place during ancient eras when men were men, somehow bigger and grander than they are today. -<br /> <br /> &quot;Long ago, in the ancient times before now...&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;A long, long time ago in a galaxy far, far away...&quot;<br /> <br /> etc. That was the tone that the writers were going for; that Exalted took place in an era of splendor unimaginable in the &quot;current&quot; era in which we live. <br /> <br /> That's why the first paragraph of Chapter 1 of the core book sets the tone for how the Exalted failed and Creation was ultimately bent and broken.<br /> <br /> I don't think 3rd edition is going for that.<br /> <br /> AnubisXy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T08:38:18-07:00","id":88192,"title":"","content":"My two Obols:<br /> <br /> ALL of the Exalted are Heroes. <br /> <br /> They are all Chosen to fight for something, and there's a community that lauds them for it. Even the &quot;villain&quot; splats! When Abyssals walk down the streets of stygia, dead mothers hold up their dead babies for the Deathknights to kiss. A Green Sun Prince can't walk down Malfeas' streets without demons crowding them for autographs and offering to buy them drinks that would kill a mortal, not because they're Cool, but because they are the key to getting them the hell out o hell, and retaking their rightful homeland. <br /> <br /> The problem with mandating that Solars, or anyone else, must be a &quot;good&quot; person, as I see it, is that you then must define what &quot;good person&quot; MEANS. And that kind of nailing down closes off way too many story/character possibilities. Better to keep it that they are Chosen for their willingness to use their power to change the world. You can Exalt among the underclasses of Grayfalls, and play out a Heroic story of raising up the people to retake their land and lives from the Realm occupiers...but to the average people among the dynastic families living there, you're a Villainous monster out to destroy their way of life!<br /> <br /> As for why the First Age started out a genuine Utopia, I suspect that a lot of that had to do with the fact that the early Solars were still taking moral instruction directly from TUS and his entourage, esp the Golden Lord and Nysela, and only later stopped consulting them and doing whatever they wanted. Some text on the Heirophant also indicates that he really did receive answers to his prayers to the Most High, before he insulted him by taking his name in vain...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T09:10:09-07:00","id":88219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88034#post88034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> David's Exaltation narrative is where a prophet goes to his father's house, finds all of his brothers wanting, and then has his father call him in from the fields where God tells the prophet &quot;this is the one, anoint him&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bah. David's Exaltation happens when he volunteers to duel a god-blooded champion and takes him down with a single headshot. Samuel is a Gold Faction Sidereal who foresaw the Exaltation and took steps to ensure it came to pass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1369-mewtarthio","name":"Mewtarthio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T10:21:14-07:00","id":88270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88192#post88192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for why the First Age started out a genuine Utopia(...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Did it, though? I know it's what 2e strongly implied, but is this actually necessary or beneficial to the established narrative of Creation?<br /> <br /> When Greeks spoke of the age of legends, they meant the time when supernatural wars ravaged the earth, heroes battled horrible monsters and gods were dicking around with humanity.<br /> <br /> It's necessary that the First Age was greater than the Age of Sorrows, but it's not necessary for it to be qualitatively better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T10:38:16-07:00","id":88280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mewtarthio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88219#post88219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bah. David's Exaltation happens when he volunteers to duel a god-blooded champion and takes him down with a single headshot. Samuel is a Gold Faction Sidereal who foresaw the Exaltation and took steps to ensure it came to pass.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that's what you get when you miss the point of the post you're quoting.<br /> <br /> When he went to fight Goliath, David was already a mighty hero. He wasn't a plucky farmboy going up against someone stronger than him and winning against all odds; he was a master slingsman, who had killed lions and bears, both with a sling and <i>barehanded</i>, and who had already been chosen by God long before that battle.<br /> <br /> When everyone fears Goliath, he steps forward confidently, engages him on highly favorable terms (ranged skirmisher, starting with a distance, against a melee fighter), and wins. But he was already Exalted long before this, when God literally picked him in his field and sent him at the court of the king.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T11:18:46-07:00","id":88314,"title":"","content":"It might be interesting to see this thread cease to move in circles.<br /> <br /> Such a thing could reasonably happen if everyone agreed on a common definition of &quot;hero&quot;.<br /> <br /> I propose choosing the definition that is actually relevant in the context of Exalted, the ancient Greek one - where heroes aren't heroes because they're lawful good, but because they do great things - without any sort of moral component.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T11:32:42-07:00","id":88320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88190#post88190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think 3rd edition is going for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might not be the World of Darkness specifically, but the framing device of a mythic prehistory is still there; it's even in the Kickstarter summary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T11:34:51-07:00","id":88321,"title":"","content":"I think it might be worthwhile to talk about what &quot;Hero&quot; means in a classical context. In Ancient Greece, &quot;heros&quot; originally referred to warriors and protectors, then later came to refer to demi-gods; In Latin, it referred to demi-gods and men of renown. In Plato's Republic, the Guardians (though closer to the DBs, as written) are a class of individuals who forsake any hope of an ordinary life or any claims to worldly property in order to protect and govern a society so that it flourishes. This touches on what I think is an important point for Solars: As a baseline, Solars are chosen from people willing to live outside of established patterns for the sake of something greater. So, I think any Solar content to live an unexceptional life is unlikely. <br /> <br /> More important than etymology are probably examples: Hercules was not particularly interested in making the world a better place. He was interested in atoning for his personal sins due to his tragic flaw (Wrath) and spent twelve years in service of a mortal king, refusing payment for all of his tasks. In doing these tasks, he sometimes saves countless lives, but was sometimes simply asked to steal an artifact for a King who wasn't particularly deserving. He was a hero because he was amazingly good at what he did and he held fast to his ideals, even if we or Aristotle might accuse him of a lack of critical thinking. Most Greek heroes follow the same template: Odysseus, Achilles, Theseus, Perseus, Jason: They often do individual things that might not fit with our 21st-century morality, but they are amazing at what they do and, while they may not have the same morality we do, they exhibit <i>moral courage:</i> being willing to risk their lives for what they believe is important. That may be family, the kingship, defeat of an ancient enemy, sworn brotherhood.<br /> <br /> In another part of the classical world, thousands and thousands and thousands of people are killed because Liu Bei refuses to give up his quest for the throne. He is a great ruler once he acquires the throne, but he reigns for only two years before being killed, and the Shu kingdom afterwards only lasts a few decades. One could easily argue it wasn't even worth it. That said, Liu Bei would still be a hero in the classical sense because he was extremely able and totally committed to his dream of ruling with the help of his sworn brothers. <br /> <br /> Gaius Julius Caesar might even be the best example to illustrate the contrast. He was a consummate imperialist who spent most of his career crushing foreign powers into dust, looting the remains, and taking whoever was still alive as slaves for Rome. He becomes unbelievably powerful through doing this and uses his loyal soldiers to end the rule of the aristocratic families <i>forever, </i>concentrating all power in his own person, the eternal dictator. Yet, he brought great prosperity to the common people of his society, made extremely useful reforms, and prevented anyone from disrupting the stability of this new Roman society. Even though he was murdered by a conspiracy of detractors, those defending his legacy proved far more powerful than those who opposed it, and the name Caesar of Rome was so influential that it continued to be adopted by rulers all over the world: The Sultan of Rum, Tsar, Kaiser. <br /> <br /> tl;dr: Gaius Julius Caesar, one of the most iconic historical examples of Solars, was a <b>gaping fascist asshole</b> by 21st century standards, but he was a hero revered above virtually all others by the standards of his ancient culture. He exemplified the Roman ideals of personal competence and service to the state, with the ideal of the best possible state winning out over the will of the actual rulers he was supposed to answer to. <br /> <br /> Ultimately, I think Solars have amazing potential for good, but I think they are destined to be <i>great</i> rather than good or evil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1595-scatters-the-ashes","name":"Scatters-the-Ashes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1595_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T12:02:14-07:00","id":88337,"title":"","content":"Exaltation does not and absolutely should not come with any moral incentives at all. Yes, I am including Abyssals and Infernals in that.<br /> <br /> The passions and desires of Solars shake the world, but they are no more inherently ethical than the rest of us.<br /> <br /> I feel that this is the best way to run things by far. A Solar can just as easily be a nightmare as a saint. Because being a Solar makes you glorious and powerful, and nothing more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T13:06:27-07:00","id":88382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes#post87146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the sense that they are good people performing good deeds in order to make the world a better place.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree 100% with your post. the above quote is pretty much what drew me to Exalted when I first read 1st ED. (Well, not the quote itself, but what it describes.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1441-ersatz","name":"Ersatz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T13:37:15-07:00","id":88395,"title":"","content":"I don't think all solars should be heroes. <br /> <br /> As a general rule, any generalization reduces the depth of the characters, the richness of the setting and the expierence of gameplay.<br /> <br /> If every solar is a hero, the options a player have at character creation are reduced, and you automatically know that every solar you meet is one of the good guys. <br /> <br /> Anything that allow you to automatically distinguish good from evil makes a setting more bland and uninteresting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2245-quimeradc","name":"Quimeradc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T14:19:02-07:00","id":88408,"title":"","content":"Really Solars are heroes like the characters from Watchmen are Heroes.<br /> <br /> That is to say, they explore the various different elements and ideas of what Heroes are. The Hero as the Ubermensch (Ozymandias), the Hero as the God (Dr Manhattan), the Hero as the Everyman (Nite Owl), the Hero as the Legacy (Silk Spectre) and so on. Solars explore what those different various versions of heroism just like Moore's work does. Your Solar does not have to be so archetypical as those characters, but they probably do explore what it means to be Heroic in some way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T16:18:30-07:00","id":88487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88034#post88034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">David's Exaltation narrative is where a prophet goes to his father's house, finds all of his brothers wanting, and then has his father call him in from the fields where God tells the prophet &quot;this is the one, anoint him&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>David's is, sure. This does not make &quot;get me a hundred foreskins oh you got two hundred?&quot; any less of a worthy Exaltation story, nor does the fact that it's... excessive, and cruel.<br /> <br /> I mean, a hundred people <i>died</i> just so that David could get married, and then he killed another hundred for no other reason than &quot;God was with [him].&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T17:04:39-07:00","id":88505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88487#post88487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">David's is, sure. This does not make &quot;get me a hundred foreskins oh you got two hundred?&quot; any less of a worthy Exaltation story, nor does the fact that it's... excessive, and cruel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh yes, yes, sorry.<br /> <br /> It's always a tricky thing when considering whether the Exaltation comes before (and enables) or after the audacity is completed, but still.<br /> <br /> In this framing, I'd say that's still the kind of thing that the Unconquered Sun looks on as &quot;this is a good candidate for fighting the enemies of the world&quot;, and doing it against cultural enemies and/or romance prospects might enhance that sense; that here's a Solar with something worth fighting for, even if that thing might be a bit horrible.<br /> <br /> Part of the <i>Nobunagun</i> reference was me thinking that there'll be at least some Solars with the demeanor of supervillains with a perspective of &quot;the world is where I keep all my stuff&quot;, except where we drop cheesy comic book moralizing or politics (the kind of thing where Lex Luthor and Superman might work together against some alien villain, but they're both really vocal about not wanting to do it).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T17:17:04-07:00","id":88514,"title":"","content":"The Unconquered Sun might just be impressed by the brutal dedication and skill required to kill two hundred men by yourself, when only half that was required. It doesn't have to be for a great purpose, I think, thought Solar Exaltation can be that. It can also be, however, in salute to the act itself. And the act itself can be horrible, as long as it's glorious and impressive. The Unconquered Sun can be virtuous, but the Unconquered Sun can also be merciless and terrible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T19:04:01-07:00","id":88563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=87365#post87365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;<b>(all of whom view themselves as righteous and making the world a better place)</b>&quot;<br /> <br /> You and I are on the same page.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok.... you know that applies to virtually anyone in position of power. Almost no one outside of complete psychopaths thinks of themselves as a villain. If your definition of &quot;Good&quot; includes Stalin and Hitler - than fine, all Solars are generally &quot;good&quot;. The word is now completely meaningless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T21:33:10-07:00","id":88636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88563#post88563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok.... you know that applies to virtually anyone in position of power. Almost no one outside of complete psychopaths thinks of themselves as a villain. If your definition of &quot;Good&quot; includes Stalin and Hitler - than fine, all Solars are generally &quot;good&quot;. The word is now completely meaningless.</div> </div> </div> </div>This comes up over and over again. You and almost everyone who disagrees with my stance are under this impression that either &quot;good&quot; means &quot;morally palatable to 21st century mainstream Western sensibilities&quot; or it means nothing at all. In almost every post I've made in this thread, <i>including the one you quoted</i>, I've tried to explain that I see &quot;good&quot; as pertains to this discussion as a really broad, flexible concept.<br /> <br /> Saying that good is subjective doesn't make it meaningless, because a great and skilled person can be a person who doesn't subscribe to any notion of good at all. You don't have to think of yourself as a villain to be looking out first and foremost for yourself. Think of every person you know. How many of those people are just trying to get by, or succeed, or leave a legacy for their family? How many are motivated by a desire to change the world, and show that motivation through their actions? In my experience, the latter group is rare indeed.<br /> <br /> Yes, my conception of the Unconquered Sun and the &quot;goodness&quot; he sees in people is that he would totally have made Stalin and Hitler Solars because of their &quot;goodness&quot;. He's unable to weigh good against its opportunity cost, so when he looks into their heads and sees that they want to lead their people to world prominence, he cannot fathom that this means they are going to kill millions of people in the process. He just sees a reflection of his own all-encompassing good and goes &quot;yep, there's a worthy Solar&quot;.<br /> <br /> If Solars are myth-heroes, then the interesting thing about their stories is the roll of magical monstrosities that they face and overcome. The story of Odysseus would have been pretty boring if Poseidon hadn't been toying with him for 10 years. Beowulf has no character traits besides the fact that he kills monsters. If your character needs to be subjected to adversity in order to be interesting, is your character actually interesting? I think that kind of character is just a foil.<br /> <br /> Steve Irwin knew this. He made himself a myth-hero in order to show people the wonders of the natural world, because it's the essence of a myth-hero to be the proxy by which an audience learns about mythos. His shows were <i>about nature</i>, not about him, just the same as the Odyssey was <i>about mythical creatures</i>, rather than about Odysseus. It is the job of a myth-hero to triumph over the supernatural dangers they face, but this doesn't make them any more dramatically interesting unto themselves than an unplugged television. And if there's one constant theme you see in White Wolf games, one setting element that overrides anything else you can say about their games, it's that your character is supposed to be dramatically interesting. That's why I think Solars Are Good: because introducing that thematic constant makes Solars interesting, where otherwise they would be the most boring beings in the setting. Myth-heroes have stories where stuff happens to them. Good guys have stories where they make stuff happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2404-chant","name":"Chant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2404_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T21:53:19-07:00","id":88656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88636#post88636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, my conception of the Unconquered Sun and the &quot;goodness&quot; he sees in people is that he would totally have made Stalin and Hitler Solars because of their &quot;goodness&quot;. <b>He's unable to weigh good against its opportunity cost, so when he looks into their heads and sees that they want to lead their people to world prominence, he cannot fathom that this means they are going to kill millions of people in the process</b>. He just sees a reflection of his own all-encompassing good and goes &quot;yep, there's a worthy Solar&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>May I ask why he would be that dumb?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T21:58:52-07:00","id":88659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88656#post88656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">May I ask why he would be that dumb?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because he is a god, and &quot;gods are narrow-minded&quot; is attested to at length in the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2404-chant","name":"Chant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2404_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T22:36:32-07:00","id":88673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88505#post88505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of the Nobunagun reference was me thinking that there'll be at least some Solars with the demeanor of supervillains with a perspective of &quot;the world is where I keep all my stuff&quot;, except where we drop cheesy comic book moralizing or politics (the kind of thing where Lex Luthor and Superman might work together against some alien villain, but they're both really vocal about not wanting to do it).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is pretty close to how I feel. I don't think a potential Solar has to be a good person like superman, but the should have intentions to do great things. Take Lex Luthor, he's solar material, he genuinely wants the world to be a better and he has the mind to do it, he's just too much of a narcissist to believe that anybody but him could lead the world to a better future. He's by no means good but not outright bad either. The Joker on the other hand is a different story, give him Solar powers and drop him in the Imperial City and certainly he could end the despotic rule of the Great Houses and the Immaculate Order a great feat indeed, but he would only be doing it because he thinks its funny to sow chaos.<br /> <br /> I guess the criteria I would use for choosing a solar is this, they must be capable of doing great things and they can have selfish motivations for doing great things, but part of their motivation should also be altruistic. If a solar aspires to rule nations, tear down empires, and dictate laws across creation, as only their person can be trusted to do, they should also want to make creation a better place and believe they can do it.<br /> <br /> Now to mix comic book metaphors, a thought just came to mind, &quot;with great power comes great responsibility&quot; and a Solar exaltation shouldn't be given to someone who can understand this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T22:54:23-07:00","id":88681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88673#post88673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think a potential Solar has to be a good person like superman, but the should have intentions to do great things. Take Lex Luthor, he's solar material, he genuinely wants the world to be a better and he has the mind to do it, he's just too much of a narcissist to believe that anybody but him could lead the world to a better future. He's by no means good but not outright bad either. The Joker on the other hand is a different story, give him Solar powers and drop him in the Imperial City and certainly he could end the despotic rule of the Great Houses and the Immaculate Order a great feat indeed, but he would only be doing it because he thinks its funny to sow chaos.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree: Lex Luthor is Solar material. I think he's a perfect example to express what I'm trying to say about Solars. He easily fits the working definition of &quot;good&quot; that I've devised elsewhere in this thread, which is simply &quot;intent and drive to bring about the world one thinks is best&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2404-chant","name":"Chant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2404_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T01:01:52-07:00","id":88706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88673#post88673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is pretty close to how I feel. I don't think a potential Solar has to be a good person like superman, but the should have intentions to do great things. Take Lex Luthor, he's solar material, he genuinely wants the world to be a better and he has the mind to do it, he's just too much of a narcissist to believe that anybody but him could lead the world to a better future. He's by no means good but not outright bad either.</div> </div> </div> </div>No he doesn't. That's the thing about Luthor. He <i>says </i>it's about improving the world. It <i>isn't</i>. It's just about himself, all about himself. If there had <i>been </i>no Superman, Luthor wouldn't have been a messiah, just a boot. He's in extreme denial, and most of the times he's gotten rid of Superman for any length of time he's completely failed to improve the world in any meaningful way in that time, despite having plenty of brainpower and resources to effect some real change within the year or so he usually gets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T01:21:11-07:00","id":88710,"title":"","content":"Lex Luthor would make a great Infernal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T01:41:45-07:00","id":88715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88636#post88636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Steve Irwin knew this. He made himself a myth-hero in order to show people the wonders of the natural world, because it's the essence of a myth-hero to be the proxy by which an audience learns about mythos. His shows were <i>about nature</i>, not about him, just the same as the Odyssey was <i>about mythical creatures</i>, rather than about Odysseus. It is the job of a myth-hero to triumph over the supernatural dangers they face, but this doesn't make them any more dramatically interesting unto themselves than an unplugged television. And if there's one constant theme you see in White Wolf games, one setting element that overrides anything else you can say about their games, it's that your character is supposed to be dramatically interesting. That's why I think Solars Are Good: because introducing that thematic constant makes Solars interesting, where otherwise they would be the most boring beings in the setting. Myth-heroes have stories where stuff happens to them. Good guys have stories where they make stuff happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's why they're also the heroes from pulp, political intrigue, history and epic tragedy. Because Beowulf (the myth hero) does not have a very compelling character and different shades of &quot;good&quot; heroes all in competition with one another is narrow and limited and generally not on focus with the setting.<br /> <br /> In hatewheel's full quote, the context is that myth heroes is what the Solars are contra the other Exalted splats who subvert and assimilate magic to making it work to human desires and goals (even it's only the Exalt's desires and goals) - Solars conquer and dominate the magical with human skill. It isn't the entire of their character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T02:08:31-07:00","id":88723,"title":"","content":"The context of Hatewheel's quote is a thread for people new to Exalted to a poster who didn't know anything about the game. I doubt it was meant to inform the reader of the Solar's relation to other Exalted as the intended reader might not even know there are other Exalted.<br /> <br /> 'You are a hero who's been chosen by the mightiest of gods to bring the world back from the brink of death,' positions the Solar Exalted as divinely appointed <i>good guys</i> and <i>saviors</i>. 'You've returned from death to become a mighty hero' does not at all suggest that you'll be taking slaves, committing genocide, or gathering 200 foreskins for your wife.<br /> <br /> This is not ambiguous language. If he didn't want people new to the game to think of Solars as heroes in the popular, modern sense, he wouldn't be using that word.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T02:27:39-07:00","id":88729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88710#post88710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lex Luthor would make a great Infernal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Outside of the Exalted Modern shard with it's specific conceits concerning Infernals, I have an extremely hard time envisioning Luther as an Infernal. A DB perhaps, Mnemon is very much Lex Luther(which is to say she hits a lot of the same super-villian notes) sans a specific Solar 'Superman' antagonist. (Modern DC) Lex, despite his ambitions, very much represents the establishment, much in the same way Mnemon does for the Realm. You could easily create a more specifically Lex Luther based Realmie DB if you wanted as well.<br /> Lex also contrasts Superman's inborn alien super powers with his own pinacle of human skill, making him rather Solar-ish.<br /> <br /> Infernal doesn't make sense, he's never behold or connected to some other worldy alien power, infact he usually specifically is not, contrasting Superman who is. I guess he doesn't fail, except in competition against Superman (at which point he's already at his height).... Just... not seeing it, power, flavour, theme, place in the setting...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/726-amine-hsu","name":"Amine Hsu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar726_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T02:34:14-07:00","id":88731,"title":"","content":"hippokrene - see here - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/78589-kickstarter-update-57-at-long-last/page10\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...ng-last/page10</a> at the bottom of the page for the quote I'm responding to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> John Morke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars, Lunars, and Sidereals occupy entirely different game-space in Exalted. Solars are myth-heroes. It is a myth-hero's purpose to subvert mythos and thereby define it. Solars fight, destroy, and ultimately recreate the status-quo, doing so by conquering the obliquely magical through acts of sheer will, force, and skill writ-large, like every myth-hero in literature.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is saying that Solars and myth-heroes where the Lunars and Sidereals aren't. Chant seemed to me to be running with a bit of an inadvertent straw man that this was all they were, which ignores all the other layers in the thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is not ambiguous language. If he didn't want people new to the game to think of Solars as heroes in the popular, modern sense, he wouldn't be using that word.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYeah, he might want to think about using that language (for reasons in the rest of this thread). The actual setting seems mainly about adding White Wolf style typical realistic worlds and people with strange pulp fantasy, which doesn't play so well with simple splats of good guys, so it would make sense to sell people on that first and foremost, rather than confuse them if they're not expecting that at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T02:45:01-07:00","id":88734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88723#post88723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The context of Hatewheel's quote is a thread for people new to Exalted to a poster who didn't know anything about the game. I doubt it was meant to inform the reader of the Solar's relation to other Exalted as the intended reader might not even know there are other Exalted.<br /> <br /> 'You are a hero who's been chosen by the mightiest of gods to bring the world back from the brink of death,' positions the Solar Exalted as divinely appointed <i>good guys</i> and <i>saviors</i>. 'You've returned from death to become a mighty hero' does not at all suggest that you'll be taking slaves, committing genocide, or gathering 200 foreskins for your wife.<br /> <br /> This is not ambiguous language. If he didn't want people new to the game to think of Solars as heroes in the popular, modern sense, he wouldn't be using that word.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, poor choice of words there on his part. He should make it clear exaltation is divided from morality, but determined by the gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T03:20:37-07:00","id":88746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88731#post88731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hippokrene - see here - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/78589-kickstarter-update-57-at-long-last/page10\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...ng-last/page10</a> at the bottom of the page for the quote I'm responding to.<br /> <br /> This is saying that Solars and myth-heroes where the Lunars and Sidereals aren't. Chant seemed to me to be running with a bit of an inadvertent straw man that this was all they were, which ignores all the other layers in the thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thoroughly misread what you meant. Yes, I see what you mean now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T03:25:05-07:00","id":88752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88723#post88723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'You are a hero who's been chosen by the mightiest of gods to bring the world back from the brink of death,' positions the Solar Exalted as divinely appointed <i>good guys</i> and <i>saviors</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what I mean when I say that the assumption that the inclination or capability to save the world means that you're obviously a good person <u>is an example of simple comic book morality</u>.<br /> <br /> (Jesus, what is it with me and forgetting to finish my sentences?)<br /> <br /> It would be an odd duck who did <i>not</i> want to save the world; it's where all their stuff is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">'You've returned from death to become a mighty hero' does not at all suggest that you'll be taking slaves, committing genocide, or gathering 200 foreskins for your wife.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are none of those things demonstrations of might?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 03-11-2014, 08:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T03:44:27-07:00","id":88755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88752#post88752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is what I mean when I say that the assumption that the inclination or capability to save the world means that you're obviously a good person.<br /> <br /> It would be an odd duck who did <i>not</i> want to save the world; it's where all their stuff is.<br /> <br /> --quote snip--<br /> <br /> Are none of those things demonstrations of might?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are not things one associates with being a hero.<br /> <br /> Yes, you can say 'but the Greek and Biblical ideal of heroism' but we're not Greeks or Biblical era Jews. When John says that Solars are mighty heroes to someone who has never played the game, I believe he's aware that they're going to use a modern concept of heroism.<br /> <br /> If he wanted people to see Solars as the amoral assholes of legend, he wouldn't be calling them heroes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88734#post88734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, poor choice of words there on his part. He should make it clear exaltation is divided from morality, but determined by the gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to try to dig up a quote where hatewheel talks how he thinks Solars should be positioned in people's minds. It's a couple years old though so wish me luck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 03-11-2014, 06:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T04:04:50-07:00","id":88756,"title":"","content":"As far as I'm concerned, Lea conclusively settled this issue in this post from 2013 on RPGnet. I agree 100% with what he says:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The heroism/villainy thing for Solars is deliberate but often badly handled; it's also a demonstration of fanon getting out of hand.<br /> <br /> By default, the straight read of Exalted is that the Solars are the reincarnated heroes of out of the past sent back to a time of woe to make right what's wrong. They're virtuous and powerful and shine with the light of the sun, and they'll confront the suffering of the world.<br /> <br /> That's deliberate. You are supposed to be able to take that as the straight read of the game and go wild, in a manner similar to, say, someone taking Werewolf and running it as &quot;You are eco-crusaders; go kill fomori and blow up Pentex buildings.&quot;<br /> <br /> There's a subtext. The subtext is not something I can concisely describe but it's made up of statements like &quot;What does heroism mean anyway?&quot; and &quot;Wait, virtue doesn't seem to equate with goodness <i>per se</i> here....&quot; and &quot;Are you sure unbound power and no accountability is going to lead to the triumph of a righteousness we want?&quot; The question of whether the Solars will save the world or destroy it is meant to loom in the distance, and as originally conceived, the setting is a tragedy -- great heroism and glory doesn't make an eternal utopia; they just lead to stories worth telling millennia later after the age of heroism and glory has passed and the flame of magic has extinguished itself, leading to the world we know today.<br /> <br /> That subtext is necessary. It needs to be present, <i>and it needs to be subtext</i>.<br /> <br /> There's two ways to go wrong here. One is to get rid of it entirely, as Kaiju Keichi constantly advocates. The other way -- and this is what 2e did, and what a lot of fans who think they're clever advocate -- is to make it text. This is bad. Bad bad bad. Do not do this. Do not decide that you've uncovered the secret truth of Exalted and proclaim it to the world: &quot;Heroism's promise is a trick! Glory is a lie! The Solars are actually villains!&quot; No. No no no.<br /> <br /> That subtext needs to be visible on the horizon; it needs to be present enough to prey on the mind, but the <i>text</i> needs to remain &quot;The Solars are the awesome glorious heroes of yore brought back to bring righteousness and virtue to an age of sorrows.&quot; When you take the subtext and make it the truth of the setting, you have stopped serving a well-spiced meal and started serving a plate heaped with spice and no actual food.<br /> <br /> Keeping this balance is really fucking hard to do over the course of years and years of supplements. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2082-schleiermacher","name":"Schleiermacher","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T04:17:15-07:00","id":88759,"title":"","content":"I think the human soul craves beauty and nobility. People will share a story of a boy wading into the raging waters of a river to save a baby deer hundreds of thousands of times, not because they're sentimental sheep, but because we know quite well that humans can be selfish, cruel, and ugly, and we need examples of the opposite. If you want to make a game that's full of humanity at its worst, don't introduce it by pissing on the brightest light the setting offers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 03-11-2014, 07:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T05:09:05-07:00","id":88777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88755#post88755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are not things one associates with being a hero.</div> </div> </div> </div>You realise that Genghis Khan and Vlad Tepes are virtually worshiped in their respective countries, right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When John says that Solars are mighty heroes to someone who has never played the game, I believe he's aware that they're going to use a modern concept of heroism.</div> </div> </div> </div>And those people are free to play Solar who are (or can be viewed by themselves and others as) good people with good intentions because nothing about Solars <i>excludes</i> those things.<br /> <br /> It is just not exclusive <i>to</i> them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If he wanted people to see Solars as the amoral assholes of legend, he wouldn't be calling them heroes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Has anybody ever been outright confused at somebody like Achilles being called a hero?<br /> <br /> Regardless, the understanding that heroism does not necessarily convey moral insight should be a subtextual point just to maintain the game's motifs.<br /> <br /> Hence the idea that, if Genghis Khan was a Solar, we'd introduce him from the perspective of the Mongols. You don't necessarily hone in on the viewpoint of everybody between China and Egypt, but you also make it clear that the Mongols are kind of pushing through that length, prompting you to consider what exactly is going on there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to make a game that's full of humanity at its worst, don't introduce it by pissing on the brightest light the setting offers.</div> </div> </div> </div>The existence of morally dubious Solars in no way diminishes any other kind of Solar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T05:17:07-07:00","id":88778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Schleiermacher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88756#post88756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I'm concerned, Lea conclusively settled this issue in this post from 2013 on RPGnet. I agree 100% with what he says:</div> </div> </div> </div>I would generally agree with that too.<br /> As I said at the beginning, Grabowski created a deconstruction of heroism (in the modern sense): a lot of Solars are not good people, but as a splat they <i>look</i> like the good guys. They're the one once and future kings, they have the divine right to rule (but wait, why is monarchy a good thing? Does being chosen by God really make them the good guys? Is this God even that good?). They're fighting an evil and corrupt empire of super-powered aristocrats (but wait, are they morally better? How do we know they won't just make their own empire ruled by super-powered aristocrats?). They literally shine (but wait, does looking like the good guys really make them the good guys?).<br /> And I've no particular problem with that. It's not a deconstruction if there's nothing to deconstruct.<br /> I just have a problem with the setting saying &quot;yes, they definitely are the good guys, they definitely were chosen for being good&quot;, etc, it robs it of all nuance. It restricts the characters you can conceivably make as both a player and ST. It doesn't pose questions. And the questions Exalted poses about morality are one of the reasons it stands above more simplistic fantasy games like Dungeons and Dragons. You have to think about morality, not just go &quot;yep, Solars are the good guys, done.&quot; I don't want that taken away.<br /> <br /> I should say though, that while Stephen says that, he's not lead developer. John Morke is lead developer. And while I adamantly believe that Solars should not be good guys (at least, no more than they should be bad guys), and that it would detract from the quality of the game, I'm not the one who'll decide. That's John. Perhaps Hippokrene is right, that he is saying that Solars are heroes in the modern sense. And if that's so, well he's lead developer so there it is. As much as I might think it's a bad decision, it's his decision.<br /> <br /> However, I would say that him saying on a thread for new players that Solars are heroes chosen to save the world, doesn't necessarily mean they are heroes in the modern sense.<br /> Firstly, because this is a simple thread for new players, and it's quite okay to say &quot;Solars are heroes chosen to save the world&quot; and then explain later that it's more nuanced than that.<br /> Secondly, because the examples he's previously given of the sort of heroes who he wants to evoke with Solars, are not necessarily heroes in the modern sense.<br /> But hey, maybe I'm wrong. We can't really tell until the new edition is out. I suspect that what we're likely to see is what Stephenis said though.<br /> On the surface, they appear to be heroes. Dig deeper, and it's not so clear-cut.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T05:27:39-07:00","id":88784,"title":"","content":"One of my favourite examples of the subtext of Solars is the excellent fluff on some of the 2nd ed Solar charms.<br /> &quot;It is the lawgivers' right to confiscate goods necessary to the service of the Unconquered Sun&quot; (Flawless Pickpocketing Technique)<br /> &quot;Only the unrighteous would lock a door to keep the lawgivers out. Such an intention is proof of iniquity&quot; (Door-Evading Technique)<br /> You oppose the Solars? You must be evil! It's okay to steal your stuff, because I'm a Solar, and Solars are good, so it must be okay to steal your stuff!<br /> Trying to stop me stealing your stuff proves that you're evil so it's okay to steal your stuff...<br /> <br /> So yeah, subtext.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T05:31:34-07:00","id":88788,"title":"","content":"I do not live in Mongolia or Romania. I'm going to guess that the stories they tell about these figures aren't exactly the stories we tell about them. Especially as most of the stories I've heard about Vlad the Impaler involve him making a deal with the devil and turning into a vampire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88777#post88777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And those people are free to play Solar who are (or can be viewed by themselves and others as) good people with good intentions because nothing about Solars <i>excludes</i> those things.<br /> <br /> It is just not exclusive <i>to</i> them.<br /> <br /> <br /> Regardless, the understanding that heroism does not necessarily convey moral insight should be a subtextual point just to maintain the game's motifs.<br /> <br /> Hence the idea that, if Genghis Khan was a Solar, we'd introduce him from the perspective of the Mongols. You don't necessarily hone in on the viewpoint of everybody between China and Egypt, but you also make it clear that the Mongols are kind of pushing through that length, prompting you to consider what exactly is going on there.<br /> <br /> The existence of morally dubious Solars in no way diminishes any other kind of Solar.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have said several times that I am fine with morally dubious Solars. I explicitly said that there will be exceptions to 'Solars are heroes' and non-heroic PCs were just as good as heroic ones in <i>the original post. </i><br /> <br /> But the default? The center? Solars are heroes. Noble, inspiring, and good.<br /> <br /> Subtext is the edge. I expect players to explore it. It gives the PCs and the setting depth, but I am devoted to 'Solars are heroes' as the surface.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T05:34:50-07:00","id":88790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88673#post88673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is pretty close to how I feel. I don't think a potential Solar has to be a good person like superman, but the should have intentions to do great things. Take Lex Luthor, he's solar material, he genuinely wants the world to be a better and he has the mind to do it, he's just too much of a narcissist to believe that anybody but him could lead the world to a better future. He's by no means good but not outright bad either. The Joker on the other hand is a different story, give him Solar powers and drop him in the Imperial City and certainly he could end the despotic rule of the Great Houses and the Immaculate Order a great feat indeed, but he would only be doing it because he thinks its funny to sow chaos.<br /> <br /> I guess the criteria I would use for choosing a solar is this, they must be capable of doing great things and they can have selfish motivations for doing great things, but part of their motivation should also be altruistic. If a solar aspires to rule nations, tear down empires, and dictate laws across creation, as only their person can be trusted to do, they should also want to make creation a better place and believe they can do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I vehemently reject this criterion. The very idea that Solar Exaltation <i>inherently requires altruism</i> goes against the setting as sold us for over a decade. And it creates an issue where you note that &quot;Solars are the only ones to be trusted with the power&quot;, which is not what hte game is about. The Solar Exalted should not have a &quot;divine right to rule&quot; actually built in the idea that by the nature of their having power, they're the guys who are guaranteed to be the &quot;least bad guy&quot; about using it.<br /> <br /> It also, again, contradicts source material. Sinbad, Achilles, and Conan didn't go about doing stuff because of altruism. Things they did that was altruistic often was a side-effect of other things. Conan didn't become king because he thought he'd be better for the people. He became king becaue the king pissed him off and he was the one who could hold the seat. That he was better at it than others and popular for not being a bad king is not linked with what got him there, which was more or less total self-interest. <br /> <br /> And as I have argued already in this thread, by making Solars intrinsically good, it makes any oppositon to Solar rule who don't have such a trait (namely, other Exalts) intrinsically working agains thte good. By Solar Exalted being the altruistic or the &quot;Right ones for the job inherently&quot;, you make it out like 2e did in a way: No one else should have the job and are actively harming Creation by ruling it in Solar's stead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88673#post88673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now to mix comic book metaphors, a thought just came to mind, &quot;with great power comes great responsibility&quot; and a Solar exaltation shouldn't be given to someone who can understand this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bullshit. Some of the more interesting stories are going to be when someone who probably shouldn't have the power in hindsight got it. Elst no Solar will fall into tyranny (they should know better) and the Usurpation apparently was only an over-reaction to the Solars who were apparently by and large the exceptions, not the rule.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T05:38:45-07:00","id":88791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88755#post88755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are not things one associates with being a hero.<br /> <br /> Yes, you can say 'but the Greek and Biblical ideal of heroism' but we're not Greeks or Biblical era Jews. When John says that Solars are mighty heroes to someone who has never played the game, I believe he's aware that they're going to use a modern concept of heroism.<br /> <br /> If he wanted people to see Solars as the amoral assholes of legend, he wouldn't be calling them heroes.</div> </div> </div> </div>John isn't doing anything new here. All editions of Exalted have consistently called the Exalted in general and Solars in particular for heroes but not any kind of hero, specifically the type of hero from epics and pulp fiction. Second Edition in its eagerness to overexplain everything in the setting had a sidebar explicitly calling out that the Exaltation doesn't care about morality while First Edition had a more 'show not tell' approach by having a bandit lord as example character concept and 'Conniver, Critic and Hedonist' among the Natures you could pick while explaining in the storytelling chapter that heroes should be flawed and the virtue flaw mechanic is supposed to help represent that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T05:39:20-07:00","id":88792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88723#post88723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...<br /> 'You are a hero who's been chosen by the mightiest of gods to bring the world back from the brink of death,' positions the Solar Exalted as divinely appointed <i>good guys</i> and <i>saviors</i>. 'You've returned from death to become a mighty hero' does not at all suggest that you'll be taking slaves, committing genocide, or gathering 200 foreskins for your wife.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on how well versed you are in the term &quot;hero&quot;. Part of the goal of the thread is help get an idea of how to word the pitch. The term hero here is probably not well-applied due to the fact that Exalted has not used hero in the modern sense since ever. So the use of it here free of contextualization is going ot lead to misleading I would say.<br /> <br /> And hate to say it to you, but with one of the sources of Exalted being the Bible, it very much <i>does</i> mean collection 200 foreskins for your wife, genocide, and enslavement. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88723#post88723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is not ambiguous language. If he didn't want people new to the game to think of Solars as heroes in the popular, modern sense, he wouldn't be using that word.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which means he chose the inappropriate word. And as this thread kind of shows based on your insistance on things and not a lot of folks agreeing with the term, the word her <i>is</i> ambiguous.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T05:47:11-07:00","id":88796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88755#post88755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are not things one associates with being a hero.</div> </div> </div> </div>For modern western culture maybe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88755#post88755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, you can say 'but the Greek and Biblical ideal of heroism' but we're not Greeks or Biblical era Jews. When John says that Solars are mighty heroes to someone who has never played the game, I believe he's aware that they're going to use a modern concept of heroism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you going to base your argument on a single quote, in a sales pitch environment, in a thread meant ot vet said quotes to make sure they don't lead to possible misunderstandings (such as Exaltation having moral qualities to it due to ambiguous terms) as the basis of your argument?<br /> <br /> Because that's a form of quote-mine if it is. The quote is a bad one. It mischaracterizes Exalted heroes in a way that isn't congruent with source material (which he cites as things like Dying Earth, Elric, Flat Earth, Greek epics, the Bible, classicla Chinese works, and anime later in the thread). Building your argument on a quote that happens to fit it in a specific context and at the expense of a lot of the rest of Exalted's spilled ink on the topic is not a good way to build your case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88755#post88755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If he wanted people to see Solars as the amoral assholes of legend, he wouldn't be calling them heroes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately for you they are heroes. Just not people you as a 21st Century Western Democratic-Republic Nation State-dwelling person inherently will view as one. And in David's case, he actually thought he was being very moral (as in what was moral was in part do what God says).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88755#post88755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to try to dig up a quote where hatewheel talks how he thinks Solars should be positioned in people's minds. It's a couple years old though so wish me luck.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is hatewheel's specific quotes all that matter, rather than GCG's, SLS's, Holden's, some of hatewheel's others, or the source material of Exalted itself? Because I'm starting to see a case that looks a lot like how some folks go about quoting Darwin on eyeballs.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T05:52:49-07:00","id":88797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88788#post88788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to guess that the stories they tell about these figures aren't exactly the stories we tell about them</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? Why assume that they'd tell stories based on the same cultural values? Why assume that nobody would view somebody leading their unified people out to conquer half the world and mercilessly crush all opposition as something laudable?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> Especially as most of the stories I've heard about Vlad the Impaler involve him making a deal with the devil and turning into a vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Errr, in that case you've not heard a single story about Vlad the Impaler.<br /> <br /> You've probably heard a lot of stories about an appropriated and enduring caricature of him by an ignorant Irish guy, though.<br /> <br /> I gather the stories Romainian people tell about Vlad are the stories where he defended the sovereignty of Romanian (specifically Wallachian) people by massacring large numbers of Turks and Magyars.<br /> <br /> I mean, don't get me wrong, there <i>have</i> been stories that frame the actual Vlad III as a bizarre monster; feasting amidst forests of stakes and all. These are stories that primarily come from people who would be his enemies.<br /> <br /> You see how standards of heroism aren't universal?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have said several times that I am fine with morally dubious Solars. I explicitly said that there will be exceptions to 'Solars are heroes' and non-heroic PCs were just as good as heroic ones in <i>the original post. </i></div> </div> </div> </div>And it's problematic to frame this as exceptional.<br /> <br /> Nor should it be central.<br /> <br /> This is one of those things Holden is talking about when he says that binary thinking is intensely unsatisfying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars are heroes. Noble, inspiring, and good.</div> </div> </div> </div>By whose values?<br /> <br /> You know, another part of it is that, while Exalted doesn't exactly have Always Chaotic Evil nonsense in it, it does still have targets that a Solar Vlad can be pointed at who, being inhuman, people might be inclined to be less concerned over being mercilessly massacred.<br /> <br /> That's not to say that these beings don't have their own depth, nor is it a matter of getting an easy out for playing a morally dubious character by pointing them at something that you don't need to have empathy for...<br /> <br /> Wait, what the hell?! What was all of that criticism about the other work being sanitized in how it presented its characters? In how they got to act as though their empire building was a-okay because it was always either pointed at monsters or never in focus?<br /> <br /> It's bad for some book series to be sanitized, but it's some kind of affront to the human impulse towards beauty and nobility if the Solar Exalted are not?<br /> <br /> A-anyway, yeah, outlet for dubious people pointed at monsters or something...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T05:53:50-07:00","id":88798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88759#post88759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the human soul craves beauty and nobility. People will share a story of a boy wading into the raging waters of a river to save a baby deer hundreds of thousands of times, not because they're sentimental sheep, but because we know quite well that humans can be selfish, cruel, and ugly, and we need examples of the opposite. If you want to make a game that's full of humanity at its worst, don't introduce it by pissing on the brightest light the setting offers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Humanity only at its best, with what it can do at its worst shown as an &quot;exception&quot;, &quot;aberration&quot; or mistake to me shows a fairly naive and simplistic view of things. It also simply shows humanity as caricature, rather than humanity as the diverse, nuanced and complicated thing that it relaly is. People aren't altruistic saints. They aren't malicious assholes. But saying people are by being one incapable of actually ever being the other is being to me denying humanity in its full extant.<br /> <br /> Note folks don't advocate Solars need to be evil bastards. I'm rejecting Solars are inherently comic book good guys. Solars are people. And you judge people on the basis of what a person they chose to be and act. The thing that makes them glow a lot and lets them act on things most people don't get to shoulnd't have a criterion on how it can be used or by whom. It just needs to be such that it is able to be used and that the person who has it will use it. Otherwise the game's tagline (What legends will they tell of your deeds?) in part is meaningless if we know a priori it is &quot;Probably good guy shit.&quot;<br /> <br /> Exalted isn't a game where you are going ot have Supermans and Darkseids. It's a game where you are going to have Conan, Jubei, David and Sinbad. People who are great in the deeds they might do to help some people and awful in what they do that destroy people or themselves.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":353,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","user":"Blaque","date":". 03-11-2014, 01:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T06:03:11-07:00","id":88801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88788#post88788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not live in Mongolia or Romania. I'm going to guess that the stories they tell about these figures aren't exactly the stories we tell about them. Especially as most of the stories I've heard about Vlad the Impaler involve him making a deal with the devil and turning into a vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>So only your perception on who's heroic from your cultural angle matters? Or are you at least acknowledging that the Khan, Vlad and in other notes, Iskander or Caesar, are heroic in their contexts if not our's? Or are we just owning-up to &quot;My world's more important&quot; modenristic view and looking for quotes to support that instead of the body of work that is the setting's baseline?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88755#post88755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have said several times that I am fine with morally dubious Solars. I explicitly said that there will be exceptions to 'Solars are heroes' and non-heroic PCs were just as good as heroic ones in <i>the original post. </i></div> </div> </div> </div>Morality =/= heroicness, which is the reason a lot of your first post has been rejected. Hero =/= good person. This entire thread came about more or less due to rejection of your first proposition: That a hero is a &quot;good person&quot; and Solar Exalted are all heroes by that defintiion by default. But you have yet to demonstrate how you came to this besides this naive view that good people can't or shouldnt' do bad or selfish things. Or that a great person is not prone to do awful things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88755#post88755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the default? The center? Solars are heroes. Noble, inspiring, and good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Noble means even less than good, since nobility itself is a term that is deconstructed in Exalted a lot. See the Dragon-Blooded, the Exalt who are supposed to be an actual played-straight &quot;My lineage gave me power, now what?&quot; group who are also a reuslt of consequences for that. And as we also note in this thread, &quot;the good&quot; is such an ambiguous term as to be practically meaningless in the discussion as a criterion in Creation, as there is no ultimate good to judge things on and so no good to make any worthwhile filter on Exaltation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88755#post88755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Subtext is the edge. I expect players to explore it. It gives the PCs and the setting depth, but I am devoted to 'Solars are heroes' as the surface.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you are reading a shallow reading of Exalted, since a lot of the point of that subtext being there is that Exalted lets you push those assumptions to their limits. ANd it is found that humans being humans, in a world with no accountability on how to use great power, the &quot;heroes reborn&quot; thing is complicated. But at least you've admitted to mostly not being interested in exploring the setting to its finer details. Just don't expect a lot of sympathy from folks who actually like Creation with more depth than mass market comic book morality.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T06:58:09-07:00","id":88821,"title":"","content":"I'm going to go ahead and take a brief break in my lurking, just to give a little reminder.<br /> <br /> Can we all calm down for a moment? It feels like things in this thread are advancing into unpleasant territory. I think it's best to keep the discussion friendly!<br /> <br /> *Goes back to lurking*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T07:45:03-07:00","id":88838,"title":"","content":"We can argue all year about the morals of real life cultural heroes and it will not get us anywhere, but what about the Bull of the North? I don't consider his campaign of conquest particulary heroic.<br /> <br /> How does that particular piece of canon works with the &quot;All solars are heroes&quot; statement?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2245-quimeradc","name":"Quimeradc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T07:57:03-07:00","id":88847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quimeradc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88838#post88838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We can argue all year about the morals of real life cultural heroes and it will not get us anywhere, but what about the Bull of the North? I don't consider his campaign of conquest particulary heroic. How does that particular piece of canon works with the &quot;All solars are heroes&quot; statement?</div> </div> </div> </div> I mean, I think this -is- an example of a cultural hero, right? He's a hero to the Icewalkers, I'm sure. But he's not any more a good or bad person than any other conqueror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/926-yishten","name":"Yishten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar926_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T08:10:54-07:00","id":88850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yishten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88847#post88847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I mean, I think this -is- an example of a cultural hero, right? He's a hero to the Icewalkers, I'm sure. But he's not any more a good or bad person than any other conqueror.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you.<br /> <br /> One of the first lessons to learn when making an argument is that absolutes are harder to defend and generally not true, thats the main problemI have with the &quot;all solars are heroes&quot; argument.<br /> <br /> Would it be safe to say all solars are heroes to someone, either willingly or unwillingly and most solar tend to be good people?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2245-quimeradc","name":"Quimeradc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T10:09:21-07:00","id":88897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quimeradc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88850#post88850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it be safe to say all solars are heroes to someone, either willingly or unwillingly and most solar tend to be good people?</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is still that &quot;tends to be good&quot; means something completely different depending on how you frame a situation, and is in fact so context sensitive that it doesn't really clarify anything. Like, say that the American Civil War was happening while Solar Exaltations are flying around. Does anyone from the South get to Exalt as a Solar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/870-side-item","name":"Side Item","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar870_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T10:20:31-07:00","id":88901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quimeradc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88850#post88850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Would it be safe to say all solars are heroes to someone, either willingly or unwillingly and most solar tend to be good people?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think earlier in the thread it was said best where good isn't the opposite of malicious. Just because you don't go about kicking dogs means you are a good person. It just means you aren't someone who goes around doing that specific generally disliked thing.<br /> <br /> Many Solars will be this. Not all of them are going to go about becoming Pillage McRapeTyrant. But that doesn't mean they are &quot;good people.&quot; Anymore than any other normal human who doesn't go about wantonly breaking the law if given power is a &quot;good person.&quot; Not doing evil is not the same as being good.<br /> <br /> Or to come accross saying the same thing a third time: Solars are people. People are bad or good on their individual actions and choices. It is usually judged as good or not after the fact depending on the consequences. And often when a person does soemthing, it is not for its &quot;ultimate good&quot; but for all matter of other reasons which run the gamut of human experience and expectations.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T10:22:31-07:00","id":88903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quimeradc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88850#post88850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it be safe to say all solars are heroes to someone, either willingly or unwillingly and most solar tend to be good people?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say almost all Solars are heroes to someone, and most Solars tend to exemplify at least one virtue, as has always been the case. In 3e, there will be a little more freedom to explore various virtues, as there will no longer be the overly reductive 4-virtue model; Courage/Valor is obviously going to be a common one from the classical assortment, as is Temperance. It's also good not to ignore Indignation: I can see a Solar being Exalted who gets destructively, violently angry, but usually does it when it is appropriate. Generosity/Magnanimity is also worth thinking about. <br /> <br /> Are Solars &quot;good&quot; people? Well, what is the &quot;good?&quot; That is a question thousands of years old at this point, and it is still debated today. Most Solars do have at least one character trait that is considered good, and exemplify it, often to the maximum. Mostly, I disagree if this is used to deduce they tend to run around doing good deeds most of the time; I think it is better if that question is left more open-ended.<br /> <br /> Whether a deed is &quot;good&quot; or not is difficult to determine, and trying to make it easy, I think, would take away a lot of nuance. It wouldn't be surprising for a group of Solars to kill or exile a tyrannical Southern Dynastic Satrap. But what about everyone earning income through trading with the Realm? What happens when Wong Bongerok's goons join forces with the Old Gods to set up a new hierarchy over the people? What happens when the Wyld Hunt is gone and strange Exalts begin moving in and carving out their own fiefdoms? Acts which are good and justified in isolation can have consequences that are far worse than acts of petty evil, and Exalted, with its emphasis on sociology, economics, and anthropology, is positively begging people to consider the ramifications of &quot;good&quot; actions. <br /> <br /> Solars will, in most cases, fight the power structures that perpetuate evil in the setting and lead the re-creation of a new status quo. That is their principle role. However, the question of whether things can get better or whether there is a constant struggle to keep things from getting even worse seems to be an important and open-ended one. To say that the Solars can beat up the bad guys and make everything better is both superficially true and dubious on a deeper level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1595-scatters-the-ashes","name":"Scatters-the-Ashes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1595_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T10:32:19-07:00","id":88908,"title":"","content":"I completely agree with you guys; i think that a level of determinsim as all heroes are &quot;good&quot; inserts a false black and white morality that is not good for the narrative and turns the setting into a saturday morning cartoon. I generally dislike anything in a game setting that clearly defines who is evil, like dnd aligment system, mounstrous races and detect evil spells.<br /> <br /> But there are others here, like hippokrene, that think otherwise. Im trying to reconcile sides as best posible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2245-quimeradc","name":"Quimeradc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T11:00:03-07:00","id":88937,"title":"","content":"If your idea of what makes a Solar means I can't make Solar Julie d'Aubigny, Solar Hercules, and Solar Conan, it's probably a flawed one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Once, there was a maiden... who spent all her time on the internet.<br /> &quot;Someone out there is WRONG,&quot; she said.<br /> So she tossed a noose made of golden light... and strangled her opponent.<br /> Both of them died alone.<br /> &quot;Love is for football players and cheerleaders,&quot; her obituary said.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/261-notthepenguins","name":"notthepenguins","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar261_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"359"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T11:04:37-07:00","id":88943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>notthepenguins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88937#post88937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your idea of what makes a Solar means I can't make Solar Julie d'Aubigny, Solar Hercules, and Solar Conan, it's probably a flawed one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now, there's a question that might be worth asking: for those who favor an interpretation of Solars as good, is Conan good? Is Hercules? Is Julie d'Aubigny? Why or why not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/926-yishten","name":"Yishten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar926_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T11:04:37-07:00","id":88944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>notthepenguins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88937#post88937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your idea of what makes a Solar means I can't make Solar Julie d'Aubigny, Solar Hercules, and Solar Conan, it's probably a flawed one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll more details to understand your point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2245-quimeradc","name":"Quimeradc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T11:11:27-07:00","id":88948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quimeradc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88944#post88944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll more details to understand your point.</div> </div> </div> </div>The entire idea of &quot;solars as heroes&quot; even if you adopt maximum ethical relativism, is that these characters think they are and/or want to make the world a better place.<br /> <br /> None of these three examples did either. Hercules bummed around trying to make up for his sins, Conan and Julie d'Aubigny just did whatever they damn well pleased. All three are <i>great</i> Solar archetypes, and all of them have been mentioned by writers as Solar archetypes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Once, there was a maiden... who spent all her time on the internet.<br /> &quot;Someone out there is WRONG,&quot; she said.<br /> So she tossed a noose made of golden light... and strangled her opponent.<br /> Both of them died alone.<br /> &quot;Love is for football players and cheerleaders,&quot; her obituary said.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/261-notthepenguins","name":"notthepenguins","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar261_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"359"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T16:22:47-07:00","id":89098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88788#post88788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not live in Mongolia or Romania. I'm going to guess that the stories they tell about these figures aren't exactly the stories we tell about them. Especially as most of the stories I've heard about Vlad the Impaler involve him making a deal with the devil and turning into a vampire.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I have said several times that I am fine with morally dubious Solars. I explicitly said that there will be exceptions to 'Solars are heroes' and non-heroic PCs were just as good as heroic ones in <i>the original post. </i><br /> <br /> But the default? The center? Solars are heroes. Noble, inspiring, and good.<br /> <br /> Subtext is the edge. I expect players to explore it. It gives the PCs and the setting depth, but I am devoted to 'Solars are heroes' as the surface.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that Solars are heroes<br /> <br /> Just not that in Exalted, hero means &quot;noble, inspiring or good.&quot; It might, but it might not be any of those things. Look at who inspires the Solar Exalted. Herakles murders his family in a fit. Achilles is the personification of hubristic rage and arrogant disdain. Gilgamesh and Enkidu are not particularly virtuous at all. Liu Biu kills thousands upon thousands in pursuit of his throne. Fingolfin is driven by covetous jealousy, Lews Therin Telamon by madness. Beowulf is a ruthless killer out for glory. Alexander the Great slaughtered cities. Genghis Khan is one of the greatest conquerors ever and his armies killed millions.<br /> <br /> Being a Solar means that you are swathed in the magnificent grandeur of an epic tale, the protaganist of your own earth shaking story, a name that will resonate for a thousand thousand years. It doesn't make you moral or immoral. It just makes you a <i>big deal</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":117,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","user":"Solar","date":". 03-11-2014, 07:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T17:02:37-07:00","id":89122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yishten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88943#post88943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now, there's a question that might be worth asking: for those who favor an interpretation of Solars as good, is Conan good? Is Hercules? Is Julie d'Aubigny? Why or why not?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm currently reading Conan. He's not as bad as some of the folks he runs into. He's not good though. He is actually kind of an asshole. He himself never seems to weigh his actions on good or bad but instead on sensible (by his standards) or perserving his pride. As a king his people seem to like him, but as i gather it's because he's not really as into some of the more tyranical habits of everyone else about. he still has slaves, and kills people.<br /> <br /> Another example I toss about is Zorayas form <i>Night's Master</i>, who I would say is the quintessential Twilight. And as I can gather, she knows full well she's a monster and doesn't give a shit. Simmu, one of the main characters in the second book of the series, seems utterly amoral in the sense that he's naive to morals. He only hates killing people because he's terrified of death itself in any form. And this series is kind of a huge bit of inspiration for Exalted as a whole.<br /> <br /> I would say similar with Heracles. He apparently thought it was worth making up for killing his family. He was as I gather kind of a likeable strongman archetype. Whether that's good or not is another matter, but he's not bad. And note it wasn't until he did something blatetnly terrible that he decided to do anything specifically good and it's questionable how many of his acts in the trials were good or just being a badass, since as I gather the point of them were to kill him.<br /> <br /> Julie d'Aubigny is an interesting as hell person. Nothing in her write-up at the same time seems especially &quot;good&quot; save I guess maybe-kinda-sorta getting a girl out of a nunnary for three months? Maybe? Being a woman of great awesome in the time she lives in was sweet, but she was also kind of as roguish as it gets while doing it.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T17:11:16-07:00","id":89124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89098#post89098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fingolfin is driven by covetous jealousy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you mean Feanor. Fingolfin was actually one of the few named Noldor who DIDN'T really lose his damn mind over the Silmarilli, though he paid the same price for Feanor's horseshit as basically every other Noldor (though at least he got to go out in an awesome way).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Won't you believe in him? Even if there is no God, or Buddha...there is still Kamen Rider.&quot; \u2014Taki Kazuya, <i>Kamen Rider SPIRITS</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">Now...count up </span><span style=\"color:#4B0082\">all your sins.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/160-cyclonejoker","name":"CycloneJoker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T18:32:58-07:00","id":89158,"title":"","content":"I'll just note, to be sure it's as clear as possible: I'd in no way advocate, and I don't think others are advocating, that resistance to the idea of Solars being good equates to the idea that Solars are therefore bad. Neither extreme is sought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":926,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/926-yishten","user":"Yishten","date":". 03-11-2014, 10:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/926-yishten","name":"Yishten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar926_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T02:12:56-07:00","id":89350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yishten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89158#post89158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll just note, to be sure it's as clear as possible: I'd in no way advocate, and I don't think others are advocating, that resistance to the idea of Solars being good equates to the idea that Solars are therefore bad. Neither extreme is sought.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll quote a part of the first edition Exalted that I feel is relevant here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>First Edition on the subject of Exaltation p27</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those Exalted who do manifest during childhood tend to grow powerful (and wilful) very quickly and can be extremely difficult to control. <b>Very few Exalted of any type are inherently malicious</b>, but any young and untrained Exalted whose power outstrip their maturity can seriously endanger those around them.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I take from that is that while the Exalted are heroes, heroes are at the end of the day people even if they are great people with great power. That popular Spider-man quote goes &quot;With great power comes great responsibility&quot; but the Exaltation doesn't force you to take responsibility, it simply grants you power and it becomes up to the Exalted itself or those around them to give them responsibility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T02:28:04-07:00","id":89354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89122#post89122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Julie d'Aubigny is an interesting as hell person. Nothing in her write-up at the same time seems especially &quot;good&quot; save I guess maybe-kinda-sorta getting a girl out of a nunnary for three months? Maybe? Being a woman of great awesome in the time she lives in was sweet, but she was also kind of as roguish as it gets while doing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>She's certainly an interesting person to read about, but actually knowing her seems like it would be like knowing Joe Pesci's character from Goodfellas; either you're the type who gets in on the &quot;joke&quot; of the violence and taboos, and maybe eggs her on a bit, or you're the person who takes offense or rubs her the wrong way, and probably get stabbed a bit. She's fun, but only to a particular kind of person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T02:48:53-07:00","id":89364,"title":"","content":"Another thing that I thinks makes for an interesting point of consideration concerning Oda Nobunaga is:<br /> <br /> Okay, let's assume for a moment that Nobunaga did not live in a context where the power of sohei fanatics made it really politically expedient to ruthlessly destroy major Buddhist centres of power, including the massacre of huge numbers of innocent people living in them. Not to excuse, just to have an image of a Nobunaga who did not commit probably his biggest major atrocity.<br /> <br /> Okay, so Nobunaga is a guy setting out to reunify Japan. We couldn't really say to his exact motives, but given his own standards for administrative method and competence, one might assume that, at least as a practical concern, things generally being good for the lives of the regular people was a concern for him, so maybe he's got a perspective that a unified Japan is in all ways better than one where everybody is fighting over stuff. Not necessarily as an altruistic motive as one concerned with orderly life, and maybe a bit of personal grandeur.<br /> <br /> Bot Nobunaga the person was kind of an asshole. A highly charismatic asshole who made a point of elevating people based on merit rather than background, but still, by most accounts, a deeply unpleasant person to actually know. Highly idiosyncratic and with a really venomous tongue; tended to come up with demeaning nicknames for everyone. Also made a lot of gestures that seemed to disgust people, while he viewed them as decent or respectful; he was kind of the &quot;honoring your worthy fallen opponent&quot; type, except did so by turning a bunch of men's skulls into gilded drinking cups. His attitude might well have been the thing that got him killed; political benefits were nice and all, but it was kind of a case of Sideshow Bob lashing back against Krusty the Klown.<br /> <br /> Is that a good person?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T06:15:55-07:00","id":89426,"title":"","content":"I could go on about how I think the notion is a steaming pile of horse shit on the basis of the OP believing herself to be right and everyone else being wrong, but I will refrain from doing that. Isator, Gayo and others are doing a fine job as it is. I will just poin out that washed-down, bleak caricatures of heroes the OP wants Solars to be, would require washed-down, bleak caricatures of enemies to fight. I do not want to see washed-down, caricaturized, bleak Abyssals, Dragon Blooded, Infernals, Sidereals or Lunars. That is the only line of defense agaisnt OP's madness that should matter in this discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T06:28:22-07:00","id":89432,"title":"","content":"I do think it's important that Solars have a unique <i>thematic</i> of heroism, which is expressed in their charms and is not exclusively limited to &quot;larger than life&quot; or &quot;really powerful.&quot; When the Solar Larceny charms are worded as if they're designed to help Solars root out evil rather than to rob banks, for instance, that is meant to be a commentary on what Solars are. The reason Solars have so many anti-CoD charms, likewise, isn't because it reflects their patron (Solars are not 2e Infernals; they don't get UCS charms, and besides, chronologically their patron was written that way because of Solars, not the other way around). Solars have Holy effects because they embody a form of heroism. Likewise, if you want to write a Solar charm, you can use &quot;this is something a hero would do&quot; as a justification for some of its mechanics -- as in, &quot;the thematic this charm expresses is that the person who has it is a good person who is looked up to by those around them.&quot;<br /> <br /> Obviously it is a loose theme in that individual Solars don't have to be heroes just because their charms talk about crushing evil, and obviously their charms sometimes seem a bit over the top in that regard to the point where it's possible to read them ironically. CoD status (and therefore anti-CoD charms) is not a universal cosmic statement of good and evil, and nothing else in a Solar charm is going to actually be able to make that (because there's no such thing in Exalted.) But these things are meant to show a particular thematic, to the extent that even a corrupt or self-serving Solar is going to find that their charms subtly encourage them to behave in a way that at least looks heroic by some definitions.<br /> <br /> I also think that it's important that Exalted be a <i>smart</i> deconstruction. What that means is that you have to accept certain basic premises about heroism in order to ask deeper, more meaningful questions -- questions like &quot;what is heroism, really?&quot; or &quot;a hero to who?&quot; or the like are important. But if you start making outright statements like &quot;hahaha fuck heroism, it's all an obvious lie and you're an idiot for talking about it&quot;, I feel you're losing sight of what the game is supposed to be -- Exalted has to be able to encompass the mindset of heroic fantasy before it can start asking useful questions about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 05-20-2014, 11:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T06:38:15-07:00","id":89435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CycloneJoker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89124#post89124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you mean Feanor. Fingolfin was actually one of the few named Noldor who DIDN'T really lose his damn mind over the Silmarilli, though he paid the same price for Feanor's horseshit as basically every other Noldor (though at least he got to go out in an awesome way).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Fingolfin was probably the best king the Noldor ever got and a generally good dude, who didn't let pride poison him to others even when those others were genuinely treating him like shit. <br /> <br /> Terrible inspiration for an Exalt, really :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T06:52:05-07:00","id":89447,"title":"","content":"I think that hippokrene may have just been affected by &quot;Solar Propaganda Charm Fluff Technique&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The enemies of the Solar Exalted are creatures of vice </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Lawgivers govern wisely </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Only the unrighteous would lock a door to keep the Lawgivers out. Such an intention is proof of iniquity </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Lawgivers are the guardians of truth. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In foul nests of demons whose ways of corruption assault the human mind; amidst the courts of faeries gluttonous for human souls; in Nexus, surrounded by a thousand temptations\u2014 though the whole world seeks to drag him down, the Lawgiver is unmoved. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T07:09:14-07:00","id":89453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89432#post89432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do think it's important that Solars have a unique <i>thematic</i> of heroism, which is expressed in their charms and is not exclusively limited to &quot;larger than life&quot; or &quot;really powerful.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>First edition expressed it in an interesting way:<br /> Logic, heroism, inspiration and nobility are their spheres of influence.<br /> <br /> Interestingly the Solars were the only Exalted that they managed to describe so succinctly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89432#post89432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason Solars have so many anti-CoD charms, likewise, isn't because it reflects their patron (Solars are not 2e Infernals; they don't get UCS charms, and besides, chronologically their patron was written that way because of Solars, not the other way around). Solars have Holy effects because they embody a form of heroism.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know the author intent, but my general impression is that the Solar Holy charms have always drawn on the Righteousness and Nobility aspects of Solars, not the Heroism one. The charms tend to have a <i>'Creation is MINE not yours'</i> feel to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T07:28:32-07:00","id":89461,"title":"","content":"Jen, you forgot <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is the Lawgivers' right to confiscate goods necessary to the service of the Unconquered Sun. </div> </div> </div>Though <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Only the unrighteous would lock a door to keep the Lawgivers out. Such an intention is proof of iniquity </div> </div> </div> is definitely the best one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know the author intent, but my general impression is that the Solar Holy charms have always drawn on the Righteousness and Nobility aspects of Solars, not the Heroism one. The charms tend to have a <i>'Creation is MINE not yours'</i> feel to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of. I think it's about surface impressions again.<br /> On the surface, Solars look like the good guys, fighting the enemies of Creation, like demons and ghosts and stuff, so they get special charms for it (well, actually all Exalts get them, Solars just have a bit more). But as the book says, all Ghosts are CoDs, not all ghosts are evil. To be honest, not all demons are evil. Some are just weird. Sesseljae have Compassion 4, IIRC. And there are plenty of evil Exalts who are not CoDs.<br /> They look like heroes, but it's a bit of a deconstruction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T07:28:35-07:00","id":89462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88788#post88788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I am devoted to 'Solars are heroes' as the surface.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is clearly the case, but I think it might be harming the discussion a little bit. When you start saying, 'the default assumptions of the setting should be this', especially when your definition is more restrictive than the published one, people are (correctly) going to react as though you're excluding their play style and preferred themes. If you had begun this thread with something like 'At my table I prefer to focus of the heroic aspects of Solars' I doubt the thread would have gotten any negative responses. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have said several times that I am fine with morally dubious Solars. I explicitly said that there will be exceptions to 'Solars are heroes' and non-heroic PCs were just as good as heroic ones in <i>the original post.</i> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but you're saying this in the context of 'The default assumptions should confirm to my preferences, and everything else is an edge case'. You may as well say 'well nothing's stopping a lunar game where everyone's Chimera', 'Lunars operate perfectly well using Knacks only, Charms are prohibited at my table', or 'if they operate within certain parameters Abyssals can plant flowers, tousle the hair of urchins and work as attendants at the local 'Make-A-Bear'. While all this may be true, they are absolutely discouraged by the material. <br /> <br /> \u200bLikewise, when you say Solars should be heroes by default you <i>definitively</i> discourage any other sort of play, no matter how much fine print you add afterwards. I don't honestly think there's a lot of people playing Havesh the Vashisher at their tables (though it there is, more power to them!) but there is a huge range of themes concerning heroism, what it is, and how you rise or fall to it that you immediately exclude if you decide <i>a priori</i> that Solars are heroes. A lot of people, as evidenced by the responses in the thread, find this a compelling space to pay in. <br /> <br /> <br /> Is there anything worth achieving by limiting the thematic space of Solars, in light of the fact that it runs against the material we've been invited to use to anticipate the tone of the new edition?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T07:32:53-07:00","id":89465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I could go on about how I think the notion is a steaming pile of horse shit on the basis of the OP believing herself to be right and everyone else being wrong, </div> </div> </div> I disagree with her, so I think I'm right and everyone who disagrees with me is wrong, for example the OP. Otherwise I wouldn't hold this view, because I wouldn't think it's right. That's just logic. And you clearly think our side is right and her side is wrong. It would be illogical otherwise.<br /> Although of course, I am obviously the one who is right. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Let's try and keep things civil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T07:36:48-07:00","id":89469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuddenThunder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't honestly think there's a lot of people playing Havesh the Vashisher at their tables</div> </div> </div> </div> If it were not cheap to steal a character wholesale from published materials, I would totally play Havesh. He is definitely in my top 10 Solars from the Caste Books.<br /> I strongly considered making him King Havesh I of Varang in the game I ran. It wouldn't have added anything to the game, but I just like him that much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 03-12-2014, 10:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T07:49:26-07:00","id":89478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89469#post89469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If it were not cheap to steal a character wholesale from published materials, I would totally play Havesh.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I've come very close to playing Lyta. I didn't burn all the Dragon-Bloods, I just spoke to them quietly about the Unconquered Sun and (thanks to social charms) completely changed their lives. I still built ziggurat temples everywhere I went, but I also freed satrapies from economic slavery, reformed the local divinities and brought (relative) religious freedom everywhere I went. <br /> <br /> The fact that I was continuing to (maybe) brainwash everyone I spent a few quiet minutes with and planned to unfold a vast, enforced Valentines Day across the entire West as a means of combating the local Abysalls, and the questions of whetrher any of this was desirable or even acceptable in the grand scheme of things were basically essential to the character's journey. <br /> <br /> None of it would be encouraged in a context where the Solars are definitively heroes. My character is, definitively, marginalised by the thread's proposition. I think possibly that all my Solar characters are. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T07:50:28-07:00","id":89479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuddenThunder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89462#post89462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> \u200bLikewise, when you say Solars should be heroes by default you <i>definitively</i> discourage any other sort of play, no matter how much fine print you add afterwards. I don't honestly think there's a lot of people playing Havesh the Vashisher at their tables (though it there is, more power to them!) but there is a huge range of themes concerning heroism, what it is, and how you rise or fall to it that you immediately exclude if you decide <i>a priori</i> that Solars are heroes. A lot of people, as evidenced by the responses in the thread, find this a compelling space to pay in.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>In my games solar player characters are generally well intentioned and heoric. <br /> <br /> But I think there are always npc solars working for purely personal motives in my games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2245-quimeradc","name":"Quimeradc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T08:07:47-07:00","id":89489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quimeradc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89479#post89479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my games solar player characters are generally well intentioned and heoric.<br /> <br /> But I think there are always npc solars working for purely personal motives in my games.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I have no issue with this. <br /> <br /> Which is why I'm not trying to declare default assumptions for the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T14:48:09-07:00","id":89726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89426#post89426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could go on about how I think the notion is a steaming pile of horse shit on the basis of the OP believing herself to be right and everyone else being wrong, but I will refrain from doing that. Isator, Gayo and others are doing a fine job as it is. I will just poin out that washed-down, bleak caricatures of heroes the OP wants Solars to be, would require washed-down, bleak caricatures of enemies to fight. I do not want to see washed-down, caricaturized, bleak Abyssals, Dragon Blooded, Infernals, Sidereals or Lunars. That is the only line of defense agaisnt OP's madness that should matter in this discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Much as I don't agree with the OP<br /> <br /> This is not a cool way to say so","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T16:36:38-07:00","id":89814,"title":"","content":"While I may not agree with the central thesis of the original post in every detail, I find myself supporting it regardless, as I find that hewing to a general impression of the setting where Solars are seen as generally good people stops my central complaint about exalted as a thing.<br /> <br /> That being, when I go into a game playing a solar, and construct a solar who is actually a good dude, who feels guilty about having to kill people (does it anyway because there isn't a reasonable alternative), tries to help people, and is in general the kind of warrior-philosopher who focuses on self-awareness and finding root causes to problems BEFORE he starts swinging his sword (as opposed to after, if ever), you know, a GOOD PERSON. I get told that I'm doing it wrong, and need to make my character a callous killer, or support slavery, or a narcissistic asshole, because EPIC TRAGEDY and DECONSTRUCTION OF TROPES and REALISM.<br /> <br /> @#$%! that noise. If I want to play that kind of mythic hero, screaming into the uncaring tide of violence and injustice of Creation, I am not having bad-wrong-fun, and I'm rather sick of being told by everyone I bring my characters up to that I am.<br /> <br /> The idea that Solars are (secretly) the true villains of the setting, and/or that the setting is irrevocably doomed to degradation and/or destruction and nothing anyone does really matters in the long run is the single most toxic meme this fandom has ever seized on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/206-sylverdyne","name":"Sylverdyne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar206_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T17:15:27-07:00","id":89835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sylverdyne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89814#post89814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I may not agree with the central thesis of the original post in every detail, I find myself supporting it regardless, as I find that hewing to a general impression of the setting where Solars are seen as generally good people stops my central complaint about exalted as a thing.<br /> <br /> That being, when I go into a game playing a solar, and construct a solar who is actually a good dude, who feels guilty about having to kill people (does it anyway because there isn't a reasonable alternative), tries to help people, and is in general the kind of warrior-philosopher who focuses on self-awareness and finding root causes to problems BEFORE he starts swinging his sword (as opposed to after, if ever), you know, a GOOD PERSON. I get told that I'm doing it wrong, and need to make my character a callous killer, or support slavery, or a narcissistic asshole, because EPIC TRAGEDY and DECONSTRUCTION OF TROPES and REALISM.<br /> <br /> @#$%! that noise. If I want to play that kind of mythic hero, screaming into the uncaring tide of violence and injustice of Creation, I am not having bad-wrong-fun, and I'm rather sick of being told by everyone I bring my characters up to that I am.<br /> <br /> The idea that Solars are (secretly) the true villains of the setting, and/or that the setting is irrevocably doomed to degradation and/or destruction and nothing anyone does really matters in the long run is the single most toxic meme this fandom has ever seized on.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I wouldn't like to be insulting to anyone you know, I have to say that what you're presenting here seems to be much more of a problem with the way the people you play with view and interpret the game as opposed to a problem with the game itself, and that a lot of people do not have this particular problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ultimate Jade-Screened Exalted Scholar, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304239-my-next-campaign-tdhr-peach\" target=\"_blank\">THDR : Future Dragon-Blooded campaign</a>, and other links.<br /> If you like Ex3, you can support <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/holdenshearer\" target=\"_blank\">Holden</a> on Patreon!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","name":"LeTipex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T17:44:47-07:00","id":89848,"title":"","content":"&quot;Solars are Heroes&quot;<br /> <br /> I agree with this statement<br /> <br /> &quot;Heroes are people who want to change the world for what they see as the better&quot;<br /> <br /> I do not agree with this<br /> <br /> For me, a Hero is not defined by his motives, but by his actions. They do things that ordinary people cannot/dare not. They confront opponents that cause lesser people to quake in their boots. And yes, culture heroes usually are doing these impossible things and confronting these terrible foes for the betterment of the cultures they represent. But they don't have to be good, or even nice. They just have to be willing to dare what others will not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a Woman, I'm a GM. <i>Of course</i> I'm Evil.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/424-dawaterrat","name":"DaWaterRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T18:07:03-07:00","id":89857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sylverdyne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89814#post89814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea that Solars are (secretly) the true villains of the setting, and/or that the setting is irrevocably doomed to degradation and/or destruction and nothing anyone does really matters in the long run is the single most toxic meme this fandom has ever seized on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m really agree with you on this. I\u2019m not sure why there is such an affinity to the darker potential of a Solar. I understand the appeal of playing a villain, or a character that relies more on vice than virtue, the last Infernal game I played in only lasted a few sessions as my villainous machinations threatened to shatter the plan my GM had come up with for the campaign. I\u2019m just not sure I see the appeal of playing a villainous or morally lacking Solar, and I am certainly surprised that so many people think that this style of character should be if not the de-facto state of a Solar, at the very least as common as the \u201cgood\u201d variety.<br /> <br /> I know there are all sorts of canon examples of nihilism and abuse of power throughout the lore of the game in regards to Solars but I really feel this is more of an outlier element. If you read the core book in its description of Solars, and the backgrounds and stories of the signature Solar circle, they all reflect the Solar drive for greatness and to some degree a motivation to do good by the world. I think someone who is a sociopathic cult leader, a skilled assassin who will take any job for the right price, or a merciless magnate of a slave caravan, should be precluded from receiving an exaltation unless they will also receive a new direction in life in the process (ie. Panther\u2019s revelation of his debauchery and vice). That\u2019s not to say that they can\u2019t lapse back into old form or find themselves pulled towards an even darker path, just that the beginning of their journey as a Solar should be virtuous in some way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T18:37:50-07:00","id":89868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sylverdyne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89814#post89814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That being, when I go into a game playing a solar, and construct a solar who is actually a good dude, who feels guilty about having to kill people (does it anyway because there isn't a reasonable alternative), tries to help people, and is in general the kind of warrior-philosopher who focuses on self-awareness and finding root causes to problems BEFORE he starts swinging his sword (as opposed to after, if ever), you know, a GOOD PERSON. I get told that I'm doing it wrong, and need to make my character a callous killer, or support slavery, or a narcissistic asshole, because EPIC TRAGEDY and DECONSTRUCTION OF TROPES and REALISM.<br /> <br /> @#$%! that noise. If I want to play that kind of mythic hero, screaming into the uncaring tide of violence and injustice of Creation, I am not having bad-wrong-fun, and I'm rather sick of being told by everyone I bring my characters up to that I am.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, idiots are a thing. If you've got idiots telling you that your characters are wrong because they don't conform to their expectations, find some new idiots to play with. If you reengineer the setting to make Solars default to &quot;good,&quot; then all that will happen will be that you will force a deviation from the original vision so that your idiots will leave you alone, but someone else will come on here and complain about their idiots who think that their jaded Solar narcissist is wrong because he or she's not a paladin. So we've traded one set of idiots for another. Let's just stick with the idiots we have, then, yeah?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The idea that Solars are (secretly) the true villains of the setting, and/or that the setting is irrevocably doomed to degradation and/or destruction and nothing anyone does really matters in the long run is the single most toxic meme this fandom has ever seized on. </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure that anyone arguing against Solars as good are arguing in favor of Solars as villains, secret or otherwise. They're arguing for Solars as people-- you know, all types. Now, the idea that the setting is doomed no matter what anyone does, yeah, that's a thing-- but it's one that has nothing, whatsoever, to do with the goodness, badness, or otherwiseness of individual characters or whole character types.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/926-yishten","name":"Yishten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar926_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T19:29:58-07:00","id":89883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sylverdyne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89814#post89814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get told that I'm doing it wrong, and need to make my character a callous killer, or support slavery, or a narcissistic asshole, because EPIC TRAGEDY and DECONSTRUCTION OF TROPES and REALISM.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. I get that, I guess, in a way, sorta. I like to play flawed heroes too, but I don't think it's fun to force my friends to play my characters and bully them if they don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/994-heroicantagonist","name":"heroicantagonist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar994_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T19:37:03-07:00","id":89885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89857#post89857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019m really agree with you on this. I\u2019m not sure why there is such an affinity to the darker potential of a Solar. I understand the appeal of playing a villain, or a character that relies more on vice than virtue, the last Infernal game I played in only lasted a few sessions as my villainous machinations threatened to shatter the plan my GM had come up with for the campaign. I\u2019m just not sure I see the appeal of playing a villainous or morally lacking Solar, and I am certainly surprised that so many people think that this style of character should be if not the de-facto state of a Solar, at the very least as common as the \u201cgood\u201d variety.<br /> <br /> I know there are all sorts of canon examples of nihilism and abuse of power throughout the lore of the game in regards to Solars but I really feel this is more of an outlier element. If you read the core book in its description of Solars, and the backgrounds and stories of the signature Solar circle, they all reflect the Solar drive for greatness and to some degree a motivation to do good by the world. I think someone who is a sociopathic cult leader, a skilled assassin who will take any job for the right price, or a merciless magnate of a slave caravan, should be precluded from receiving an exaltation unless they will also receive a new direction in life in the process (ie. Panther\u2019s revelation of his debauchery and vice). That\u2019s not to say that they can\u2019t lapse back into old form or find themselves pulled towards an even darker path, just that the beginning of their journey as a Solar should be virtuous in some way.</div> </div> </div> </div>The argument isn't Solars need to be secret villains or sociopaths. The argument is that the default Solar is intrinsically good. That, frankly, is total crap. Solars are Heroes, they make history by their own hands, they dare to do what others cannot, but they are not inherently good or evil, that characteristic comes from the person who is a Solar, not their Solarness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T20:18:44-07:00","id":89899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89885#post89885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The argument isn't Solars need to be secret villains or sociopaths. The argument is that the default Solar is intrinsically good. That, frankly, is total crap. Solars are Heroes, they make history by their own hands, they dare to do what others cannot, but they are not inherently good or evil, that characteristic comes from the person who is a Solar, not their Solarness.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am, actually, aware of the specifics of the argument. I'm arguing that the original argument has merit. Even if you establish that solars are, in general and by assumption, reasonably good people you do not somehow negate the fact that 'Good Person' is an incredibly vague term, and that even the best of good people can do horrific things from a removed perspective.<br /> <br /> There are issues with the tone in 2e that makes almost everyone in my area think Solar Great Curse == Your character must be a terrible person who will only ever make the world worse. I'm arguing that going forward, the tone should be that the solars are, in general, by and large good people. I also advocate leaving Havesh and Lyta in as is.<br /> <br /> The argument is not that, like a D&amp;D paladin, your goodness makes you a solar. The argument is that whatever vague, mysterious, unknown and unknowable processes that lead to one becoming a solar, that resulting sample of the population (Read: the population of individuals who actually DID exalt into solars) tends to favor people who, in the right light, are 'good', whatever that means.<br /> <br /> Please explain what about the setting breaks if that is true, because I don't think it changes ANYTHING other then how the players and fans approach solars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/206-sylverdyne","name":"Sylverdyne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar206_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T20:46:41-07:00","id":89910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89857#post89857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019m really agree with you on this. I\u2019m not sure why there is such an affinity to the darker potential of a Solar. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>This is part of your hang-up. You're creating a false dichotomy. You are first accepting hippokrene's intial (and argued to be false) definition of heroism as inherent &quot;goodness&quot; (whatever the fuck that actually even means beyond &quot;I as a 21st Century Western Wrold person thinks is good&quot;). And since we say it is not inherently good, you then claim it means they are particularly villainous. You don't actually build the bridge of logic to cross that gap.<br /> <br /> I'm not &quot;more interested in the villainous potentila of Solars more than their heroic.&quot; I think &quot;Solars are good guys always&quot; is juevenile, against the source material, and both intellectually and philosophically lazy and boring. I'm not interested in the &quot;darker potential of Solars&quot; and more in the actual potential of humanity. Humans are inherently flawed and can do bad things. It's not the job a magic doo-dad to limit their potential to do these at a certain scale.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89857#post89857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... I understand the appeal of playing a villain, or a character that relies more on vice than virtue, the last Infernal game I played in only lasted a few sessions as my villainous machinations threatened to shatter the plan my GM had come up with for the campaign. I\u2019m just not sure I see the appeal of playing a villainous or morally lacking Solar, and I am certainly surprised that so many people think that this style of character should be if not the de-facto state of a Solar, at the very least as common as the \u201cgood\u201d variety.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're pulling the false dichotomy shit again. I'm not interested in &quot;villainous&quot; or &quot;heroic&quot; or &quot;good&quot; people for Solars. I'm interested in <i>great</i> people. And the itneresting people of fiction and history that Solar Exalted draw upon are going to be more nuanced than a simple villain/rogue virtue/vice thing. You get that in most any other fantasy setting (lots of the ones with anti-heroes even more or less treat them as working on these alignment stuff your working off of). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89857#post89857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know there are all sorts of canon examples of nihilism and abuse of power throughout the lore of the game in regards to Solars but I really feel this is more of an outlier element. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea that Solars don't eventually become people with lots of power and no responsiblity to use it wisely, as a note, is ab it of a foundation to the entire Usurpation. You undermine a lot when you make &quot;Solars can do bad things because people do bad things and Solars aren't normal people but a subset of them&quot;. And you cut off a lot of people who are really just htere doing big stuff. I again cite Conan, Sinbad and Achilles in the case of ficiton, or Oda Nobunaga, Genghis Khan or Julius Caesar in the case of history. People who, by your defintions of hero are not &quot;good enough&quot; to be Solars. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89857#post89857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... If you read the core book in its description of Solars, and the backgrounds and stories of the signature Solar circle, they all reflect the Solar drive for greatness and to some degree a motivation to do good by the world. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Aesha, literally the very first Solar Exalt we ever see, draws a group of soldiers into a shadowland to be slaughtered, kills two Dragon-Blooded and steals their shit with an intention of selling it to fund her escape from the city. We have no idea of her background beyond growing up in that city (and seems not really intent on &quot;fixing&quot; it ever). Unless genocide against people from the Blessed Isle or funding a scavenger's coffers is &quot;good&quot;, she's not really any or less moral than some of the characters I note above.<br /> <br /> Dace goes after Ma-Ha-Suchi, that's heroic, but that's monster slaying in general. Evne Conan slayed monsters, though Dace is a nice guy overall. He still is a sellsword, as a note, so how much hired soldier is an upright good thing is antoher matter. Profiteering I would think by modern standards is not continued very moral. That's about it. Harmonious Jade robs a tomb (good for her), Swan tricks a wood spider (who is going to fuck someone less clever over later on), Panther became good by Exalting, not Exalt for being good (and we haven't seen more than what I would say is a caricature of actual abolitionism personally). And I for the life of me can't actually remember what the fuck Arianna's ficiton is about. So you read a very different set of fiction pieces about Solars than I did.<br /> <br /> Also, the Usurpation was a thing and there's at least some pretense that Chejob actually thought he did the right thing, unless you want to paint the Sidereals as a bunch of scheming power-grabbing viziers and the Solars were actually good kings with a bad rap.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89857#post89857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... I think someone who is a sociopathic cult leader, a skilled assassin who will take any job for the right price, or a merciless magnate of a slave caravan, should be precluded from receiving an exaltation unless they will also receive a new direction in life in the process (ie. Panther\u2019s revelation of his debauchery and vice). ...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think such a view is showing your holding onto too black and white a moral view in general. It was asked, but would you be okay with Howard's Conan never being a Solar then? Because Sinbad never really wanted to do anything but travel and get rich, he's not a good guy either right? Just a leader to men's deaths, a cuthroat merchant and in a few cases outright murderer? Is it okay because he's the protagonist? What's the line, and why does the Exaltation get to draw it instead of just letting people be people and draw it as their actions seem logcial to dictate? That's actual drama of humans and characters worthy of being like those in history and legend in my opinion instead of something in the young adult section of the bookstore.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89857#post89857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... That\u2019s not to say that they can\u2019t lapse back into old form or find themselves pulled towards an even darker path, just that the beginning of their journey as a Solar should be virtuous in some way.</div> </div> </div> </div>And we're arguing that's what all sorts of other &quot;hero reborn&quot; plots do anyhow. Or superhero plots. Or really most fantasy plots with non esplicit anti-heroes (who in a weird way do that anyhow). We want characters who are humans, not some whitewashed view of &quot;The best of humanity.&quot; I will also note that such a want for Solars, and Solars only has other problems. Mainly in making opposing Solars in general or preventing them in happening at all is casting any Exalt opposing a Solar as opposing a person who was at least inherently good to start. Which makes a Solar's antagonists easily evil. WHich is kind of damaging for all sorts of reasons.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T21:01:41-07:00","id":89912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sylverdyne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89899#post89899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I am, actually, aware of the specifics of the argument. I'm arguing that the original argument has merit. Even if you establish that solars are, in general and by assumption, reasonably good people you do not somehow negate the fact that 'Good Person' is an incredibly vague term, and that even the best of good people can do horrific things from a removed perspective. There are issues with the tone in 2e that makes almost everyone in my area think Solar Great Curse == Your character must be a terrible person who will only ever make the world worse. I'm arguing that going forward, the tone should be that the solars are, in general, by and large good people. I also advocate leaving Havesh and Lyta in as is. The argument is not that, like a D&amp;D paladin, your goodness makes you a solar. The argument is that whatever vague, mysterious, unknown and unknowable processes that lead to one becoming a solar, that resulting sample of the population (Read: the population of individuals who actually DID exalt into solars) tends to favor people who, in the right light, are 'good', whatever that means. Please explain what about the setting breaks if that is true, because I don't think it changes ANYTHING other then how the players and fans approach solars.</div> </div> </div> </div> It doesn't change the setting. It changes the theme of the portrayal (which is not universally desired) and for some, the verisimilitude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/926-yishten","name":"Yishten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar926_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T21:19:25-07:00","id":89913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89910#post89910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I will also note that such a want for Solars, and Solars only has other problems. Mainly in making opposing Solars in general or preventing them in happening at all is casting any Exalt opposing a Solar as opposing a person who was at least inherently good to start. Which makes a Solar's antagonists easily evil. WHich is kind of damaging for all sorts of reasons.<br /> <br /> And stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>You bring this point up again and I still do not understand it. Why does the fact a Solar is a good person automatically make their opposition evil? Just looking it over it comes off as a rather simplistic moral outlook where conflict can only arise between &quot;bad&quot; or evil&quot; people, So just to be clear why can't two good people get into a conflict with each other that could potentially burn a country to the ground or shake the heavens? If we know that one is a good person why can't the other one be a good person as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon","name":"Calboon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar223_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T21:24:32-07:00","id":89915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sylverdyne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89899#post89899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am, actually, aware of the specifics of the argument. I'm arguing that the original argument has merit. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>First, the OP wasn't an argument and has yet to be argued for by the OP. It was a declarative statement. It was &quot;I say hero = this and Solars are heroes, so Solars are this.&quot; It's a valid argument. It's an unsound one because the first premise &quot;hero = this&quot; is a false statement, or at least a yet ot be defended-for one beyond admited attempts of quote-mining.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sylverdyne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89899#post89899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Even if you establish that solars are, in general and by assumption, reasonably good people you do not somehow negate the fact that 'Good Person' is an incredibly vague term, and that even the best of good people can do horrific things from a removed perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue is that &quot;good person&quot; is not definable in a way that matters in Creation to even be a criterion. It creates an issue that if Solars are &quot;good people&quot; and yet no objective state of Creation says what a &quot;good person&quot; even is, it leads to all sorts of shitty consequences. The logic is flawed. You are left with an issue where goodness is defined by Solarness, as a world with no intrinsic measure a good, save apparently the Solar Exaltation, you have made <i>that</i> the measuring stick of goodness.<br /> <br /> It also does other shitty things. Since Solars are the only Exalt that's baseline &quot;good&quot;, they are the Exalt most likely to be expected to be good. It becomes difficult to expect or categorize poor Solar behavior, yet at the same time you can outrigh tjust call Dragon-Blooded, Lunars, Sidereals or any other Exalt as &quot;bad&quot;. They're not Solars, so you have no assumption to their apparent good or badness. This is outright unacceptable if you want them to be NPCs and you want any ambiguity on the return of the Solars as being a good thing. By Solars also being assumed to be good or tending towards good behavior save as accpetion, you also undermine the Usurpation, which is one of the most defining eveng of the setting probably since the Primordial War.<br /> <br /> Or to put it another way, it leads to absurdity and contradicitons. It's a bad point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sylverdyne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89899#post89899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are issues with the tone in 2e that makes almost everyone in my area think Solar Great Curse == Your character must be a terrible person who will only ever make the world worse. I'm arguing that going forward, the tone should be that the solars are, in general, by and large good people. I also advocate leaving Havesh and Lyta in as is.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a way to acheive a non-2e feel without making Solar Exaltation objective goodness in the setting. You even explain it in your own post here. If you write Solars as simply not going asshat by default, you can get a lot better results in presenting interesting characters. But note that &quot;not doing bad things&quot; =/= &quot;a good person&quot;. Just becuase I proved you're not a total scumbag does not mean I proved you're a saint. Look at it logically like this:<br /> <br /> 1) (x)(Bad(x) -&gt; Kicks(x,puppies)) (In all cases of x, where ix is bad, than x kicks puppies)<br /> 2) ~Kicks(Bob,puppies) (Bob doens't kick puppies).<br /> C) ~Bad(Bob) due to 1, 2 and MT (some other stuff, but basically since i can show Bob doens't kick puppies, Bob isn't bad).<br /> <br /> The thing I proved here, though, <i>didn't</i> prove Bob is good. It only shows he didn't do an act I consider bad. Replace kicks puppies with anything else you consider evil. Murder, rape, whatever. Not doing bad things doesn't make you good. You have to do good to do good. That's been argued through this thread. No one is &quot;inehrently good&quot; since &quot;good&quot; is subjective and not something you probably can have inherently. But your acts and deeds might be seen as good. Or bad. Or neither. The only thing Exaltation requires is your acts be great. Going at them in another way actually hurts a lot of the setting's ideas.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sylverdyne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89899#post89899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The argument is not that, like a D&amp;D paladin, your goodness makes you a solar. The argument is that whatever vague, mysterious, unknown and unknowable processes that lead to one becoming a solar, that resulting sample of the population (Read: the population of individuals who actually DID exalt into solars) tends to favor people who, in the right light, are 'good', whatever that means.</div> </div> </div> </div>What the fuck is the &quot;right light&quot;? And this still doesn't work, as it introduces an objective good. If there's somethign that favors more &quot;good Solars' beyond random, dumb luck having done it this time around, you have in effect said there is a quality of good in the unvierse, evne if it's not demarcatable. But folks WILL try to demarcate it. And apparently all Solars have that quality. This is philosophical poison to the game's premises. It IS saying &quot;You Exalt as a Soalr because you are good&quot; if most Solar Exalted are by some defintion good. Making what defines that vague still is acknowledging it exists as soemthing beyond what humans subjectively claim it is. You again hit the same Euthyphro issue, reworded: Is a Solar good because she is morally good, or is she morally good because the Exaltation dictates what is morraly good? Since there is no objective moral good as defined elsehwere in the setting, Solar Exaltation <i>in itself</i> defines moral goodness. This is untenable in the way the setting works.<br /> <br /> And agian, also outright cans allowing for Conan, Sinbad, Zorayas, Julie dAubigny. If these people are even remotely good, their acts are good in regards to Creation (objectively good for being Solars) or the Solar Exaltation's definitinos of good are bullshit and pointless. Best just not have it give a shit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sylverdyne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89899#post89899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please explain what about the setting breaks if that is true, because I don't think it changes ANYTHING other then how the players and fans approach solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>See above. It is riddled with all sorts of holes when pressed to any decent amount of logic.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T21:36:28-07:00","id":89919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yishten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89912#post89912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> verisimilitude.</div> </div> </div> </div>You used this term, and I have to fight really hard to not immediately dismiss you entire point as pedantry. That my be due to the D&amp;D edition war, but still, pointing that out.<br /> <br /> On what you actually said, ignoring the useless argument word, I dispute that it actually IS changing the primary theme of the presentation. All of the subtext that implies the more complex, detailed realistic political shit is still there. It's just not shoved in your face. See the giant quote form SLS earlier in the thread for a much better summation of this phenomenon as I have experienced it.<br /> <br /> My point is, if you need gigantic signs in your text saying 'SUBTEXT HERE PAY ATTENTION!!!11!' then you don't actually think it's subtext, you think it should be text. If THAT'S what you're saying, Yishten, then we have a broader issue to debate then the superficial obvious presentation of Solar Exaltation.<br /> <br /> Again, to clarify my position, I beleive that, back in 1e from my own reading of that book, Solars were presented as usually decent, good, inspiring people, by and large. I found that this held true through caste books even. Of course there were exceptions, but those were fairly obviously outliers, there to prove the rule, as it were, and to make it clear that exaltation was not simple. The subtext you claim to be so integral to the theme of the splat, and the game, and to provide your 'verisimilitude' was always there, just not spelled out explicitly in the text. It worked out alright for me at the time, and that's really all I can provide legitimate data for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/206-sylverdyne","name":"Sylverdyne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar206_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T21:58:57-07:00","id":89935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89910#post89910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is part of your hang-up. You're creating a false dichotomy. You are first accepting hippokrene's intial (and argued to be false) definition of heroism as inherent &quot;goodness&quot; (whatever the fuck that actually even means beyond &quot;I as a 21st Century Western Wrold person thinks is good&quot;). And since we say it is not inherently good, you then claim it means they are particularly villainous. You don't actually build the bridge of logic to cross that gap.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok I will concede that good isn\u2019t the right word for the defining characteristic I\u2019m trying to describe. But I don\u2019t think a simple will to do great things is enough either. I think a Solar should have some element of positive virtue guiding their actions at the moment of exaltation, or their exaltation should instill that virtue in them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89910#post89910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not &quot;more interested in the villainous potentila of Solars more than their heroic.&quot; I think &quot;Solars are good guys always&quot; is juevenile, against the source material, and both intellectually and philosophically lazy and boring. I'm not interested in the &quot;darker potential of Solars&quot; and more in the actual potential of humanity. Humans are inherently flawed and can do bad things. It's not the job a magic doo-dad to limit their potential to do these at a certain scale.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I agree with you on this. After gaining their exaltation I don\u2019t think there should be anything stopping them from becoming a black hearted despot, or the drug addled prince of an opium ring. These are interesting parts of human nature to explore. I don\u2019t want the \u201cmagic doo-dad\u201d that is a exaltation to limit players from heading in these directions, I do think the \u201cdoo-dad\u201d wouldn\u2019t chose them to become exalts if they were already there. I have played with people who made a Solar who was amoral from the very start and I think it is the easy path, you have no moral boundaries to play within and no expectations to make decisions that could negatively effect your character because they are the right thing to do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89910#post89910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're pulling the false dichotomy shit again. I'm not interested in &quot;villainous&quot; or &quot;heroic&quot; or &quot;good&quot; people for Solars. I'm interested in <i>great</i> people. And the itneresting people of fiction and history that Solar Exalted draw upon are going to be more nuanced than a simple villain/rogue virtue/vice thing. You get that in most any other fantasy setting (lots of the ones with anti-heroes even more or less treat them as working on these alignment stuff your working off of).</div> </div> </div> </div>Heroes can very often be rash, vain, hot-tempered, and prideful, but I would argue that this is not the defining element of their character as a hero. It is their bravery, skill, wisdom, and strength that make heroes heroic, their flaws are something to be overcome or inversely overwhelmed by, but they should not be the basis of a hero\u2019s character.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89910#post89910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea that Solars don't eventually become people with lots of power and no responsiblity to use it wisely, as a note, is ab it of a foundation to the entire Usurpation. You undermine a lot when you make &quot;Solars can do bad things because people do bad things and Solars aren't normal people but a subset of them&quot;. And you cut off a lot of people who are really just htere doing big stuff. I again cite Conan, Sinbad and Achilles in the case of ficiton, or Oda Nobunaga, Genghis Khan or Julius Caesar in the case of history. People who, by your defintions of hero are not &quot;good enough&quot; to be Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say all these examples you gave both fictional and historical have potential to be Solars. The only problem I have with the case of the historical power players becoming Solars is that we know very little of their true mindsets in why they did what they did. If they would as quickly do terrible things as they would do magnificent things, simply to increase their personal power and importance, I think that should preclude them from becoming a solar. I would like to think the Unconquered Sun has a better perspective on someone\u2019s nature than us mere mortals and could weed out those who are only in it for themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89910#post89910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aesha, literally the very first Solar Exalt we ever see, draws a group of soldiers into a shadowland to be slaughtered, kills two Dragon-Blooded and steals their shit with an intention of selling it to fund her escape from the city. We have no idea of her background beyond growing up in that city (and seems not really intent on &quot;fixing&quot; it ever). Unless genocide against people from the Blessed Isle or funding a scavenger's coffers is &quot;good&quot;, she's not really any or less moral than some of the characters I note above.<br /> <br /> Dace goes after Ma-Ha-Suchi, that's heroic, but that's monster slaying in general. Evne Conan slayed monsters, though Dace is a nice guy overall. He still is a sellsword, as a note, so how much hired soldier is an upright good thing is antoher matter. Profiteering I would think by modern standards is not continued very moral. That's about it. Harmonious Jade robs a tomb (good for her), Swan tricks a wood spider (who is going to fuck someone less clever over later on), Panther became good by Exalting, not Exalt for being good (and we haven't seen more than what I would say is a caricature of actual abolitionism personally). And I for the life of me can't actually remember what the fuck Arianna's ficiton is about. So you read a very different set of fiction pieces about Solars than I did.<br /> <br /> Also, the Usurpation was a thing and there's at least some pretense that Chejob actually thought he did the right thing, unless you want to paint the Sidereals as a bunch of scheming power-grabbing viziers and the Solars were actually good kings with a bad rap.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I open the core book the first Solars I see are the signature circle, who save a village from an enraged river god, temper their response when they learn the true reasons for his attack, and hunt down the rapist bandits who started the problems in the first place. In fact every single chapter comic in the book that features a Solar presents them doing virtuous and dare I say good things. Yes their methods may sometimes be questionable, and their personalities flawed, but I still believe that there is some positive element at the centre of all their actions. Though maybe the signature circle are nicer than the average solar.<br /> In regards to the Usurpation, I in no way want to make something similar impossible from happening again by the very nature of a Solar exaltation. What I am suggesting however is that the vast majority of first age Solars would have started their journey as virtuous people because that should be a criteria for becoming a solar in the first place. Certainly they can have flaws but that shouldn\u2019t be the driving force of their being.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89910#post89910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think such a view is showing your holding onto too black and white a moral view in general. It was asked, but would you be okay with Howard's Conan never being a Solar then? Because Sinbad never really wanted to do anything but travel and get rich, he's not a good guy either right? Just a leader to men's deaths, a cuthroat merchant and in a few cases outright murderer? Is it okay because he's the protagonist? What's the line, and why does the Exaltation get to draw it instead of just letting people be people and draw it as their actions seem logcial to dictate? That's actual drama of humans and characters worthy of being like those in history and legend in my opinion instead of something in the young adult section of the bookstore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sinbad probably wouldn\u2019t make a very good Solar, he was a great leader, but he only led men to further his own greed and lust for adventure, his redeeming qualities are few and far between. If anything Sinbad would be an awesome Infernal. Conan however is different matter, yes he is a violent carouser, but he cares for the men under his command, and aspires to be a great king, not because he simply wants power, but because he truly believes he can be a great king. I think a Solar exaltation should be able to discern this distinction because it is modeled on the most powerful being in the setting who is himself the very avatar of perfect virtue. Even the Unconquered Sun has his flaws, but only a fool would dare say he has no virtue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89910#post89910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And we're arguing that's what all sorts of other &quot;hero reborn&quot; plots do anyhow. Or superhero plots. Or really most fantasy plots with non esplicit anti-heroes (who in a weird way do that anyhow). We want characters who are humans, not some whitewashed view of &quot;The best of humanity.&quot; I will also note that such a want for Solars, and Solars only has other problems. Mainly in making opposing Solars in general or preventing them in happening at all is casting any Exalt opposing a Solar as opposing a person who was at least inherently good to start. Which makes a Solar's antagonists easily evil. WHich is kind of damaging for all sorts of reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again I\u2019m all for characters with depth and flaws, it adds interest to the game. All I\u2019m suggesting it that we are playing a game called Exalted in which Solars are the living embodiment of the most noble and perfect god. I do not think it is too unfair to suggest that virtue and maybe even some level of inherent goodness should be expected from those he chooses.<br /> <br /> Sorry if this seems like an attack on everything you said, you just made so many points and I wanted to make sure I clarified what my views were in return. I honestly don\u2019t think there is too much of a gap in our viewpoints, it just seems that the last little distance is a vat of Vitriol or maybe a wall of Orichalcum.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","user":"turkeygiant","date":". 03-13-2014, 01:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T21:59:24-07:00","id":89937,"title":"","content":"Blaque, the mistake you make is that there is some sort of objective category of things that makes you qualify somehow for solar exaltation. There is not. Mr. Morke has been very clear on this in the past. The reason I dismiss you long, well written rebuttal is because your initial premise is functionally irrelevant.<br /> <br /> Feel free to correct me, but your entire argument hinges on the assumption that I, or Hippokrene for that matter, is arguing for an objective good, and that we wish to set such an objective category as a restriction on some absolute qualification for exaltation. Simply put, NO. Allow me to repeat, no, that is not my position, and I do not believe it was the original position presented in first post.<br /> <br /> I am arguing for a change in the manner in which the solar exalted are presented, in an attempt to effect a change in the way they are perceived in the broader audience. First, there are no hard, or even implied conditions for exaltation. I find that putting forth such conditions was one of the stupidest things that 2e did, but that is neither here nor there. I agree with the impression I have received from the lead developer in his posts on this forum and elsewhere is that he wishes for exaltation to be a miracle. That means that it is, inherently, inexplicable. You cannot categorize it in any detail. You can draw some vague tendencies from studying the population, but there will always be those who seem to match your tendencies perfectly who do not exalt, and those who seem to run completely counter to them who will.<br /> <br /> Second, I am not arguing for a change in the way that they are perceived within the game world. I am arguing for a change in the way they are presented to us, the player. I trust you understand the difference? Insofar as my support for this, again, I reference the post by SLS quoted up thread, and numerous other posts by Mr. Morke and Mr. Shearer elsewhere on this forum, the old forum, and elsewhere on the internet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/206-sylverdyne","name":"Sylverdyne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar206_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T22:06:39-07:00","id":89940,"title":"","content":"Changing what is presented to the player <i>is</i> changing the setting. The setting is defined and shaped by what you give to the readers of the book. You can't change what the player is shown without changing the content of the setting, because the former is supposed to represent the latter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Once, there was a maiden... who spent all her time on the internet.<br /> &quot;Someone out there is WRONG,&quot; she said.<br /> So she tossed a noose made of golden light... and strangled her opponent.<br /> Both of them died alone.<br /> &quot;Love is for football players and cheerleaders,&quot; her obituary said.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/261-notthepenguins","name":"notthepenguins","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar261_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"359"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T22:16:16-07:00","id":89949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Calboon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89913#post89913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You bring this point up again and I still do not understand it. Why does the fact a Solar is a good person automatically make their opposition evil? Just looking it over it comes off as a rather simplistic moral outlook where conflict can only arise between &quot;bad&quot; or evil&quot; people, So just to be clear why can't two good people get into a conflict with each other that could potentially burn a country to the ground or shake the heavens? If we know that one is a good person why can't the other one be a good person as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is based on a bit on how probabiltiy works in logic and reasonabilty.<br /> <br /> If &quot;goodness' (again, whatever the fuck that is) is a criterion of Solar Exaltation, than there's a higher likelihood a Solar is good. So in more complicated speak:<br /> <br /> Pr(Good|Solar) = Solars - n/Solars, where &quot;n&quot; is how many are bad (since you start good at Exalting and have to &quot;go bad&quot; from there). <br /> <br /> Pr(Good|Anything Else) = m/ANything Else. Note that instead of being the total number (your group of choice) minus the bad people, you have a baseline that's neither good or bad, and have to work up the genuinely good people. <br /> <br /> So take Solars and Lunars. Assume 150 Solars and 300 Lunars. Say about 10% of Solars are these exceptions we tlak about (high apparently by some views). This emans the chance of a Solar being a good person is:<br /> <br /> Pr(Good|Solar) = 135/150 = 90%<br /> <br /> Take the Lunar Exalted, who apparently run on normal human standards, so are good or bad probably 50/50. But apparently being good is &quot;actively good&quot; as defiend so far. So much rarer. But I'll be generous and say 40%. So with Lunars, this means:<br /> Pr(Good|Lunar) = 120/300 = 40%<br /> <br /> So here's a bit of math for you.<br /> <br /> The likelihood of things being a specific combination are their percentages multiplied. SO this means that in a match-up. We have a field of total match-ups too. Whether the Solar/Lunar is good/bad. We need to do some maths, but with 450 Exalts, this means your chance of being a Solar is 1/3, versus a Lunar's 2/3. 33% v. 66%.<br /> <br /> With the total percentages above, this amounts to:<br /> <br /> Good Solars: 29.7% of the pool.<br /> Bad Solars: 3.3% of the pool.<br /> Good Luanrs: 26.4% of the pool.<br /> Bad Lunars: 39.6% of the pool.<br /> <br /> So suddenly bad Lunars are more common than anything else. This is with generous numbers of what &quot;good&quot; means. Note that I don't at any point need to make Luanrs 50/50 or really any percentage. We can assume at any given time, Lunars are a random sampling of humanity, and due to such a small population, a fairly lopsided one at that. But wait, gets better!<br /> <br /> How probable is for these to be good v. bad match ups for different combos?<br /> <br /> It goes on. But right now, you can see that you're more likely to encounter a bad Lunar than a Solar. This is due to greater numbers of Lunars, sure. But note also you are more likely to hit a Good Solar than a good Lunar despite this. <br /> <br /> This is what I'm getting at. Solars with &quot;goodness&quot; as a criterion, and being bad as a rare event, will have a huge skew like this. Other Exalts or supernaturals having no such criterion, will have no minimum and are at whims of normal human statistics, which can vary wildly.<br /> <br /> This opens up both for a &quot;Well he glows gold, so he's probably good&quot; issue, whcih is bad. This is a &quot;he's not gold, so he's more likely to be bad&quot;, which is statistically a reasonable position. And it means that in most conflicts (whcih I have to think the math out on but its' 1:13 am here and i need to get to bed) are going to be more often Solars v. Bad Exalts isntead of Solars v. Good Exalts. So it is often likely that the Solar is the good guy and so gets to be right in her choice. Even if she's not, she's got likelihood on her side.<br /> <br /> TL;DR: If Solars get 'being good' as a criterion, everyone else is less liekly to be good than Solars, therefore, Solar are the most good Exalt. Which is bullshit, as this isnt' a fucking &quot;color coded for your convenience&quot; comic book or cartoon show.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T22:38:37-07:00","id":89967,"title":"","content":"What about the likelihood of becoming terribly corrupt soon after exalting Solar? Unlike all the other exalt types there is no large, long-standing support structure to help them deal with it. You were a pig farmer, now you're a god-king, go! Dragonblooded are already the corrupt power block of the world, and the Sidereals/Lunars have their respective groups which you are always taken into or branded an outlaw. You have somebody watching out to make sure you don't go crazy.<br /> <br /> However with Solars suddenly you have the power to punch that smug satrap right in the face and tell everyone else that this is your kingdom now. Finally the shoe is on the other foot and you can stop anyone from EVER treating you or your friends like that again! I'd say that barring DBs who are more often than not raised in corruption, a Solar has the biggest chance to fall the fastest into tyranny. Contrary to what you might think generally speaking if you give the powerless great power from nowhere they tend less towards using their experience as a downtrodden member of society to inform their choices and more often languish in the new luxuries of their station.<br /> <br /> Not to mention, isn't it more likely that Solars will be going against bad people anyway? DBs are usually bad, with their horrible oppressive empire, Abyssals wade through oceans of blood and Infernals burn with the insane hatred of hell. The only people who are usually not so bad are Sidereals and Lunars.<br /> <br /> The game is already color coded for our convenience. The idea of a kind and sympathetic Abyssal/Infernal is a subversion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T22:47:14-07:00","id":89969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89935#post89935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think a Solar should have some element of positive virtue guiding their actions at the moment of exaltation, or their exaltation should instill that virtue in them.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>And that's the problem. The Solar Exaltation is the will of the UCS empowering a mortal who is destined for greatness. They must have the will to use the power, and will shape history with it. No virtue is connected to it, or does it bring virtue into the soul. It's the UCS giving an awesome person awesome power to do with what they will.<br /> <br /> The most pious and virtuous man ever could be humble and meek, and so he will never be a Solar Exalt. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T22:53:29-07:00","id":89970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Schleiermacher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=88756#post88756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I'm concerned, Lea conclusively settled this issue in this post from 2013 on RPGnet. I agree 100% with what he says:<br /> <br /> (quoted stephenls stuff)</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for bringing that into this thread. I've been made to feel like I'm crazy for reading &quot;Solars are good guys&quot; in the material; the quoted states, explicitly and with a high degree of authority, that that's the intended face-value read. And the subtext that questions it, the notion that wait, are Solars going to really fix anything by being Big Damn Heroes?, that's a big part of what I like about Exalted, but I feel like that subtext has been inflated by the community to define Solars at face value, which Lea says is a bad thing, and puts so eloquently into words why it frustrates me.<br /> <br /> Again, thank you. I've felt like reference to actual facts and quotes has been incredibly sparse in this thread, and by defying that trend you have made my day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2404-chant","name":"Chant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2404_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T22:54:32-07:00","id":89972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89969#post89969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And that's the problem. The Solar Exaltation is the will of the UCS empowering a mortal who is destined for greatness. They must have the will to use the power, and will shape history with it. No virtue is connected to it, or does it bring virtue into the soul. It's the UCS giving an awesome person awesome power to do with what they will.<br /> <br /> The most pious and virtuous man ever could be humble and meek, and so he will never be a Solar Exalt.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not excluding the potential for greatness as a necessary trait to become a Solar, I just think that they should start with a good helping of virtue as well to begin with. Whether they nourish that virtue or let it wither is up to them, self determination is another one of the inherent traits of the Solar. I don't think the Unconquered sun would give a exaltation to someone who doesn't share at least some affinity to his versions of virtues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","user":"turkeygiant","date":". 03-13-2014, 01:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T22:55:55-07:00","id":89973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89935#post89935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok I will concede that good isn\u2019t the right word for the defining characteristic I\u2019m trying to describe. But I don\u2019t think a simple will to do great things is enough either. I think a Solar should have some element of positive virtue guiding their actions at the moment of exaltation, or their exaltation should instill that virtue in them.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is &quot;positive virtue&quot; here? All you're doing is relabeling the qualitative trait. Virtues in Creation aren't even themselves &quot;postiive or negative&quot;, they're just Virtues. And SOlars already have Virtues in their characters. And high Virtue is not in itself good. Achilles was an asshole, remember. And Aristotle (whom we get a lot of the thematics of Virtues for) saw it more as balance than some positive or negative context. Everyone has them, it's how well they manage them, which is divorced form good/bad or positive by-the nose shit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89935#post89935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I agree with you on this. After gaining their exaltation I don\u2019t think there should be anything stopping them from becoming a black hearted despot, or the drug addled prince of an opium ring. These are interesting parts of human nature to explore. I don\u2019t want the \u201cmagic doo-dad\u201d that is a exaltation to limit players from heading in these directions, I do think the \u201cdoo-dad\u201d wouldn\u2019t chose them to become exalts if they were already there. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? And what is that going to be besides some arbitrary case of the Sun who decided he didnt like a person, and what justification does he have beyond his personal opinion? ANd why should that be considered good or bad or anything of note besides whether or not the Sun liked you? And why shouldn't the motherfucking opium Godfather not be a potential Solar? Because you don't like the guy still doesn't demonstrate why he shouldn't be able to be allowed to have a narrative of power and might.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89935#post89935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... I have played with people who made a Solar who was amoral from the very start and I think it is the easy path, you have no moral boundaries to play within and no expectations to make decisions that could negatively effect your character because they are the right thing to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems to me to be an issue i see with RPGs in general. Some people are actually so divorced form their characters or the setting they would maek a chracter like this anyhow. Moral boundries won't impact someone going and making amoral characters from the start, I feel. And a game that on the onset has no objective morality, no consistent way can be done to apply such moral boundries without in a way saying those are an objective thing of the world independent of the beings in it. It also leads to you imparting <i>your</i> views on a world that might actually not find so repulsive. There were folks in the Opium Wars who probably thought the entire exercise was moral and heroic and viruteous and good for their homelands. An especially successful pusher is probably just fine for Exaltation. You might find him abhorent, but that's your views of what's right and wrong impacting a world that doens't share those views and it shoulnd't. The best way to avoid this is not even let it into the system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89935#post89935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heroes can very often be rash, vain, hot-tempered, and prideful, but I would argue that this is not the defining element of their character as a hero. It is their bravery, skill, wisdom, and strength that make heroes heroic, their flaws are something to be overcome or inversely overwhelmed by, but they should not be the basis of a hero\u2019s character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bullshit. Heracles is who he was because he lost his temper. Achilles and Sinbad are who they are due to their flaws (being thrill-seeking asses). Zorayas would of been some nobody crippled priestess in a cave if she didn't decide she was going to conquer the world and fuck anyone who got in her way. And these characters to some extent fell or ended their careers at times due to acts of folly. Achilles is known as an example of heroes taken low as much as he is a hero. Liu Bei has been talked about a lot already as a great example of his flaws defining a lot of who he is.<br /> <br /> Character flaws aren't just challenges to overcome. They're as much part of a character as his or her strengths and add as much to her profile as her strengths do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89935#post89935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say all these examples you gave both fictional and historical have potential to be Solars. The only problem I have with the case of the historical power players becoming Solars is that we know very little of their true mindsets in why they did what they did. If they would as quickly do terrible things as they would do magnificent things, simply to increase their personal power and importance, I think that should preclude them from becoming a solar. I would like to think the Unconquered Sun has a better perspective on someone\u2019s nature than us mere mortals and could weed out those who are only in it for themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Zorayas didnt' get power until she decided to become sorceress queen. Sinbad didn't get rich until he led hudnreds to their deaths on his voyages. Conan outright states in &quot;The Black Colossus&quot; that if he and his mercenaries don't get paid in a budget cut, they're going to loot the damned city and he does this with not a tinge of guilt. <br /> <br /> With historical people, sure, we can't get into their head. But their stories and legends are what matter. And trying to have their good acheivements withotu acknowledging their flaws or their mistakes is just creating a cartoon caricature of the person. We odn't know how rash Nobunaga was but it looks like no one liked working for him (he was an asshole and he had cups made of fucking skulls). We don't know what motivated her, but Julie d'Aubigny doesn't seem like she ever did anything but be a rash crazyperson but she's probably a great Zenith, Night or Dawn character.<br /> <br /> So no, I disagree with any of this. What still matters to me shoudl be deeds and ability to do them. Nothing else can even be measured consistently I feel. Or even as you're showing, without suddenly making modern prefences Creation's truths.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89935#post89935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I open the core book the first Solars I see are the signature circle, ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, so the comic. I'm basing things ont he 1e corebook. WHich you know, had the opening fiction have a Solar personally defeat a Wyld Hunt's two Dragon-Blooded, steal a daiklave and think of selling the bits to leave town. It was a bit less....cartoony in 1e. And what I generally draw on for what I am talking about. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89935#post89935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In regards to the Usurpation, I in no way want to make something similar impossible from happening again by the very nature of a Solar exaltation. What I am suggesting however is that the vast majority of first age Solars would have started their journey as virtuous people because that should be a criteria for becoming a solar in the first place. Certainly they can have flaws but that shouldn\u2019t be the driving force of their being.</div> </div> </div> </div>This invalidates part of the Usurpation though. If all Solars are good to start, why the Jade Prison? Why not just Ender's Game that shit now that you have a clean slate to work with? It's inconherent and still more or less says that Solars werne't given a chance and that modern attempts to stop Solars more or less is working against &quot;Really good people most of the time.&quot; Instead of the general actual mindset is that the kind fo person that becomes a SOlar is a powerful person. And powerful people with out checks do things powerful people do, for better or ill.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89935#post89935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sinbad probably wouldn\u2019t make a very good Solar, he was a great leader, but he only led men to further his own greed and lust for adventure, his redeeming qualities are few and far between. If anything Sinbad would be an awesome Infernal.</div> </div> </div> </div>He survied seven voyages. He integrated (and married) many culture.s He saw the world, and saw dozens of people. He was a sailer, a businessman, an admiral and a pretty nice guy to the kid wanting to talk with him. He's a great Solar. He's probably one of the best Eclipse examples out there (mostly all the Abilites, including Ride with giant birds). That he was a greedy asshole somehow disqualifies him and makes him an Infernal to me proves my point. In what way is wha the does not supernal feats of human skill and drive to use that skill? Why should his being a thrillseeking asshole somehow bar him? Because you dont' liek him? And why does Infernal suddenly click? Because being a &quot;bad guy&quot; is all green for other Exalt types? Do you not see the issue here? Is it really in the end, &quot;Your anima = your alignment?&quot; Because at face value, that's what this says to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89935#post89935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conan however is different matter, yes he is a violent carouser, but he cares for the men under his command, and aspires to be a great king, not because he simply wants power, but because he truly believes he can be a great king. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of this isn't the case, as a note, until his competence gets him into ranks of positon, long after a career defined of being a self-serving gloryseeking brute. And while he cares for his men, he doenst' do a lot of good of keeping them alive. And he's a good king it seems for benig good at being a king. He didnt' seem to think through how to get to that job.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89935#post89935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... I think a Solar exaltation should be able to discern this distinction because it is modeled on the most powerful being in the setting who is himself the very avatar of perfect virtue. Even the Unconquered Sun has his flaws, but only a fool would dare say he has no virtue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but his Virtue makes him a contrarian crazyperson who still mostly gets to define what's just and right becuase he says so based on how he feels at a given time. And well, part of where we are is apparently he valued his view of things more than loyalty.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89935#post89935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again I\u2019m all for characters with depth and flaws, it adds interest to the game. All I\u2019m suggesting it that we are playing a game called Exalted in which Solars are the living embodiment of the most noble and perfect god. I do not think it is too unfair to suggest that virtue and maybe even some level of inherent goodness should be expected from those he chooses.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a big chunk of the point of the Sun is that for someone so noble and perfect, <i>he himself is also flawed</i>. If the Most High is not without flaws, no one should be expected to also be. Virute is expected: Too much of it is poison to the mind. And virtueousness =/= goodness. It just means virtueousness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89935#post89935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry if this seems like an attack on everything you said, you just made so many points and I wanted to make sure I clarified what my views were in return. I honestly don\u2019t think there is too much of a gap in our viewpoints, it just seems that the last little distance is a vat of Vitriol or maybe a wall of Orichalcum.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not distance. I honestly think you're wrong, and while you seem to be claiming that you don't think Exalted will end up wiht objective morality in this, you have failed to show how this is the case still. <br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T22:58:57-07:00","id":89976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89969#post89969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The most pious and virtuous man ever could be humble and meek, and so he will never be a Solar Exalt.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Humble and meek doesn't necessarily mean &quot;unwilling to act when the chips are down&quot; A lot of real world heroes - those people who pull a person from a burning car, those kids who drive their mothers suffering diabetic shock - are pretty humble people, at least in the interviews.<br /> <br /> And I think it's the will to act when it &quot;counts&quot; that makes a hero, and what calls the attention of the Unconquered Sun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a Woman, I'm a GM. <i>Of course</i> I'm Evil.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/424-dawaterrat","name":"DaWaterRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T23:00:49-07:00","id":89978,"title":"","content":"I have the feeling that this entire discussion will be rendered completely moot when 3E comes out, and we have a clear definition of what kind of people become what kind of Exalt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T23:02:03-07:00","id":89979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89972#post89972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not excluding the potential for greatness as a necessary trait to become a Solar, I just think that they should start with a good helping of virtue as well to begin with. Whether they nourish that virtue or let it wither is up to them, self determination is another one of the inherent traits of the Solar.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm saying they shouldn't. If they are virtuous it's because their goal as an awesome person is virtuous, but they were chosen because they were awesome, not virtiuous. An awesome bastard whose goal is to wreck everyones shit, will exalt just as likely, because he is awesome. What should be required for a Solar, is a cause or motivation, why they will use the metaphysical gun called the Solar Exaltation. It doesn't matter if that great cause is building up or burning down all the orphanages, so to speak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T23:16:32-07:00","id":89983,"title":"","content":"I'd also like to point out that for a game setting that's making absolutely sure that the solar exaltation has nothing whatsoever at all to do with morals...the scroll of exalts is remarkably lopsided. Almost none of the infernals or abyssals are even close to pleasant, most of them cartoonish evil in every imaginable way. The Solar exalted on the other hand have got like..Arianna kind of, Elias maybe a tiny bit due to his ignorance? Faka Kun a bit because of her thievery from the wealthy to give to the poor I guess. Mirror Flag possibly depending on interpretation?<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure that the general idea given by the books already is that Solars are generally pretty cool people, who at the best are upstanding, generous, sympathetic people, and at the worst are people who are angry and only want what's best for their people. With a very few exceptions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T23:17:05-07:00","id":89984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89949#post89949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This opens up both for a &quot;Well he glows gold, so he's probably good&quot; issue, whcih is bad. This is a &quot;he's not gold, so he's more likely to be bad&quot;, which is statistically a reasonable position. And it means that in most conflicts (whcih I have to think the math out on but its' 1:13 am here and i need to get to bed) are going to be more often Solars v. Bad Exalts isntead of Solars v. Good Exalts. So it is often likely that the Solar is the good guy and so gets to be right in her choice. Even if she's not, she's got likelihood on her side.</div> </div> </div> </div>The number of abjectly terrible assumptions you've made and failed to make explicit is really frustrating, here.<br /> <br /> First: your emphasis on how likely a bad guy is to be a given Exalt type gives no notice to the fact that if you pin down Solars as good guys, and you <i>don't</i> pin down anyone else in any way, then you automatically have fewer bad guys, total. Which means that Lunars aren't any worse than a regular person, nor any worse than they would be if Solars were statistically amoral. Of course, I don't even have to argue that point, because your analysis is predicated on precisely that.<br /> <br /> Second: you make a fallacious leap of logic that assumes that the converse of a statement is true, which an Intro to Logic level mistake. Specifically, you take the statement &quot;most bad guys are Lunars&quot; and turn it into &quot;most Lunars are bad guys&quot;. I really don't like how hostile it makes me sound to point this out, but you <i>can't do that</i> if you're trying to make a logically consistent argument.<br /> <br /> Third: you arbitrarily limit your analysis to Exalts. Aren't there bad guys who are gods, and heroic mortals, and raksha, etc. etc.?<br /> <br /> Fourth: you seem to predicate your conclusion on the notion that good can only come into conflict with bad, and vice versa. Exalted is a setting which offers a lot of moral complexity, and a good Solar (who is good because he wants to end slavery) can fight against a good Sidereal (who is good because he wants to ensure the insanity of the Solars never brings the world into peril again) without the &quot;good&quot; of either being diminished.<br /> <br /> To illustrate the absurdity of your analysis, I pose an alternate proposition, which I neither believe nor intend to defend: All Exalted are good. By the methods you've demonstrated, this assertion is impossible to analyse. It breaks down where you try to tabulate the likelihood of a bad guy being a member of each Exalt type. You get a 0% probability across the board, and the conclusion is that bad guys don't exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2404-chant","name":"Chant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2404_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T23:20:27-07:00","id":89985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sylverdyne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89937#post89937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Feel free to correct me, but your entire argument hinges on the assumption that I, or Hippokrene for that matter, is arguing for an objective good, and that we wish to set such an objective category as a restriction on some absolute qualification for exaltation. Simply put, NO. Allow me to repeat, no, that is not my position, and I do not believe it was the original position presented in first post.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Let me requote:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In the sense that they are good people performing good deeds in order to make the world a better place. ...<br /> <br /> Some Solars will not be heroes, but those are exceptions.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">... As I said, there are exceptions, but they need to be treated as such. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>She's doing a simple thing here:<br /> P1: Solars are heroes.<br /> P2: Heroes are defined as &quot;good people performing good deeds in order to make the world a better place.&quot;<br /> C: Solars are &quot;good people performing good deeds in order to make the world a better place.&quot;<br /> <br /> This is a valid arguement. It is an unsound one. Premise 2 is false. It is false because heroism in Exalted isn't about good people. It's about great people. And it is impossible for it to be true, as &quot;good people performing good deeds in order to make the world a better place.&quot; is a meaningless term in a world where ther eis no objective good. Anything that is a good deed performed for good is often declared that post-hoc. And what is one man's good is ofthen antoher man's evil. So it is contradictory and useless a descriptor anyhow.<br /> <br /> On top of this, she then says that Solar Exalted who aren't heroes as she's defined them should be highlighted as exceptions and aberrant. The only way for this to happen is that there is some process within Exaltion to let this happen, as heroic is not her defintion of heroic. If it is, it makes Solar Exaltation able to select &quot;good people performing good deeds in order to make the world a better place.&quot; And since it does it in a way that is apparently not contradictary, it knows what that is. It turns Solar Exlatation in the good-guy-finder.<br /> <br /> What I'm doing is a bit of reductio ad absurdum. I am granting her her case. And showing that if it is her case, it leads to an absurd consequence if logically followed. Mainly:<br /> <br /> P1) Assume Solars are good people and non good Solars are an exception.<br /> P2) This is apparently independent of random sampling of humanity, which is a mix of good and not good.<br /> P3) So Solar Exaltations somehow select, as it is not random human goodness at work.<br /> P4) This means Solar Exaltations know what's good.<br /> P5) But there is no objective good in Creation. This is a contradiction.<br /> C) P1 can't be true as it leads to a contradiction. <br /> <br /> Her defintion of heroic breaks the setting if applied how she thinks it should be applied to Solars. Therefore, it is a poor definition to use for describing Solar Exalted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sylverdyne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89937#post89937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am arguing for a change in the manner in which the solar exalted are presented, in an attempt to effect a change in the way they are perceived in the broader audience. First, there are no hard, or even implied conditions for exaltation. I find that putting forth such conditions was one of the stupidest things that 2e did, but that is neither here nor there. I agree with the impression I have received from the lead developer in his posts on this forum and elsewhere is that he wishes for exaltation to be a miracle. That means that it is, inherently, inexplicable. You cannot categorize it in any detail. You can draw some vague tendencies from studying the population, but there will always be those who seem to match your tendencies perfectly who do not exalt, and those who seem to run completely counter to them who will.</div> </div> </div> </div>But apparently one of those tendencies is finding some sort of &quot;good people&quot;. Which means that whatever mysteries there are in the proces,s there's soemthing in there that has a good chance of finding goodness. Which means goodness is a quantity that htey can find or that the unvierse likes to give powers to. This feels like shifting the problem to the gaps. It's still a problem. And as few criterion as possible allows for the broadest membership to the Solar Host with most story potentila. &quot;They all are good save exceptions&quot; is not a good criterion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sylverdyne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89937#post89937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, I am not arguing for a change in the way that they are perceived within the game world. I am arguing for a change in the way they are presented to us, the player. I trust you understand the difference? Insofar as my support for this, again, I reference the post by SLS quoted up thread, and numerous other posts by Mr. Morke and Mr. Shearer elsewhere on this forum, the old forum, and elsewhere on the internet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you fundementally misunderstand SLS' post. He is arguing for nuance in balacing text and subtext as I read it. The subtext not being beaten over your head doesn't mean its not there and in the end the idea of heroism as goodness is still bullshit. Whitewashing Solars and then going really loud that the ones that don't follow the text are DOing it Wrong is more or less tossing out the subtext, not balancing it. In 1e there was no statement of Havesh or Lyta or Fehim or Moray or Nimiun ro Mirror Flag's goodness or badness or exceptional meanness. THey were just there and left for others to ponder what that meant that they got to be Exalts too. <br /> <br /> That's balancing text and subtext. Not going and trying to play up the good and villainis ethe bad.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T23:38:33-07:00","id":89994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89973#post89973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not distance. I honestly think you're wrong, and while you seem to be claiming that you don't think Exalted will end up wiht objective morality in this, you have failed to show how this is the case still.<br /> <br /> And stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand that every person in the world has a different view on what constitutes good and evil some of them widely different. I also believe however that there is a lot more agreement than there is disparity in these views. I would even be willing to believe that despite whatever you may say we very likely have very similar views on what we personally determine to be actions that are good and evil.<br /> <br /> A General who wages a brutal and bloody war against the evil empire because he wishes to free his people from tyrannical oppression is a good man, his motivation is drawn from virtue and goodness.<br /> <br /> A General who wages a brutal and bloody war against the evil empire because he gains sadistic pleasure from seeing blood spilled on the sand is a evil man, his motivation is drawn from vice and evilness.<br /> <br /> Yes things are not always so clear cut there are many shades of grey. All I am saying is that their should be a requirement of at the very least some virtue or goodness from a potential Solar. You can say I don't get to define goodness all you want, but I do, I define what is Good and Evil every day of my life and so do you. I'm even okay with a character who deludes themselves into thinking they are doing good when the rest of the world would disagree if they truly believe it, but a psychopath doesn't think they are doing good, they simply do not care that they are doing evil, the concept is foreign to them and i think that should preclude them from being a Solar. I don't think every Solar needs to be wholly virtuous, half virtuous, or even just a little virtuous, all I know is there must be some small grain of virtue there or the exaltation would not and should not go to them.<br /> <br /> Saying we cant call a empire apples red because some people are colour blind just doesn't work for me. I am entirely willing to establish subjective defnitions of good and evil if i know the majority of people will agree with me. And I think adding even a little goodness into the make up of every Solar in the moment they exalt will in no way cause the system to implode in on itself in a philosophical black-hole.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure I have any more to add to this without spinning in circles and circles and circles, so I am now going to slowly walk away from the thread.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T00:42:25-07:00","id":90017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89983#post89983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd also like to point out that for a game setting that's making absolutely sure that the solar exaltation has nothing whatsoever at all to do with morals...the scroll of exalts is remarkably lopsided. Almost none of the infernals or abyssals are even close to pleasant, most of them cartoonish evil in every imaginable way. The Solar exalted on the other hand have got like..Arianna kind of, Elias maybe a tiny bit due to his ignorance? Faka Kun a bit because of her thievery from the wealthy to give to the poor I guess. Mirror Flag possibly depending on interpretation?<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure that the general idea given by the books already is that Solars are generally pretty cool people, who at the best are upstanding, generous, sympathetic people, and at the worst are people who are angry and only want what's best for their people. With a very few exceptions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah it does a very crappy job. The difference between the origins of a Solar, Abyssal, and Infernal shouldn't be good/evil. It should be exalting doing something awesome, exalting trying to do something awesome and dying, and exalting trying to doing something awesome and failing. Further thematics comes from the nature of each Exaltation and not their morality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T00:45:26-07:00","id":90020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89994#post89994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> All I am saying is that their should be a requirement of at the very least some virtue or goodness from a potential Solar.</div> </div> </div> </div>And we're saying no there shouldn't.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T03:15:59-07:00","id":90075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89994#post89994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand that every person in the world has a different view on what constitutes good and evil some of them widely different. I also believe however that there is a lot more agreement than there is disparity in these views. I would even be willing to believe that despite whatever you may say we very likely have very similar views on what we personally determine to be actions that are good and evil.<br /> <br /> A General who wages a brutal and bloody war against the evil empire because he wishes to free his people from tyrannical oppression is a good man, his motivation is drawn from virtue and goodness.<br /> <br /> A General who wages a brutal and bloody war against the evil empire because he gains sadistic pleasure from seeing blood spilled on the sand is a evil man, his motivation is drawn from vice and evilness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the problem: people are capable of committing horrible atrocities for the cause they believe is right. Most crusaders really believed they're on a mission from God to help their brothers and sisters in faith, yet they didn't flinch when that mission turned out to involve genocide. Motivation drawn from virtue and what they perceived as goodness, horrible results.<br /> <br /> I actually agree with you that most people know good from evil for their own use, but I disagree that it can be averaged into a useful, universal standard that everybody can agree upon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T04:34:09-07:00","id":90093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89967#post89967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea of a kind and sympathetic Abyssal/Infernal is a subversion.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this, too, is entirely terrible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T04:42:59-07:00","id":90099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LeTipex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89835#post89835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I wouldn't like to be insulting to anyone you know, I have to say that what you're presenting here seems to be much more of a problem with the way the people you play with view and interpret the game as opposed to a problem with the game itself, and that a lot of people do not have this particular problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is not, however, altogether an uncommon occurence. Like, at all. I've found exactly the same thing happening to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T04:45:51-07:00","id":90102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89983#post89983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure that the general idea given by the books already is that Solars are generally pretty cool people, who at the best are upstanding, generous, sympathetic people, and at the worst are people who are angry and only want what's best for their people. With a very few exceptions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am in agreement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89978#post89978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have the feeling that this entire discussion will be rendered completely moot when 3E comes out, and we have a clear definition of what kind of people become what kind of Exalt.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect that the discussion will continue because it's less us talking about canon and more about our desires and interpretations. Different players want different things from Exalted.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think that's a good thing. I wouldn't want Exalted to be a game for 'hippokrene and people who are exactly like her.'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 03-13-2014, 07:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T05:01:19-07:00","id":90109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90075#post90075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's the problem: people are capable of committing horrible atrocities for the cause they believe is right. Most crusaders really believed they're on a mission from God to help their brothers and sisters in faith, yet they didn't flinch when that mission turned out to involve genocide. Motivation drawn from virtue and what they perceived as goodness, horrible results.<br /> <br /> I actually agree with you that most people know good from evil for their own use, but I disagree that it can be averaged into a useful, universal standard that everybody can agree upon.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Exactly, if you try to define goodness, its not just about motivation. I can have 6 Solars, all motivated to end salvery, but the can't agree on which course of action to take, so they go separate ways.<br /> <br /> The first starts a guerrilla war against slaver bands and slave merchant.<br /> The second solar inserts himself in a position of power and tries modify the law to abolish slavery.<br /> The third slaughters a slaver camp and writes with their blood on the walls the from that point on, anyone wh deals in slaves will die horrible deaths.<br /> The fourth solar visits every slaver leader and organization in creacion and gives them speeches full sorrow that break their hearts and are emotionally compelled to stop trading slaves.<br /> the fifth solar poisons every slaver in creation.<br /> The last one offers money, education and means to start a new bussiness to every slaver willing to end their trade.<br /> <br /> <br /> Are they all good because they want to end slavery?<br /> <br /> ANd what about the solar who aids slavers because he can't have others going on personal walls, modify laws to suits their own agenda, slaughtring legal merchants, mass poisoning an entire proffesion, compelling others against their will, or don't consider the repercutions the end of slavery would have in creation. is he a good exalt or a bad one for condoning slavery.<br /> <br /> I think that this is not a question about heroism and goodness of solars. If we want to reach an agreement we first need to ask a question about goodness in general,<br /> <br /> Is morality in creation relative? are some of the above solars evil?<br /> <br /> Edit: And while we are asking us question, why would any good solar end slavery through violence, if there are clearly many non violent ways to do so?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2245,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2245-quimeradc","user":"Quimeradc","date":". 03-13-2014, 08:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2245-quimeradc","name":"Quimeradc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T05:09:51-07:00","id":90118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sylverdyne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89919#post89919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You used this term, and I have to fight really hard to not immediately dismiss you entire point as pedantry. That my be due to the D&amp;D edition war, but still, pointing that out. On what you actually said, ignoring the useless argument word, I dispute that it actually IS changing the primary theme of the presentation. All of the subtext that implies the more complex, detailed realistic political shit is still there. It's just not shoved in your face. See the giant quote form SLS earlier in the thread for a much better summation of this phenomenon as I have experienced it. My point is, if you need gigantic signs in your text saying 'SUBTEXT HERE PAY ATTENTION!!!11!' then you don't actually think it's subtext, you think it should be text. If THAT'S what you're saying, Yishten, then we have a broader issue to debate then the superficial obvious presentation of Solar Exaltation. Again, to clarify my position, I beleive that, back in 1e from my own reading of that book, Solars were presented as usually decent, good, inspiring people, by and large. I found that this held true through caste books even. Of course there were exceptions, but those were fairly obviously outliers, there to prove the rule, as it were, and to make it clear that exaltation was not simple. The subtext you claim to be so integral to the theme of the splat, and the game, and to provide your 'verisimilitude' was always there, just not spelled out explicitly in the text. It worked out alright for me at the time, and that's really all I can provide legitimate data for.</div> </div> </div> </div> Honestly, if you have issues with a word, I recommend you try reading more dictionaries and fewer forums. I didn't follow any of the D&amp;D nonsense, so I don't know what connotation you've picked up that you've somehow confused with definition, but I don't intend to change my style of picking the most appropriate word I can think of, or trimming English vocabulary, to suit some self-imposed redefinition scheme. If something's going to invalidate an argument, asking for anything like that would be it. <br /> <br /> Insofar as verisimilitude (no quotation marks) means &quot;the seeming of being real,&quot; and insofar as elevating any particular group to being typically and objectively good (and if people are just arguing for subjective good, they're just wasting bytes-- everyone is subjectively good to someone, even if only themselves) harms many people's perception that the setting has any seeming of reality. Especially when the setting contains actual gods that are not-- and no one is arguing should be-- good people. <br /> <br /> So I stand by my statement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/926-yishten","name":"Yishten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar926_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T05:14:04-07:00","id":90126,"title":"","content":"And is not as as easy with motivation either. The same 5 solars can have their &quot;metamotivations&quot; differ a lot:<br /> <br /> I want to end slavery in creation, because slavery is wrong.<br /> <br /> I want to end slavery in creation, because they sold me as a kid and don't that happeing to anyone else.<br /> <br /> I want to end slavery in creation, because i don't like their smell and creatin would be more beautiful without them.<br /> <br /> I want to end slavery in creation, because they sold me as a kid and i want revenge.<br /> <br /> I want to end slavery in creation, because in the long run slavery is bad counterproductive for societies.<br /> <br /> I want to end slavery in creation, because without it my bussiness of highly trained workers will skyrocket and make me rich.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2245,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2245-quimeradc","user":"Quimeradc","date":". 03-13-2014, 08:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2245-quimeradc","name":"Quimeradc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T05:16:18-07:00","id":90129,"title":"","content":"I'm still thinking about a person like Nobunaga, where whether or not he's doing a thing that's &quot;right&quot; is more for society and history to judge, but might not really be the standards he's holding himself to.<br /> <br /> People like to add a bit of edge to their assessments by saying &quot;most people do what they think is good or right or what have you&quot;, but that's not really it; most people don't give profound moral consideration to their actions, and to the extent that Solars do, they're likely to be doing it in accordance with their commensurately greater power, but even then a person really having the perspective that their powers are a big deal that needs to be weighed carefully, that's still unusual (and probably more than a little bit melodramatic).<br /> <br /> I would say that this is because most people aren't really in a situation where their capabilities or decisions are actually in a position to have the kind of impact that makes careful consideration seem warrented, but that's probably the default perspective of people no matter what their place is. Maybe it's a bit different when you've got democratically elected leaders, where the culture and system incorporates the idea that you only have position that you seek out and have validated, but historically most people of power have not been like that, even when they were peasants who rose up to become emperors, and it's certainly not what the Exalted are. Most people view their lives as small, because they can only ever see it from the perspective of one person, and when your life is small you don't guide yourself with onerous moral abstractions, you go with what suits your wants and needs and circumstances.<br /> <br /> This is not to say that people are profoundly selfish, they're often quite the opposite. But when you do things that are helpful for other people, you do it because they're right there in front of you, not because of your adherence to an abstraction. But that also means that what you do comes out of what's around you. What was around a person like Nobunaga was war and destruction and retainers, and that generates motivations to make it safe to go down to the shops for a bit as well as to burn down temples serving as refuges for warrior monks and their protectorates and families.<br /> <br /> The Chosen in Creation are not immaculate philosophers descended from Heaven; they are children in war torn regions given a gun. You are not a bad person. You are not a good person. You're a person amidst a complex and unstable melange of societies, with a random assortment of people around you to drive your motivations and responses. You are your experiences. You are your friends and family. You are your villains. Perfect Soul, despite the ironic name, is not a moral exemplar, she is ruler of a kingdom, she is enemy of House Mnemon, she is Chosen by a god who sympathized with her sense of being abandoned and betrayed that she expressed in a violent denouement. She will do what makes sense as those things play out around her, to the best of her ability to decide what makes sense, not because she's got good intentions but because she can't do nothing and because she can't sit around internally arguing about what best fits some abstraction while things fall apart around her. Sometimes this means comforting and inspiring the beaten down and destitute, and sometimes it means leaving disemboweled Mnemon soldiers outside of a fortress to get them to fuck off.<br /> <br /> The Solars, the Exalted, are heroes, but they're the uneasy, unsanitized kinds of heroes you get in a world that is struggling not to die, right down to how such a world produces people who find more release in wild abandon than in struggling to make sure that there's a tomorrow, or that tomorrow looks better than today, whatever that should happen to look like to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T05:19:09-07:00","id":90134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuddenThunder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89462#post89462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is clearly the case, but I think it might be harming the discussion a little bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd enjoyed the discussion I've read. I don't regard repeating myself as a conversational failure in a 19 page thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuddenThunder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89462#post89462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bLikewise, when you say Solars should be heroes by default you <i>definitively</i> discourage any other sort of play, no matter how much fine print you add afterwards.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes well, as persuasive as I am, I find that if someone is only willing to create PCs that fit a specific thematic default then I don't have much sympathy for them if they dislike the results.<br /> <br /> Lunars are monstrous and draw from a sort of primal/savage aesthetic. If you want to play a sophisticated city dwelling Lunar who is basically a shapechanging Captain America, then you should do that. Dragon-Bloods are a decadent military aristocracy by default. If you want to play a yokel outcaste who bumbles his way from one madcap adventure to another, then you should do that.<br /> <br /> This isn't like Chimerism or the use of Knacks because it's not a mechanical discussion.<br /> <br /> Even if you believe in your heart of hearts that I'm judging you for not playing a paladin Solar, I assume you are secure enough in yourself that lack of my approval doesn't matter when it comes to your PC.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is there anything worth achieving by limiting the thematic space of Solars, in light of the fact that it runs against the material we've been invited to use to anticipate the tone of the new edition? </div> </div> </div>The new edition seems to embrace the characterization of Solars as heroes.<br /> <br /> But let's assume that wasn't the case. Why would I advocate 'Solars are heroes' as a legitimate statement? Because it's one that appeals to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 03-13-2014, 08:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T05:41:35-07:00","id":90150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90099#post90099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is not, however, altogether an uncommon occurence. Like, at all. I've found exactly the same thing happening to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>*shrugs* People having a stupid opinion are plentiful*. Doesn't make that opinion any more right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90134#post90134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The new edition seems to embrace the characterization of Solars as heroes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. The mistake happens when one tries to say that heroes = generally good people. Blaque is generally right in saying that your argument is valid but unsound.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90134#post90134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But let's assume that wasn't the case. Why would I advocate 'Solars are heroes' as a legitimate statement? Because it's one that appeals to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's all well and good for your game. After all, YCMV! What's not good is saying it should be the case for Creation as it is presented in general, that solars who are not good <i>&quot;are exceptions who <b>need</b> to be treated as such&quot;</i>. (your second post in the thread, btw) It's the &quot;need&quot; that makes it seem as though you'd like for this view to be the default. <br /> <br /> *Note that I never said they were stupid people in general. Smart people can, and do, have stupid opinions at times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ultimate Jade-Screened Exalted Scholar, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304239-my-next-campaign-tdhr-peach\" target=\"_blank\">THDR : Future Dragon-Blooded campaign</a>, and other links.<br /> If you like Ex3, you can support <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/holdenshearer\" target=\"_blank\">Holden</a> on Patreon!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","name":"LeTipex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T05:51:16-07:00","id":90152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89984#post89984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First: your emphasis on how likely a bad guy is to be a given Exalt type gives no notice to the fact that if you pin down Solars as good guys, and you <i>don't</i> pin down anyone else in any way, then you automatically have fewer bad guys, total. Which means that Lunars aren't any worse than a regular person, nor any worse than they would be if Solars were statistically amoral. Of course, I don't even have to argue that point, because your analysis is predicated on precisely that.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have fewer bad guys in total since a bunch fo them aren't Solars. But this basically means that since we have defined Solars as having special exemption from being bad people at Exalting, yet haven't done the same for others, it's still going to be a comparison of Solars who are known to be good and anyone else who is no better htan the average population (or worst, given the stories and behaviors attributed other Exalts being acceptable apparently v. Solars).<br /> <br /> I don't know how to say it again. If one group is <i>required to be good</i>, but no other group has this requirement, then any given member of the first group <i>is more likely to be good than the other group</i>. Lunars are not required to be good, and so are no better than a random sampling of the population as a whole. Solars are, and so don't represent the whole, but a pre-determined subset of the population. If were to point at the acts of a given Solar or a given Lunar, I am more likely to say the Solar is a good person and the Lunar is not. This goes with Solar and any other random Exalt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89984#post89984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second: you make a fallacious leap of logic that assumes that the converse of a statement is true, which an Intro to Logic level mistake. Specifically, you take the statement &quot;most bad guys are Lunars&quot; and turn it into &quot;most Lunars are bad guys&quot;. I really don't like how hostile it makes me sound to point this out, but you <i>can't do that</i> if you're trying to make a logically consistent argument.</div> </div> </div> </div>I pointed out earlier that I'm not arguing the converse.<br /> <br /> (x)(Solar(x) -&gt; Good(x)) has more or less been the argument, as &quot;heroic&quot; = &quot;good&quot; and all Solars are this definiton of heroic. Which means (x)(!Good(x) -&gt; !Solar(x)), as a result. But that's a thing. It means that if you are a Solar, you are good. The logical result is you aren't good, you aren't a Solar. This in effect can be read as &quot;Non-Solars are not good.&quot; By pinning down Solars as something, you define non-Solarness as including non-goodness to. Now yes, this is more complciated with necessary and sufficient instead of just true/false or likely. But it doens't change the fact that Solars apparently by the way their population is defined are always going to be people that are good, while no one else gets to claim this. And so SOlars in general are going ot be assumed to be doing the good thing, and everyone else is more easily made &quot;villainous&quot; as they have no sort of &quot;Moral requirement so I don't risk folks going about being bad guys with no consequences&quot;.<br /> <br /> This combined with the likelihood above means that if I pick a random person, and they're bad, they're not a Solar. Apparently it's bad if Solars are evil. But anyone else is fine. They're not Solars and only Solars are defined as good as a requirement. In my view <i>no sort of Exalt should have as a requirement a moral factor, period</i>. The way to not have this issue at all is to have Exalts have the same &quot;goodness&quot; as a population as...the population of humans they come from.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89984#post89984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Third: you arbitrarily limit your analysis to Exalts. Aren't there bad guys who are gods, and heroic mortals, and raksha, etc. etc.?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, which is why I have through this thread said non-Solar entities. Becuase I do include raksha, gods and what have you in that, but Exalts are easier to point out since they glow different and in the case of Lunars, have numbers that are easier to compare with without speculation of headache inducing. And it still stands that Solars are apparently a unique group in requiring goodness to be a member of that group, while no other being has that, and therefore no other being gets to be as likely to be &quot;the good guy&quot; in a situation. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89984#post89984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fourth: you seem to predicate your conclusion on the notion that good can only come into conflict with bad, and vice versa. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Do I? I note outright that there's a good chance of good v. good fights. BUt the issue is that since non-Solars are more likely to not be the specific sort of good (good people doing good deeds with intent on chanigng the world into a better place) and people not necessariliy &quot;evil&quot; but not necessarily altruistic don't get to be &quot;good&quot; either, along with a greater amount of non-Solars than Solars total and they being subjected to more general population moral standards....totals to no matter how you math it out, SOlars are generally going to be Solar v. Not Good Guys more often than Solar v. Good Guy.<br /> <br /> I didn't do the math this morning since that requires me to sit and build the equations. But in a simple analogy, say i have two revolvers. One has five bullets in it's six chambers, the other has four This means if I fire both guns at a target, the likelihood that both fire is 27.7...%. This in a sense is like tow &quot;good people&quot; fighting. The likelihood of th efirst gun firing and the other one not however is 55.5...%. For completeness, both guns not firing is 11.1...% and the first not firing and the second firing is only 5.5...%.<br /> <br /> This extends with larger groups or smaller groups. When comparing two populations with uneven distribution of a trait, the one that has the higher trait is more likely to encounter whatever trait is higher in the second group. And since whatever the second group is is random or arbitrary, it is easy to skew or make what you want as you want. Which puts Solars at a moral advantage as they are requried to be better than the general population. And so conflicts with non-good groups are less likely because by the definiton given, most people aren't that good.<br /> <br /> So again, I don't reject the idea of good people don't conflict with good people. But the idea that one group is good and the rest arent' required to be causes problems I don't think are good for the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89984#post89984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exalted is a setting which offers a lot of moral complexity, and a good Solar (who is good because he wants to end slavery) can fight against a good Sidereal (who is good because he wants to ensure the insanity of the Solars never brings the world into peril again) without the &quot;good&quot; of either being diminished.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who defines slavery as bad, as a note, besides our modern post-abolutionist views? Why should our standards matter against slavery when it is to some extent hypocritical and modernist? Why should I judge either as &quot;good&quot; in such a way that one got him his Exaltation and so he gets to use that as a justification of his actions, while the other is often played as politics or action they chose to do on beliefs? What should any of whether someone's good or not even matter for what anima they have?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89984#post89984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To illustrate the absurdity of your analysis, I pose an alternate proposition, which I neither believe nor intend to defend: All Exalted are good. By the methods you've demonstrated, this assertion is impossible to analyse. It breaks down where you try to tabulate the likelihood of a bad guy being a member of each Exalt type. You get a 0% probability across the board, and the conclusion is that bad guys don't exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doens't break down since I allow for probabilities, which make things a bit less simple than true deductive logic will allow. Otherwise this would indeed be the case. Which is why defining a group as &quot;good&quot; provides nothing to the themes of the game that have been part of its premise since Day Zero.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T07:12:02-07:00","id":90185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LeTipex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90150#post90150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Blaque is generally right in saying that your argument is valid but unsound.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh dear, my thoughts on Solar exalted fail to meet the criteria for a sound argument. Well, at least my opinions are valid, no need to slit my wrists.. <i>yet</i>. <br /> <br /> You and Blaque may feel that this discussion would benefit from me expressing my thoughts as 'valid and sound' arguments, but I do not. My justification for Solars being heroes is that <i>the human soul craves beauty and nobility</i>, and I'm not even prepared to present an argument for the existence of the human soul, that beauty and nobility are quantifiable, or that even if they were that an RPG about mythic superheroes is at all the right vector for them.<br /> <br /> I understand if that's your preferred mode of discussion and appreciate that engaging with someone disinterested in it may be frustrating for you. I have been in that situation myself. However, the idea that I'm not presenting a sound argument doesn't bother me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And that's all well and good for your game. After all, YCMV! What's not good is saying it should be the case for Creation as it is presented in general, that solars who are not good <i>&quot;are exceptions who <b>need</b> to be treated as such&quot;</i>. (your second post in the thread, btw) It's the &quot;need&quot; that makes it seem as though you'd like for this view to be the default. </div> </div> </div>But I do think that it should be the case for Exalted.<br /> <br /> It's one thing if you disagree, I expect people to disagree, but the idea that me starting this thread was a bad thing boggles my mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T07:19:57-07:00","id":90191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90152#post90152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(x)(Solar(x) -&gt; Good(x)) has more or less been the argument, as &quot;heroic&quot; = &quot;good&quot; and all Solars are this definiton of heroic. Which means (x)(!Good(x) -&gt; !Solar(x)), as a result. But that's a thing. It means that if you are a Solar, you are good. The logical result is you aren't good, you aren't a Solar. This in effect can be read as &quot;Non-Solars are not good.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It, uh, really, really cannot. That's the &quot;Dogs have four legs, things without four legs are not dogs, therefore non-dogs don't have four legs,&quot; error.<br /> <br /> ***<br /> <br /> I don't have a dog (four-legged or otherwise) in most of this fight, but I do have some concerns regarding Stephenls's text/subtext division. That being... the subtext is the thing you're supposed to get after a while, yeah? It's the thing you don't realize when the movie <i>starts</i>, but that you understand by the end. Which works fine in a book, or a movie, or whatever, because these things <i>have</i> ends. I can understand how you could, say, write the Ex3 core with &quot;But really, does heroism even matter?&quot; as subtext. I can even see that coming out as subtext over the course of a campaign - again, there's (always) an ending.<br /> <br /> But most of us have played campaigns, and reached the endings of 'em. We've seen the point where subtext clicks - and if the subtext points to the answer &quot;Heroism is bunk,&quot; it's hard to see how <i>the community conversation</i> is not going to necessarily treat the subtext as text. The game's still leading to that conclusion - it's just asking us to take our time about getting there.<br /> <br /> So for those of us who have played Exalted, who have had the subtext click... how is a more careful subtexting meant to change the way we think about or play the game? What's different?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T07:21:04-07:00","id":90192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90134#post90134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The new edition seems to embrace the characterization of Solars as heroes.<br /> <br /> But let's assume that wasn't the case. Why would I advocate 'Solars are heroes' as a legitimate statement? Because it's one that appeals to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a nominal fallacy, or at least a problem very similar to one, and a selective quoting.<br /> <br /> Its something like a nominal fallact because having something named doesn't mean its understood anymore than if it didn't had a name. In this case we should all agree that solars should be heores, since the devs are calling them heroes. however that doesnt mean in anyway that we understand or agree on what a hero is.<br /> <br /> Its selective quoting because the devs when on to explain what it means to them that solars are heroes. The complete quote is<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Solars are myth-heroes. It is a myth-hero's purpose to subvert mythos and thereby define it. Solars fight, destroy, and ultimately recreate the status-quo, doing so by conquering the obliquely magical through acts of sheer will, force, and skill writ-large, like every myth-hero in literature.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't assume at any point that being a hero is being good. Its above being agents of change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2245,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2245-quimeradc","user":"Quimeradc","date":". 03-13-2014, 10:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2245-quimeradc","name":"Quimeradc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T07:26:51-07:00","id":90197,"title":"","content":"I selectively quoted a dev... in a post where I didn't quote a dev at all?<br /> <br /> Also, your complete quote isn't complete. You quote two sentence from a multi-paragraph post. The complete quote (which you were quoting, not I) would be:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Solars, Lunars, and Sidereals occupy entirely different game-space in Exalted. Solars are myth-heroes. It is a myth-hero's purpose to subvert mythos and thereby define it. Solars fight, destroy, and ultimately recreate the status-quo, doing so by conquering the obliquely magical through acts of sheer will, force, and skill writ-large, like every myth-hero in literature. IE, a Solar built to win a foot race will win a foot race with the very Maiden of Journeys. The Solar will outrun Death itself.<br /> <br /> Lunars are heart-eating, shapeshifting skin-walker legends and monsters. They turn into swift cats and soaring birds, fish that can swim and giant monsters that can rend down fortress walls. They are monsters and beasts. Compare them to the great monsters and beasts of legend. Less Hercules, more hydra and chimera. That is their game-space.<br /> <br /> Sidereals are literally sorcerer-bureaucrats with kung fu. They are the most literal agents of myth that you can get. They are not subversive, but rather assimilationist. They occupy a radically different game-space than Solars.<br /> <br /> Many members of both the Lunar and Sidereal Exalted have set themselves against the Solar Exalted. This will be an extremely interesting conflict. Just keep the different game-spaces in mind, because these spaces imply different meaning and purpose for all three Exalt types. This will be reflected in their Charms (and always has been). </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 03-13-2014, 10:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T07:26:55-07:00","id":90198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90134#post90134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes well, as persuasive as I am, I find that if someone is only willing to create PCs that fit a specific thematic default then I don't have much sympathy for them if they dislike the results.</div> </div> </div> </div>Setting the mold just so people could break it is pretty dumb, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T07:33:24-07:00","id":90204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90197#post90197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I selectively quoted a dev... in a post where I didn't quote a dev at all?<br /> <br /> Also, your complete quote isn't complete. You quote two sentence from a multi-paragraph post.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are right, you weren't quoting, im sorry.<br /> <br /> But you did said that the game is being dsigned with solars as heroes in mind, without explaining what those heroes are supposed to be. I incorrectly assumed you were refering to that quote in particular. Still i think that despite my error the point stands. Solars are going to be heroes in EX3, thats being explicitly stated. But that doesn't mean they are going to be good.<br /> <br /> I'll try to confrim my assumptions in the future instead of taking them granted <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2245-quimeradc","name":"Quimeradc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T07:41:53-07:00","id":90211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90185#post90185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh dear, my thoughts on Solar exalted fail to meet the criteria for a sound argument. Well, at least my opinions are valid, no need to slit my wrists.. <i>yet</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>*rolleyes*<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90185#post90185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You and Blaque may feel that this discussion would benefit from me expressing my thoughts as 'valid and sound' arguments, but I do not. My justification for Solars being heroes is that <i>the human soul craves beauty and nobility</i>, and I'm not even prepared to present an argument for the existence of the human soul, that beauty and nobility are quantifiable, or that even if they were that an RPG about mythic superheroes is at all the right vector for them.<br /> <br /> I understand if that's your preferred mode of discussion and appreciate that engaging with someone disinterested in it may be frustrating for you. I have been in that situation myself. However, the idea that I'm not presenting a sound argument doesn't bother me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, but you not wanting to face some of our critiques doesn't invalidate those critiques.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90185#post90185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I do think that it should be the case for Exalted.<br /> <br /> It's one thing if you disagree, I expect people to disagree, but the idea that me starting this thread was a bad thing boggles my mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said starting this thread or this discussion was a bad thing. I said saying Solars are &quot;good&quot; in the text was a bad thing. You're entitled to your opinions, but so far, you've been saying in essence <i>&quot;I want this to be the case for Exalted* because I feel like it**, and I will not engage the critics of my position***&quot;</i>. Can you see why some people might be a bit peeved at that?<br /> <br /> * Your words<br /> ** &quot;human soul craves beauty and nobility&quot; is nothing more than &quot;i think that should be the case because&quot;, especially if you don't even try to define &quot;good&quot;, &quot;hero&quot;, &quot;soul&quot;, or &quot;nobility&quot;.<br /> *** that's pretty much the gist of my second quote up there","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ultimate Jade-Screened Exalted Scholar, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304239-my-next-campaign-tdhr-peach\" target=\"_blank\">THDR : Future Dragon-Blooded campaign</a>, and other links.<br /> If you like Ex3, you can support <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/holdenshearer\" target=\"_blank\">Holden</a> on Patreon!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","name":"LeTipex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T07:41:59-07:00","id":90212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90198#post90198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Setting the mold just so people could break it is pretty dumb, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, but I don't believe I've advocated that Solars be heroes just so PCs can break the heroic mold.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quimeradc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90204#post90204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are right, you weren't quoting, im sorry.<br /> <br /> But you did said that the game is being dsigned with solars as heroes in mind, without explaining what those heroes are supposed to be. I incorrectly assumed you were refering to that quote in particular. Still i think that despite my error the point stands. Solars are going to be heroes in EX3, thats being explicitly stated. But that doesn't mean they are going to be good.<br /> <br /> I'll try to confrim my assumptions in the future instead of taking them granted <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I want you to know that I appreciate you coming into the discussion and am not attempting to shut you down.<br /> <br /> I think that Solars will be heroic in E3, and I'm guessing that they'll be positioned as 'good guys.' Only time will tell if my guess is accurate or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 03-13-2014, 10:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T07:53:32-07:00","id":90217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90212#post90212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree, but I don't believe I've advocated that Solars be heroes just so PCs can break the heroic mold.</div> </div> </div> </div>But you do acknowledge this mold will be broken - more often than not, judging by the amount of opposition you've received in this thread?<br /> <br /> Because I see no practical difference between setting a mold for the express purpose of breaking it, and setting one despite knowing it will be broken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T07:54:34-07:00","id":90220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90212#post90212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree, but I don't believe I've advocated that Solars be heroes just so PCs can break the heroic mold.<br /> <br /> <br /> I want you to know that I appreciate you coming into the discussion and am not attempting to shut you down.<br /> <br /> I think that Solars will be heroic in E3, and I'm guessing that they'll be positioned as 'good guys.' Only time will tell if my guess is accurate or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I absolutely believe so too. But that doesn't mean &quot;all solars are heroes and heroes are good&quot; (hwhich is a simplified version of the part of your argument most of your opposition argues against).<br /> <br /> And in a world where the only true objective evil (\u200bi can think of) from creation inhabitants point of view is anything that attempts to destroy creation or submit it to its will, what a good guy is is not pretty clear unless the antagonist in question is one those external creation destroying/submiting threats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2245-quimeradc","name":"Quimeradc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T08:12:30-07:00","id":90228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90217#post90217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But you do acknowledge this mold will be broken - more often than not, judging by the amount of opposition you've received in this thread?<br /> <br /> Because I see no practical difference between setting a mold for the express purpose of breaking it, and setting one despite knowing it will be broken.</div> </div> </div> </div>But there's no theme that everyone will value or be interested in, and even if they value it and are interested in it, that doesn't mean they'll take their PC in that direction. The only way to make a theme everyone accepts is something like Exigent where it seems to be build-your-own-themes.<br /> <br /> That said (because, I think you're suggesting this) if introducing Solars as heroes is off-putting to the majority of player, then it's probably bad for the game line as they're the core splat. But I don't find the responses to this thread compelling evidence that this is the case.<br /> <br /> While the people of this forum are passionate, we're not representative of anything but ourselves.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, I'm saying this when I earlier talked about the wants of all humanity. So yeah... I probably shouldn't have done that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T08:25:08-07:00","id":90231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90228#post90228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said (because, I think you're suggesting this) if introducing Solars as heroes is off-putting to the majority of player, then it's probably bad for the game line as they're the core splat. But I don't find the responses to this thread compelling evidence that this is the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not entirely true if solar are being introduced as heroes in the world changing agent sense instead of heroes in the good natured wolrd saver sense.<br /> <br /> Edit: in my opinion, as i can't speak with any one else, the argument is not about the statemente &quot;solars are heroes&quot;. Its about the definition of heroes or the types of heroes that will be represented in the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2245,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2245-quimeradc","user":"Quimeradc","date":". 03-13-2014, 11:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2245-quimeradc","name":"Quimeradc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T08:29:38-07:00","id":90232,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quimeradc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90220#post90220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I absolutely believe so too. But that doesn't mean &quot;all solars are heroes and heroes are good&quot; (hwhich is a simplified version of the part of your argument most of your opposition argues against).<br /> <br /> And in a world where the only true objective evil (\u200bi can think of) from creation inhabitants point of view is anything that attempts to destroy creation or submit it to its will, what a good guy is is not pretty clear unless the antagonist in question is one those external creation destroying/submiting threats.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I like about Exalted (core) is that it positions the player no differently than the DC superhero line. You are a hero and you have awesome powers! Go forth and collapse the evil Realm! Abolish slavery! Save the helpless village from the horrible fae folk horde!<br /> <br /> If you want to, you can embrace that completely and have awesome games where you wrestle a rotting zombies the size of the Empire State building in order to save Creation.<br /> <br /> But what Exalted does that DC superheroes doesn't support, is also give you a setting where you can explore what it means to be a hero. You can tell stories where toppling the evil Realm has serious economic and political consequences. Where saving the day is more than beating the shit out of a giant monster/evil organization. Where you can look across the field and see that the guy you're fighting is also trying to be one of the good guys.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quimeradc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90231#post90231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not entirely true if solar are being introduced as heroes in the world changing agent sense instead of heroes in the good natured wolrd saver sense.<br /> <br /> Edit: in my opinion, as i can't speak with any one else, the argument is not about the statemente &quot;solars are heroes&quot;. Its about the definition of heroes or the types of heroes that will be represented in the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, what I think ought to remain subtext - 'What does being good mean?' 'But the god who picked me isn't a god of 'good,' he's a god of virtue.' 'Being a hero in Creation isn't necessarily the same as the popular, modern concept of heroes.' - they want to be the text.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, I am completely for positioning the Dragon-Blooded as &quot;heroes.&quot; That they're a nobility that's slid into decadence and corruption is something I think should be front and center.<br /> <br /> If the Lunars manual had introductory fiction where a Lunar sig tore out the heart of her foe and devoured it, I'd love it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 03-13-2014, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T08:41:18-07:00","id":90243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90232#post90232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Right, what I think ought to remain subtext - 'What does being good mean?' 'But the god who picked me isn't a god of 'good,' he's a god of virtue.' 'Being a hero in Creation isn't necessarily the same as the popular, modern concept of heroes.' - they want to be the text.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. An undefined heroe is better than a defined one. That includes wheter they should be good or agents of change or paragons of skill. its up to the player to decide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2245-quimeradc","name":"Quimeradc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T08:46:21-07:00","id":90245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90232#post90232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Right, what I think ought to remain subtext - 'What does being good mean?' 'But the god who picked me isn't a god of 'good,' he's a god of virtue.' 'Being a hero in Creation isn't necessarily the same as the popular, modern concept of heroes.' - they want to be the text.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't personally have any problem with the various arguments for keeping subtext as subtext. I think my ability to see this as truly the crux of the argument as opposed to a method of bolstering other arguments is a nitpick if I'm honest. If one says Solars -are- good people (as opposed to seem to be, or can be, or might be), it sort of dismisses the subtext as even being a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/926-yishten","name":"Yishten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar926_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T08:49:53-07:00","id":90246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90217#post90217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But you do acknowledge this mold will be broken - more often than not, judging by the amount of opposition you've received in this thread?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey now anecdotes are not data, just because we have a bunch of people arguing in circles in one thread does not give us any real idea about what the fanbase wants as a whole. Really go back through the thread and you will see maybe 10 people actually taking part in this discussion consistently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon","name":"Calboon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar223_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T08:55:43-07:00","id":90250,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure it's <i>possible </i>for a fanbase to want things as a whole. I can't really picture it -- what would they do with their time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T09:01:44-07:00","id":90258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yishten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90245#post90245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I don't personally have any problem with the various arguments for keeping subtext as subtext. I think my ability to see this as truly the crux of the argument as opposed to a method of bolstering other arguments is a nitpick if I'm honest. If one says Solars -are- good people (as opposed to seem to be, or can be, or might be), it sort of dismisses the subtext as even being a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I think saying &quot;Solars seem to be heroes&quot; or &quot;Solars seem to be good people&quot; destroys the subtext by making it text.<br /> <br /> This is my preferred introduction -<br /> Text: Solars are heroes and good guys. The supreme god has granted you the power to smite the everloving shit out of your enemies. Enjoy!<br /> Player: But what does that mean?<br /> <br /> This seems to be the introduction prefered by others -<br /> Text: Solars may be heroes. Heroism in Creation is defined around ancient mythology and heroic Solars can be monsters. Enjoy!<br /> Player: Awesome, a fantasy game that doesn't shove morality down my throat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90250#post90250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure it's <i>possible </i>for a fanbase to want things as a whole. I can't really picture it -- what would they do with their time?</div> </div> </div> </div>My default answer would be 'make nude mods' and 'write fan fiction where they have sex with the main character.' At least, my experience with fandoms leads me to believe that... though anecdotes are not data.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 03-13-2014, 12:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T09:07:40-07:00","id":90260,"title":"","content":"I enjoy playing Heroes as Good Guys. People who want to change the world for the better.<br /> <br /> My group also tends to play good guys. I'm currently doing a 1st ed/1st age game as a prelude to the game I plan to run once 3rd (finally) drops. And I have to be really careful about how I present the Elder Solars, because I know my players, and they'd be the type to start a revolution against the corrupt deliberative if I let it be obvious.<br /> <br /> That said, I don't expect &quot;Good Guy&quot; to be the Solar default in 3rd ed. Heroes, yes. Good... only by virtue of contrast to the &quot;bad&quot; of the Realm and whatever enemies of creation are out there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a Woman, I'm a GM. <i>Of course</i> I'm Evil.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/424-dawaterrat","name":"DaWaterRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T09:10:58-07:00","id":90262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90258#post90258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> While I think saying &quot;Solars seem to be heroes&quot; or &quot;Solars seem to be good people&quot; destroys the subtext by making it text. This is my preferred introduction - Text: Solars are heroes and good guys. The supreme god has granted you the power to smite the everloving shit out of your enemies. Enjoy! Player: But what does that mean? This seems to be the introduction prefered by others - Text: Solars may be heroes. Heroism in Creation is defined around ancient mythology and heroic Solars can be monsters. Enjoy! Player: Awesome, a fantasy game that doesn't shove morality down my throat.</div> </div> </div> </div> I can see what you mean here. I still feel like something's a bit off, but I'll admit to having a difficult time elucidating it. It exists somewhere in the realms of disliking the premise that any group could ever, realistically (for whatever value if realistic Creation strives for), be quantified as objectively good; and in my feeling that the subtext is more about the utilization of power and the consequence thereof than morality specifically. But, yeah, I find myself wavering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/926-yishten","name":"Yishten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar926_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T09:11:54-07:00","id":90263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90258#post90258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I think saying &quot;Solars seem to be heroes&quot; or &quot;Solars seem to be good people&quot; destroys the subtext by making it text.<br /> <br /> This is my preferred introduction -<br /> Text: Solars are heroes and good guys. The supreme god has granted you the power to smite the everloving shit out of your enemies. Enjoy!<br /> Player: But what does that mean?<br /> <br /> This seems to be the introduction prefered by others -<br /> Text: Solars may be heroes. Heroism in Creation is defined around ancient mythology and heroic Solars can be monsters. Enjoy!<br /> Player: Awesome, a fantasy game that doesn't shove morality down my throat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both textes are leading too much and leaving subtext behind. i would go with something like this:<br /> <br /> Text: Solars are heroes, paragons of human prowess imbued with the powers of the unconquered sun, reappearing in a crumbling world after thousnads of years of abscense. Will their coming herald a new age of wonders or is it too late for creation? Enjoy!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2245-quimeradc","name":"Quimeradc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T09:21:03-07:00","id":90270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=89970#post89970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you for bringing that into this thread. I've been made to feel like I'm crazy for reading &quot;Solars are good guys&quot; in the material; the quoted states, explicitly and with a high degree of authority, that that's the intended face-value read. And the subtext that questions it, the notion that wait, are Solars going to really fix anything by being Big Damn Heroes?, that's a big part of what I like about Exalted, but I feel like that subtext has been inflated by the community to define Solars at face value, which Lea says is a bad thing, and puts so eloquently into words why it frustrates me.<br /> <br /> Again, thank you. I've felt like reference to actual facts and quotes has been incredibly sparse in this thread, and by defying that trend you have made my day.</div> </div> </div> </div>That SLS post doesn't say that Solars are the good guys. Solars are virtuous and righteous and they shine with the light of the sun, yet at the end of the day those things do not add up to goodness even if they are inspiring and make for interesting stories to tell. It's important that the game support playing Solars <i>as if</i> they are good even as it asks the players to question just what they are doing and what kind of legacy will be left by their actions. The latter part can be left out for groups running &quot;paladins and lawbringers fighting evil and achieving peace&quot; which Exalted supports too, if that's their thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90185#post90185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh dear, my thoughts on Solar exalted fail to meet the criteria for a sound argument. Well, at least my opinions are valid, no need to slit my wrists.. <i>yet</i>.<br /> <br /> You and Blaque may feel that this discussion would benefit from me expressing my thoughts as 'valid and sound' arguments, but I do not. My justification for Solars being heroes is that <i>the human soul craves beauty and nobility</i>, and I'm not even prepared to present an argument for the existence of the human soul, that beauty and nobility are quantifiable, or that even if they were that an RPG about mythic superheroes is at all the right vector for them.<br /> <br /> But I do think that it should be the case for Exalted.<br /> <br /> It's one thing if you disagree, I expect people to disagree, but the idea that me starting this thread was a bad thing boggles my mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>No offense, but it seems you might be unaware that &quot;valid and sound&quot; are formal terms used for discussion of logic in argumentation. Your argument is valid in that your conclusion follows from your premises. Soundness comes after if all of the premises hold true. If you are ok with your unsound arguments, it means that you are admitting your premises are false; your use of a modern definition of hero and its appeals to goodness is the incorrect premise many posters here have identified. If you feel that your position is correct obviously we cannot convince you otherwise, but the critiques here have shown how this damages the central thesis of the game, its incompatibility with historical and mythological inspirations, and how unsupported it is by evidence within the setting.<br /> <br /> Whether individual Exalts are good is a question for us, the readers and players and storytellers, to toy with after the fact based on the intentions and outcomes of their adventures and our own cultural frame. Most of them will be incredibly complicated people who defy such a label, as great historical figures tend to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1564-shinjo","name":"Shinjo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T09:24:04-07:00","id":90273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yishten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90262#post90262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I can see what you mean here. I still feel like something's a bit off, but I'll admit to having a difficult time elucidating it. It exists somewhere in the realms of disliking the premise that any group could ever, realistically (for whatever value if realistic Creation strives for), be quantified as objectively good; and in my feeling that the subtext is more about the utilization of power and the consequence thereof than morality specifically. But, yeah, I find myself wavering.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's cool.<br /> <br /> Rejecting something on a gut level is as legitimate as writing a multiparagraph post on how it doesn't work. If you're going to pour hours into a game, it needs to be something that appeals to you on a basic level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T09:26:26-07:00","id":90274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90258#post90258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I think saying &quot;Solars seem to be heroes&quot; or &quot;Solars seem to be good people&quot; destroys the subtext by making it text.<br /> <br /> This is my preferred introduction -<br /> Text: Solars are heroes and good guys. The supreme god has granted you the power to smite the everloving shit out of your enemies. Enjoy!<br /> Player: But what does that mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>My issue with this is that the question is kinda silly. We know what being heroes and good guy's mean, or at least most people really think they do. So if you tell people that their characters are good, they're going to assume that the characters are good in the way that they understand being good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2005-cosar","name":"CoSaR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T09:28:07-07:00","id":90275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90093#post90093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this, too, is entirely terrible.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Indeed, I'm just stating that the position of &quot;This is what exalted has been presented as.&quot; is not exactly consistant. In fact most of second edition was full of text telling people about how monsterous and terrible the Solars can be, and then almost all the examples of second age solars are some combination of modern superheroes.<br /> <br /> I think they do it perhaps a little too much. I think most people know now that Solars can be pretty bad dudes, we don't need a first age book showing us the ten tousand ways to be a monster. Maybe it's just my group but I now find that when a Solar is introduced into a game the default assumption is that he's going to stab you in the back. Or punch you in the face. I want to feel like I did about Solars when I first started playing, where I felt like the golden shining hero and not just the one good person amongs monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T09:30:01-07:00","id":90277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90185#post90185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh dear, my thoughts on Solar exalted fail to meet the criteria for a sound argument. Well, at least my opinions are valid, no need to slit my wrists.. <i>yet</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Barring the sarcasm, to me an unsound argument is about as bad as an invalid one. Sometimes worst since they tend to rise out of cruddy reasoning of how the world works. Or in this case, how terminology works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90185#post90185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You and Blaque may feel that this discussion would benefit from me expressing my thoughts as 'valid and sound' arguments, but I do not. My justification for Solars being heroes is that <i>the human soul craves beauty and nobility</i>, and I'm not even prepared to present an argument for the existence of the human soul, that beauty and nobility are quantifiable, or that even if they were that an RPG about mythic superheroes is at all the right vector for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well if you won't, I will. The &quot;human soul&quot; is as I gather not real and in Creation, is not something craves what you say or anymore than our not-souls seem to. It's a functional device, not a teleological one in Creation. What is beautiful and noble is contextual and subjective. Throwing feel-good alternatives of &quot;I like it this way because I like it this way&quot; more or less is admitting that you have no reasons besides bias and personal taste. Which means you have no basis going about making declarative statements of what words mean and then try to use the word only to mean that thing in your discussion.<br /> <br /> Also, Exalted has been outright stated in other venues as not a superheroes game, although it draws aspects from specific parts of the superhero genre.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90185#post90185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand if that's your preferred mode of discussion and appreciate that engaging with someone disinterested in it may be frustrating for you. I have been in that situation myself. However, the idea that I'm not presenting a sound argument doesn't bother me.</div> </div> </div> </div>It also means you basically aren't open to criticism and are going to carry on ranting about your choice of words as if your opinion has weight. And we will continue to criticize you loudly on that point because at the end of the day your original post was and seems to still be a fluffy way of saying &quot;I want this because I like it.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90185#post90185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I do think that it should be the case for Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have yet to demonstrate such though, as validity is not in itself the goal of an argument. Especially since it's gained through fallacy, as noted above.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90185#post90185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's one thing if you disagree, I expect people to disagree, but the idea that me starting this thread was a bad thing boggles my mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think folks have said it's a bad thing in itself. But it has been a bad argument.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T09:35:12-07:00","id":90279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90191#post90191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It, uh, really, really cannot. That's the &quot;Dogs have four legs, things without four legs are not dogs, therefore non-dogs don't have four legs,&quot; error.</div> </div> </div> </div>Save that four legs isn't actually a defintion of dog. Being a canine, however is. I woudl say &quot;being good&quot; so far has been argued by some (if not hippokrene) as being a criterion to Solarness, with no exceptions at the time of Exaltation. This to me seems more like &quot;dogs are canines&quot; than &quot;dogs have four legs.&quot; Which then invites the comparisons. Note that there can be non-dogs who are canines (coyotes). But given any random animal who's not a dog, it'll probably not be a canine. It's only a fallacy if innproper predicates have been used.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90191#post90191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have a dog (four-legged or otherwise) in most of this fight, but I do have some concerns regarding Stephenls's text/subtext division. That being... the subtext is the thing you're supposed to get after a while, yeah? It's the thing you don't realize when the movie <i>starts</i>, but that you understand by the end. Which works fine in a book, or a movie, or whatever, because these things <i>have</i> ends. I can understand how you could, say, write the Ex3 core with &quot;But really, does heroism even matter?&quot; as subtext. I can even see that coming out as subtext over the course of a campaign - again, there's (always) an ending.<br /> <br /> But most of us have played campaigns, and reached the endings of 'em. We've seen the point where subtext clicks - and if the subtext points to the answer &quot;Heroism is bunk,&quot; it's hard to see how <i>the community conversation</i> is not going to necessarily treat the subtext as text. The game's still leading to that conclusion - it's just asking us to take our time about getting there.<br /> <br /> So for those of us who have played Exalted, who have had the subtext click... how is a more careful subtexting meant to change the way we think about or play the game? What's different?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll get to this in a later post, but my main issue with hippokren is she conflates heroic with good. This is the problem. Heroism is where the subtext is. That heroism is good should be the issue. But she isn't interested in subtext. She has stated that Solars should overwhelmingly be shown as good, and not-good Solars as the exception. This isn't highlighting the subtext. It's making the text the reality straight-out, and tossing the subtext out, as instead of heroism being bunk, non-good acts are unheroic and so are such Solars. It turns the text into the whole topic.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T09:39:22-07:00","id":90285,"title":"","content":"Hippokrene, the big problem is that you're presenting an argument and then refusing to defend it. You're saying that it doesn't need to be sound, you're dismissing the burden of prooving that your argument holds any water and anyone should take it seriously. You speak as if it can either be dismissed with no explenation or simply accepted without one. That leads to nowhere. The only evidence that you have for it being true are mined quotes and a big argument from ignorance (&quot;when John speaks about heroes he MUST speak about heroes in a way *I* define, because jee willikers if he doesn't, then I DON'T KNOW what he's talking about and that can't be right&quot;).<br /> <br /> Until you actually convince us that it makes sense nobody, NOBODY has any obligation to refute it. It's really that simple.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2052,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","user":"FromBeyond","date":". 03-13-2014, 12:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T09:41:06-07:00","id":90286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90212#post90212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree, but I don't believe I've advocated that Solars be heroes just so PCs can break the heroic mold.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except, you know, your definiton of hero is not one that fits the context of Exalted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90212#post90212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... I think that Solars will be heroic in E3, and I'm guessing that they'll be positioned as 'good guys.' Only time will tell if my guess is accurate or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember Aesha from the 1e corebook opening fiction? The first Solar we saw? And who's fiction is now floated about with permission because she summarizes a lot of Solars?<br /> <br /> I think it'll be more likely they'll be positioned as the main characters. You can do that without comic book &quot;good guy&quot; presentations.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T09:47:13-07:00","id":90288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90228#post90228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But there's no theme that everyone will value or be interested in, and even if they value it and are interested in it, that doesn't mean they'll take their PC in that direction. The only way to make a theme everyone accepts is something like Exigent where it seems to be build-your-own-themes.<br /> <br /> That said (because, I think you're suggesting this) if introducing Solars as heroes is off-putting to the majority of player, then it's probably bad for the game line as they're the core splat. But I don't find the responses to this thread compelling evidence that this is the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>We never said Solars aren't being presented as heroes. You just have yet to argue in any fashion your definniton is that definition. So I will say folks are quite fine with Solars as heroes. Your definition is still wrong. I might be a broken record on this ,but you seem to keep insisting it is right on basis of...you said so. And so folks will criticize your point and be off put by your arguments as they are built on false premises. Your characterization of others not following your definiton being against &quot;Solars are heroic&quot; is, as a note, a strawman. And is a bit like the whole argument of &quot;If you don't like hamburgers, you're un-American, as I defined American.&quot; Which is to say: Fluff and framing terms to suit your needs without addressing your point's failings.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T09:52:32-07:00","id":90294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90285#post90285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hippokrene, the big problem is that you're presenting an argument and then refusing to defend it. You're saying that it doesn't need to be sound, you're dismissing the burden of prooving that your argument holds any water and anyone should take it seriously. You speak as if it can either be dismissed with no explenation or simply accepted without one. That leads to nowhere.<br /> <br /> Until you actually convince us that it makes sense nobody, NOBODY has any obligation to refute it. It's really that simple.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your post comes from such an different viewpoint, I'm not sure how to react to it.<br /> <br /> 1) I have no interest in making or defending an argument.<br /> 2) People are under no obligation to 'refute' my non-argument.<br /> 3) I am rather satisfied with this thread and the discussions I've read/participated in, so I'm unlikely to change my communication style.<br /> <br /> You seem... upset? I suppose you see a problem here that I don't, which is frustrating?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 03-13-2014, 12:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T09:52:42-07:00","id":90295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90228#post90228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said (because, I think you're suggesting this) if introducing Solars as heroes is off-putting to the majority of player, then it's probably bad for the game line as they're the core splat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Solars as heroes is perfectly acceptable. Narrowing down the definition of heroism the way you want it... not so much off-putting as a needless restriction that may actually harm the thesis of the game.<br /> <br /> Just so we're on the same page: I oppose making this a certain and definite thing not because I don't want to see Solars played that way*, but because throughout the years I've grown fond of many different, often conflicting points of view espoused by different factions and types of beings in the setting, and am wary of anything that could make those viewpoints seem invalid by default.<br /> <br /> *In fact, the most fun I've ever had with Exalted was when I played as straight a good guy as humanly possible, though he was an Orichalcum Caste Alchemical rather than a Solar. I had a blast with him, and would play him again, or reuse his personality for a Solar in 3e, in a blink of an eye. Still, I don't think my experience would be any richer if Alchies were penned as straight good guys by default, rather than champions of morally ambiguous totalitarian states, and I don't think playing a Solar expy of him would be made any better by a definite statement to this effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T09:54:58-07:00","id":90296,"title":"","content":"As a random additon, Shinjo, FromBeyond, Quimerac and LeTipex help me not believe I'm being a ragaholic philosophy person as I type things. -_-<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":353,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","user":"Blaque","date":".  Additon/editon slip-up. Even I won't let that typo stand. 03-13-2014, 01:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T10:05:26-07:00","id":90302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90296#post90296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a random edition, Shinjo, FromBeyond, Quimerac and LeTipex help me not believe I'm being a ragaholic philosophy person as I type things. -_-<br /> <br /> And stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've enjoyed reading your posts and am glad you participated in my thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T10:15:38-07:00","id":90310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90294#post90294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your post comes from such an different viewpoint, I'm not sure how to react to it.<br /> <br /> 1) I have no interest in making or defending an argument.<br /> 2) People are under no obligation to 'refute' my non-argument.<br /> 3) I am rather satisfied with this thread and the discussions I've read/participated in, so I'm unlikely to change my communication style.<br /> <br /> You seem... upset? I suppose you see a problem here that I don't, which is frustrating?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the fact that you're making an argument and then try to twist it by claiming that you're actually NOT making an argument and thus you're free from defending it, instead acting as if it's some form of an objectively existing fact is EXTREMELY FRUSTRATING. I'd very much apreciated if you stopped.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2052,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","user":"FromBeyond","date":". 03-13-2014, 01:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T10:29:44-07:00","id":90319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90294#post90294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your post comes from such an different viewpoint, I'm not sure how to react to it.<br /> <br /> 1) I have no interest in making or defending an argument.<br /> 2) People are under no obligation to 'refute' my non-argument.<br /> 3) I am rather satisfied with this thread and the discussions I've read/participated in, so I'm unlikely to change my communication style.<br /> <br /> You seem... upset? I suppose you see a problem here that I don't, which is frustrating?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hippokrene, I think that FromBeyond has a valid point here. If you don't think you are defening or making and argument, you should clearly defined it as an opinion instead of stating it as a fact.<br /> <br /> Stating &quot;all solars are heroes and heroes are good &quot;(once again simplifying the argument most opponent refute) is making an statement. and giving reasons for that statement is defending it.<br /> <br /> If instead of that you would say &quot;i believe all solar are good heroes&quot; the thread would have a different tone, where we could try to convince each other of our opinions but where no one would ultimately be right or wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2245,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2245-quimeradc","user":"Quimeradc","date":". 03-13-2014, 01:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2245-quimeradc","name":"Quimeradc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T10:30:56-07:00","id":90320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90310#post90310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yes, the fact that you're making an argument and then try to twist it by claiming that you're actually NOT making an argument and thus you're free from defending it, instead acting as if it's some form of an objectively existing fact is EXTREMELY FRUSTRATING. I'd very much apreciated if you stopped.</div> </div> </div> </div> This may surprise you but it is possible to have a discussion with people without having to turn it into a crazy throw down debate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon","name":"Calboon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar223_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T10:36:19-07:00","id":90325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Calboon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90320#post90320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> This may surprise you but it is possible to have a discussion with people without having to turn it into a crazy throw down debate.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is. But when the initial post is done with a tone that invites debate, and then later it is revealed that the person initiating it is in effect arguing from bad faith, folks get pissed.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T11:13:19-07:00","id":90345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90310#post90310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, the fact that you're making an argument and then try to twist it by claiming that you're actually NOT making an argument and thus you're free from defending it, instead acting as if it's some form of an objectively existing fact is EXTREMELY FRUSTRATING. I'd very much apreciated if you stopped.</div> </div> </div> </div>We seem to be operating under a very different set of assumptions.<br /> <br /> You see my making this thread as akin to stepping into a boxing ring and challenging everyone to fight me. Then you're unhappy because I don't seem to be following the rules. You see this as dishonest of me.<br /> <br /> I see this thread as pulling out my grill and inviting everyone over for a pool party.<br /> <br /> That said, I understand what's bothering you and would like to clarify that I don't see 'Solars are heroes' as some objectively existing fact. Nor do I see 'good people doing good deeds to make the world a better place' as statement that can be objectively assessed as any better than any other definition of heroism.<br /> <br /> I hope that helps and you're more comfortable with my thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90325#post90325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is. But when the initial post is done with a tone that invites debate, and then later it is revealed that the person initiating it is in effect arguing from bad faith, folks get pissed.<br /> <br /> And stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>You totally got a debate out of this thread. I've been watching you for five days now, and if that's what you wanted, then you did get it. Just not with me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 03-13-2014, 02:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T11:29:50-07:00","id":90353,"title":"","content":"The matter of fact-lye statment of the original posting did seem to hard to be just an opinion and many people in forms take any chance to start an argument. <br /> <br /> Normally when someone post something im assuming they want feedback, otherwise they would keep it to themselves. so it stands to reason that people would try to refute it. Having it being an absolute claim makes it harder to resist. Its like a lamb exposing the neck for the wolves.<br /> <br /> Even then sometimes counter arguments can seem very aggresive. I take my time to acknowledge others and tell them what i agree with or not, insead &quot;striking&quot; directly with a counter argument and i also try, whenever posible, attempt to reconcile my position with the other party, instead of tying to win the argument, because nothing new or productive can come out of a competitive debate, in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2245-quimeradc","name":"Quimeradc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T11:40:44-07:00","id":90359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90279#post90279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Save that four legs isn't actually a defintion of dog. Being a canine, however is. I woudl say &quot;being good&quot; so far has been argued by some (if not hippokrene) as being a criterion to Solarness, with no exceptions at the time of Exaltation. This to me seems more like &quot;dogs are canines&quot; than &quot;dogs have four legs.&quot; Which then invites the comparisons. Note that there can be non-dogs who are canines (coyotes). But given any random animal who's not a dog, it'll probably not be a canine. It's only a fallacy if innproper predicates have been used.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds to me like an invalid-but-inductive argument, i.e., &quot;Given that someone is good, it's overwhelmingly likely that they'll be a Solar, even if not necessarily guaranteed.&quot; Which is a workable approach, except that I have no idea where you're getting that as a premise. I haven't seen anyone argue that Creation has only a few hundred good people, and several people arguing the converse, so the induction's pretty weak - and I definitely haven't seen anyone arguing &quot;Solar if and only if good.&quot;<br /> <br /> Again, not agreeing with hippokrene in general here, but I think you're stepping beyond solid ground on this line of critique.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T12:01:40-07:00","id":90365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90258#post90258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is my preferred introduction -<br /> Text: Solars are heroes and good guys. The supreme god has granted you the power to smite the everloving shit out of your enemies. Enjoy!<br /> Player: But what does that mean?<br /> <br /> This seems to be the introduction prefered by others -<br /> Text: Solars may be heroes. Heroism in Creation is defined around ancient mythology and heroic Solars can be monsters. Enjoy!<br /> Player: Awesome, a fantasy game that doesn't shove morality down my throat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say &quot;Doesn't shove morality down my throat&quot;. That sounds like the response of someone who wants to avoid moral questions or wants an excuse to behave badly.<br /> <br /> It's more it's <br /> <br /> &quot;The morality of powerful people isn't identifiable by the color of their anima, like in real life?!&quot; <br /> <br /> and <br /> <br /> &quot;Awesome! So Solar characters can be any of those awesome charismatic heroes from literature and real life who weren't necessarily very &quot;good&quot;? Who didn't have personalities that could just be called &quot;good&quot; or &quot;evil&quot; as much as &quot;human&quot;?&quot;<br /> <br /> No one's trying to avoid morality or &quot;good people&quot; just because they think it's limiting and limited to have it turn up in splat-centric terms. <br /> <br /> If Solars are good or not (and I think, if we look at the whole history of the game, in canon, it's &quot;not&quot;), Ten Sheaves and Janest still exist. There is still beauty and nobility in the world to stir the soul, even if it's not color coded by splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T12:08:09-07:00","id":90369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90359#post90359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This sounds to me like an invalid-but-inductive argument, i.e., &quot;Given that someone is good, it's overwhelmingly likely that they'll be a Solar, even if not necessarily guaranteed.&quot; Which is a workable approach, except that I have no idea where you're getting that as a premise. I haven't seen anyone argue that Creation has only a few hundred good people, and several people arguing the converse, so the induction's pretty weak - and I definitely haven't seen anyone arguing &quot;Solar if and only if good.&quot;<br /> <br /> Again, not agreeing with hippokrene in general here, but I think you're stepping beyond solid ground on this line of critique.</div> </div> </div> </div>It stems mostly from this idea that Solars specifically need to be good people some how. Those people through the thread arguing that seem to cite Solars as good heroes, Solars changing the world, and in one case, a historically exemplary Solar being said to &quot;Not really be a Solar, probably an Infernal instead&quot; in persuit for an idea for Solar Exalted specifically being good.<br /> <br /> The issue I take is that why Solars. Why can this not be spread to other Exalts? No one has presented why only Solars are brought into this discussion. If I were to grant it, however, the setting breaks. Dragon-Blooded, Lunar, Abyssals and Infernals outright cannot be &quot;good guys at start&quot; in order ofr a lot of the stories we expect for the setting to work. So we then find ourselves back to Solars and good being a criteron for <i>their</i> Exaltation. This in turn leads to problems I keep hammering at (introduction of objective good, confusing of where unlikable characters stand as Solars, and so on). Among them is the induction as you summarize it.<br /> <br /> I admit it's deliberately hyperbolic. I bring it up in part because there seems to be this want of Solars to be good guys, but just as easily an argument can be made to make all other Exalts or supernaturals bad guys. And while this seems unneded, I've seen enough times hwere this is brought up (in this thread even, where Sinbad being bad means he's obviously an Infernal, not a Solar). I am only trying to show how this imbalance of presentation between Solar Exalted and other beings can lead to pretty awful assumptions that or justifications for awful baseline to make the black/white presentation starker and reasonably so. It leads to either the goodness of the Solars being pointless (as it's no different from the general population and so a waste of words that tries to elimiante subtext) or it can be brandied as a justification to villainize any Exalt you personally don't like (whcih I have seen done enough to not want to give any fodder to it).<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T12:19:25-07:00","id":90375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90258#post90258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is my preferred introduction -<br /> Text: Solars are heroes and good guys. The supreme god has granted you the power to smite the everloving shit out of your enemies. Enjoy!<br /> Player: But what does that mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>Remove &quot;and good guys&quot; from that and I'll agree 100%. Unless I grossly misunderstand your position, you consider &quot;hero&quot; to encompass &quot;good guy&quot; anyway, so it's a meaningless addition to you, but removing it would make the follow-up question seem more valid.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T12:25:29-07:00","id":90379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90345#post90345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We seem to be operating under a very different set of assumptions.<br /> <br /> You see my making this thread as akin to stepping into a boxing ring and challenging everyone to fight me. Then you're unhappy because I don't seem to be following the rules. You see this as dishonest of me.</div> </div> </div> </div>You come in stating something as fact. People have gone and argued for or agaisnt that fact. You then try to provide evidence for that fact (mainly through quote-mining and continued equivocation fallacy). Others have then tried to buoy up your stated-as-fact as the way things should be. People have shown how that if your initial view of what should be were true, the setting is undermined. If you wanted to express an opinion, state it as one. If you want to express things as a statement, defend that statement. If you want to watch people dance for your bemusement, don't wait until folks have wasted their time assuming you are trying to convince them of something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90345#post90345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see this thread as pulling out my grill and inviting everyone over for a pool party.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then preface it that way. Otherwise then yes, this thread was pointless to post, as you enver were interested in anything but watching people rant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90345#post90345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, I understand what's bothering you and would like to clarify that I don't see 'Solars are heroes' as some objectively existing fact. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>First: Stop with the conflating. It does nothing but make you look petty and arrogant. If you mena good, say good. If you mean heroic, acknowledge your definition is not that or fucking defend it. As stated through this thread: Solars are heroes. Every person agrees on that. But not in the sense you say and seem to like being cute in keep saying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90345#post90345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Nor do I see 'good people doing good deeds to make the world a better place' as statement that can be objectively assessed as any better than any other definition of heroism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except folks have demonstrated that in context of Exalted, it is an demonstrably worse one due to its undermining of setting prinicples and misleading connotations. If you then go and say that it should be that anyhow, you present a case where we aren't arguing in good faith. But as you have shown, you apparently never were. and this is somewhat an exercise to get monkeys to dance for your bemusement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90345#post90345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope that helps and you're more comfortable with my thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the sense that this is probably the last time I acknowledge your mostly irrelevant commentary save the starting off point, sure. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90345#post90345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You totally got a debate out of this thread. I've been watching you for five days now, and if that's what you wanted, then you did get it. Just not with me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been debating with people who seem to think a lot more of your opinion than you are committed to being. Which shows a few things to me: <br /> 1) You're apparently ambivilant of those who share your ideas and seek to defend them, as you are not willing to do much besides le them do the work for them.<br /> 2) You're apparently wishy-washy on what ideas you will commit to, as it appears that even when you went to defend your points it was all for show.<br /> 3) You've wasted my time when I've attempted to directly debate you. Since a lot of this thread and my comments stem in the end from me calling out <i>your posts</i> and others who then latch onto them are mistaken since you, their source, are flawed. So yes, I have been debating you. You are apparently just willing to start a debate, let it roll on for a bit, and then tell people that you never were invested. Thanks for the heads up.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T12:37:28-07:00","id":90384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90345#post90345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We seem to be operating under a very different set of assumptions.<br /> <br /> You see my making this thread as akin to stepping into a boxing ring and challenging everyone to fight me. Then you're unhappy because I don't seem to be following the rules. You see this as dishonest of me.<br /> <br /> I see this thread as pulling out my grill and inviting everyone over for a pool party.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it's like you're inviting everyone into your pool party and serving people steaks that smell suspiciously like shit and when people call you out on that and want you to prove them that they're actually steaks and thus safe to eat, you refuse to do it.<br /> <br /> Is it so strange that people refuse to eat your steakes then?<br /> <br /> But I diagress. I don't really want to get dragged into discussion about pure semanthics.<br /> <br /> Instead, I'm, going to put a different spin on this whole discussion and ask you, knowing that you have a pretty definitive idea about what &quot;hero&quot; means in Exalted, would you preffer the books to be fully prescriptive in what such terms like &quot;good&quot;, &quot;evil&quot;, &quot;heroic&quot;, &quot;villainous&quot; and so on mean in Exalted, or would you preffer the game to operate via terms that need to be defined on player-by-player basis and are never defined by the books?<br /> <br /> Because it seems to me like most of us who argue with you preffer the second option. We want our Exalted to be a little like Bioshock, you know. Strange and possible to interpret in a lot of different ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2052,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","user":"FromBeyond","date":". 03-13-2014, 03:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T14:57:52-07:00","id":90433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90384#post90384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, it's like you're inviting everyone into your pool party and serving people steaks that smell suspiciously like shit and when people call you out on that and want you to prove them that they're actually steaks and thus safe to eat, you refuse to do it.<br /> <br /> Is it so strange that people refuse to eat your steakes then?</div> </div> </div> </div>As an outside observer: Considering that in this metaphor the steaks are being brought by everyone and &quot;eating the steaks&quot; means &quot;participating in the discussion&quot; I submit that this is a tone-poor excuse for a complaint and would advise you to stick to the topic instead of clotting the thread with irksome metaconversation.<br /> <br /> I've been in a three-year argument before; the parts that entailed pixelbitching over logical fallacies were inarguably the least fun bits of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T15:51:25-07:00","id":90462,"title":"","content":"In 3e, not only are Solars axiomatically good, but ONLY Solars are allowed to be good. There will be a line on your character sheet where you write 'good' as a Solar. Everyone else is required to write 'bad'.<br /> <br /> You heard it here first, folks. Hot from the playtest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>A Green Sun Destrier</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/77-kongurous","name":"kongurous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar77_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"417"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T16:04:54-07:00","id":90472,"title":"","content":"this is a troll thread right, I mean everyone actually knows there is no objective good or bad in exalted and the premise behind an exaltation of any stripe is the willingness to use the power?<br /> <br /> I will say I only read a couple of pages before putting this up so not sure if the joke was popped or not","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T16:15:36-07:00","id":90477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dezeroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90472#post90472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">this is a troll thread right, I mean everyone actually knows there is no objective good or bad in exalted and the premise behind an exaltation of any stripe is the willingness to use the power?<br /> <br /> I will say I only read a couple of pages before putting this up so not sure if the joke was popped or not</div> </div> </div> </div>On the one hand it seems like most people are arguing about the presentation of Solars moreso than any actual requirements; they quoted SLS a while back and the gist of the whole thing was &quot;you have to balance between having that subtext there and making it text outright, which is a tough line to walk.&quot; So I think most folks here are really arguing about degrees moreso than anything, and the difference just <i>seems</i> insurmountable because the people arguing have different priorities.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, one person explicitly called out Sinbad the Sailor as a really bad Solar because he was selfish and greedy and thus a better Infernal, so.<br /> <br /> Me? I don't particularly care about the presentation as long as it's clear that there's room for people of all stripes to earn their Exaltation. Or, rephrased: if Solar Oda Nobunaga is wrong, I don't want to be right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":451,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","user":"Kirby Jerusalem","date":". 03-13-2014, 07:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T16:16:55-07:00","id":90479,"title":"","content":"Just rewatched the first couple of episodes of Samurai Champloo, and I'm reminded of how suitable Mugen and Jin are as Solars.<br /> <br /> They're absolute dicks though, and have no higher concerns than testing their sword skills.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T16:43:45-07:00","id":90495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90477#post90477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Me? I don't particularly care about the presentation as long as it's clear that there's room for people of all stripes to earn their Exaltation. Or, rephrased: if Solar Oda Nobunaga is wrong, I don't want to be right.</div> </div> </div> </div>Meanwhile, a lot of video games present him as some kind of unstoppable demonic entity.<br /> <br /> ...which would be accurate from an Immaculate perspective, anyway. Huh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T16:44:05-07:00","id":90497,"title":"","content":"@Hippokrene I feel I should say this;<br /> <br /> I do not agree with your assumption that Solars are inherently (with some exceptions) virtuous. I don't have any problem with inherently virtuous heroes, but it does not fit with what I think should be the default for Exalted. <br /> <br /> However, I do think that the game should support your style of play, absolutely. However, just as how making the default power level lower doesn't invalidate high power games, but making the default power level high makes lower power games harder, making Solars ethically undetermined is easier to turn into Solars are inherently virtuous than the other way around. One includes the other, the other excludes the other.<br /> <br /> So I think that Ex3 will satisfy us both in that I will play the default and you will play the easily adjusted version that you prefer.<br /> <br /> And I should also say that were I ever to play in a game you ran, then I would find your assumption entirely acceptable and no barrier whatsoever to an enjoyable game.<br /> <br /> Just to clarify, I think your point is valid and sound, I just have a different preference and think that for the default game, it creates a wider options of play experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T16:53:49-07:00","id":90501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dezeroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90472#post90472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">this is a troll thread right, I mean everyone actually knows there is no objective good or bad in exalted and the premise behind an exaltation of any stripe is the willingness to use the power?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, is there no objective good or bad in Exalted?<br /> <br /> The thing about 1e was it let you decide. If you believe in existance of some form of cosmic principle of good, you can say that it exists for your Creation and you will find things in the narrative to support this point. Or you may think that there is no objective standard. That's ok, the setting will support that too.<br /> <br /> 2e was clumsy in this regard. It tried a bit too hard to present the setting in a straightforward way. It just didn't go far enough with it. This resulted in people arguining endlessly about what it was supposed to actually mean. If you're supposed to break your destiny over the knee or if it's unavoidable spiral of doom. At the same time, it was clear that it IS one of those. We just had no idea which one. It's kinda like the ending of Mass Effect 3. You're supposed to decide yourself what it means, but nothing in the rest of the game suggests that you should, so you're left confused as to what is going on.<br /> <br /> Hopefully 3e will be clear in that it will let us decide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2052,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","user":"FromBeyond","date":". 03-13-2014, 07:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-14T07:37:13-07:00","id":90891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90501#post90501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know, is there no objective good or bad in Exalted?<br /> <br /> The thing about 1e was it let you decide. If you believe in existance of some form of cosmic principle of good, you can say that it exists for your Creation and you will find things in the narrative to support this point. Or you may think that there is no objective standard. That's ok, the setting will support that too.<br /> <br /> 2e was clumsy in this regard. It tried a bit too hard to present the setting in a straightforward way. It just didn't go far enough with it. This resulted in people arguining endlessly about what it was supposed to actually mean. If you're supposed to break your destiny over the knee or if it's unavoidable spiral of doom. At the same time, it was clear that it IS one of those. We just had no idea which one. It's kinda like the ending of Mass Effect 3. You're supposed to decide yourself what it means, but nothing in the rest of the game suggests that you should, so you're left confused as to what is going on.<br /> <br /> Hopefully 3e will be clear in that it will let us decide.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shinma Nirguna, among its aspects, contained Advaita Iraivan - god, the absolute. Nirguna does not exist, and neither do its aspects. Hence, there is no absolute authority around, nor any absolute assurance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-14T08:55:21-07:00","id":90928,"title":"","content":"If I want to play a good guy, I play a good guy, even if the setting tells me there's no objective good. If I want him to believe in objective good (however I might define it at the moment), I play him like that even if the setting flat out tells me he's wrong. Fuck no, I'll prove the setting wrong if I want to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-14T20:52:55-07:00","id":91365,"title":"","content":"Why does it matter if there's an objective good in the setting? It matters in the real world, because it what we should be doing. Exalted is just a game, a role-playing game. All that matters is what the PCs and NPCs believe is good.<br /> <br /> Or, to phrase it an entirely different way:<br /> Of course there is an objective good in the setting, because some things are objectively good and some are bad. And these things are in the setting. Serial killers are still evil, charitable doctors are still good. But nothing in the setting is enforcing that. There's no all-knowing God who knows exactly what's objectively good and evil and rewards or punishes appropriately.* So while PCs can and should argue about it, it's not DnD where Pelor is good and Vecna is bad. And such, I see no reason why the setting should say &quot;Solars are good&quot; even if it's only just most rather than all of them, when nothing else in the setting works like that, everything is nuanced. In fact I see no reason why the setting should say anyone else is good, or evil. You don't need to be told &quot;guys, Mask of Winters is evil!&quot; because you can judge for yourself. The point is you think about what's good and bad, rather than just reading &quot;goblins are Chaotic Evil, but Elves are Chaotic Good&quot;.<br /> So when your Solar is a good guy/girl, it's because he/she <i>chose</i> to be a good guy/girl (man, sometimes I wish English worked like Mandarin and lacked gender pronouns).<br /> <br /> *And of course, this is what a lot of people believe is the case in the real world. But just because there is no universal believed standard for good, and even if there is no spiritual entity or karmic system based on it, that doesn't mean that objective good doesn't exist in the real world. I don't really understand why people are saying that because there's no objective good promoted or enforced by the setting, this makes it a horrific crapsack doomed world with no hope. Unless you believe in God/Karma, etc, surely that's the same in the real world? Nothing's enforcing, deciding, or even perfectly understanding objective good, but that doesn't mean it doesn't exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 03-15-2014, 12:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T16:46:41-07:00","id":92539,"title":"","content":"Personally I see Solars as righteous beings, rather than good. Because if Warhammer 40k has taught me anything, it's that 'righteous' does not automatically mean 'good'. More specifically, I think a Solar should embody at least ONE of the virtues, even if not in a particularly good or wholesome manner. Exalt a warrior who drinks and fucks everything she sees because she'll fight to her last breath (and then swing once more for good measure), an assassin with perfect self-control and a love for the thrill of the kill, etc etc. If Sol judged people by his own standards of good, after all, it's doubtful he'd ever exalt anyone.<br /> <br /> That said, Evil McBadguy exalting as a solar should be the exception rather than the rule. Much like the Lunar who lives in the city, or the Abyssal who loves animals, or the Sidereal who thinks fate is bullcrap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T17:13:32-07:00","id":92547,"title":"","content":"&quot;Oh, Black Dynamite, you're so <i>righteous</i>.&quot;<br /> &quot;This is also true.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T18:34:26-07:00","id":92559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=92539#post92539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, Evil McBadguy exalting as a solar should be the exception rather than the rule. Much like the <b>Lunar who lives in the city</b>, or the Abyssal who loves animals, or the Sidereal who thinks fate is bullcrap.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why we can't have nice things.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/726-amine-hsu","name":"Amine Hsu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar726_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T18:52:50-07:00","id":92564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amine Hsu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=92559#post92559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is why we can't have nice things.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>In my defense, what I know about how Lunars are usually played could fill a thimble halfway. And what I know about Lunars comes entirely from KoC","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T20:29:22-07:00","id":92611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=92539#post92539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I see Solars as righteous beings, rather than good. Because if Warhammer 40k has taught me anything, it's that 'righteous' does not automatically mean 'good'. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Different take-aways on &quot;righteousness&quot; I think. As it seems to me in 40K, &quot;righteousness&quot; more or less is a post-hoc thing. Your acts being righteous or not is not some fact. It's something decided after the fact by those in authority to jusitfy their actions. As far as I can tell, the only decent human I see brought up a lot is the Emperor. ANd he got hosed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=92539#post92539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... More specifically, I think a Solar should embody at least ONE of the virtues, even if not in a particularly good or wholesome manner. Exalt a warrior who drinks and fucks everything she sees because she'll fight to her last breath (and then swing once more for good measure), an assassin with perfect self-control and a love for the thrill of the kill, etc etc. If Sol judged people by his own standards of good, after all, it's doubtful he'd ever exalt anyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>The use of &quot;virtuous&quot; instead of &quot;good&quot; in a weird way doesn't fix a lot I find. It merely shifts the burden fo terms at use and adds a value statement. Now the Sun being a god of Virtue does help in that bias being explicit. But it should always be noted that Virtues in Exalted are not a priori good. They are very much classical Aristotelian ones: a good Virtue is a balance of two extremes. Anyone really can be found on that spectrum I think. I would rather it just be capability to acts that the Sun likes, than quality of character he judges more.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=92539#post92539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, Evil McBadguy exalting as a solar should be the exception rather than the rule. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>See above on issue sin this. Mainly if there's a filter that makes said &quot;bad&quot; people less likely amongst Solars in any amount than the general population's tendency towards &quot;badness&quot;, that means Solar Exaltation or the Sun can consistently and regularly identify goodness. Which means that &quot;goodness&quot; is a quality that can be quantified and counted on. Which makes it independent of subjective biases, in other words, objective. Any amount of &quot;bad is the exception&quot; or &quot;good is the norm&quot; in describing an Exalt makes good and bad real features to impact Exaltation. And thus undermines the lack of such things being real traits out in the world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=92539#post92539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Much like the Lunar who lives in the city, or the Abyssal who loves animals, or the Sidereal who thinks fate is bullcrap.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing in the nature of these Exaltations or the people who Exalt as them prevents them from being any of these.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T20:54:41-07:00","id":92623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=92611#post92611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Different take-aways on &quot;righteousness&quot; I think. As it seems to me in 40K, &quot;righteousness&quot; more or less is a post-hoc thing. Your acts being righteous or not is not some fact. It's something decided after the fact by those in authority to jusitfy their actions. As far as I can tell, the only decent human I see brought up a lot is the Emperor. ANd he got hosed.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Emperor a GOOD person? Shows what you know about the series :P<br /> <br /> Joke aside, 'Righteous' in that universe is generally defined as 'Im doing what's less sickeningly evil'.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The use of &quot;virtuous&quot; instead of &quot;good&quot; in a weird way doesn't fix a lot I find. It merely shifts the burden fo terms at use and adds a value statement. Now the Sun being a god of Virtue does help in that bias being explicit. But it should always be noted that Virtues in Exalted are not a priori good. They are very much classical Aristotelian ones: a good Virtue is a balance of two extremes. Anyone really can be found on that spectrum I think. I would rather it just be capability to acts that the Sun likes, than quality of character he judges more. </div> </div> </div>So a virtue can be bad or good...Isn't that what I said?<br /> <br /> Also, I'm not suggesting a ruleset, why are you treating it like one?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> See above on issue sin this. Mainly if there's a filter that makes said &quot;bad&quot; people less likely amongst Solars in any amount than the general population's tendency towards &quot;badness&quot;, that means Solar Exaltation or the Sun can consistently and regularly identify goodness. Which means that &quot;goodness&quot; is a quality that can be quantified and counted on. Which makes it independent of subjective biases, in other words, objective. Any amount of &quot;bad is the exception&quot; or &quot;good is the norm&quot; in describing an Exalt makes good and bad real features to impact Exaltation. And thus undermines the lack of such things being real traits out in the world. </div> </div> </div>... I'm not sure I understand, your problem is that it's not realistic? &gt;.&gt;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nothing in the nature of these Exaltations or the people who Exalt as them prevents them from being any of these.<br /> <br /> And stuff. </div> </div> </div>Exactly. Nothing prevents such exalted from coming about, but they're still rare (as far as I know), right?... Though, those may have been bad examples.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T22:01:33-07:00","id":92650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=92623#post92623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Emperor a GOOD person? Shows what you know about the series :P</div> </div> </div> </div>The Emperor is good by some of the things i consider good. Namely he seemed to be wanting to lead humanity into an age of technology and enlightenment when the Horus Heresy happened and now he's more or less a corpse with his soul stapled to it. He was decent. His cult not so much and he still had issues. Like you know, being an emperor.<br /> <br /> J<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=92623#post92623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oke aside, 'Righteous' in that universe is generally defined as 'Im doing what's less sickeningly evil'.<br /> <br /> So a virtue can be bad or good...Isn't that what I said?<br /> <br /> Also, I'm not suggesting a ruleset, why are you treating it like one?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorta. I just think that it's so broad and post-hoc that making it a criterion is pointnless and more restricting than it seems at first.<br /> <br /> it's a problem because you're adding to the pile of &quot;It should be this and not that' as what Solar Exaltation should be that this thread is full of. Even if it is not a rule, i think it is bad to even try and make it fanon or a regular bit to suggest for PCs. &quot;Solars should be these kind of good/virtueous/righteous/other arbitrary quality&quot; is not a position I think can be argued for without underming the setting. Especially when most terms are just as ambiguous as good, or so broad as to not have a point being there in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=92623#post92623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... I'm not sure I understand, your problem is that it's not realistic? &gt;.&gt;</div> </div> </div> </div>It's incoherent in the context of what we're told on Creation's workings. Realism isn't what I'm against it for. It's illogical and leads to absurdity. Righteousness is often presented as baiscally often &quot;Good by another name&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=92623#post92623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly. Nothing prevents such exalted from coming about, but they're still rare (as far as I know), right?... Though, those may have been bad examples.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're awful examples. Lunars have no bias towards cities whatsoever, and often a lot of the &quot;barbarian lands' of the Lunar Exalted are places with major cities. Nothing about how an Abyssal feels about animals seems to matter or even prevent them from killing them and using zombies. And a lot of Sidereals are under no obligation to actually like their job whatsoever. None of these are at all useful or defining things of these Exalts and probably, again, have no real expectations to be different than any other randomly selected part of the population expected or able to deeds associated with that Exal task. None of these traits would prevent Exaltation into that Exalt sort, and it treats &quot;virtue or good or whatever&quot; as more or less &quot;Likes ot live in cities&quot; which is making it more &quot;real&quot; than it hsould be by a good amount.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T23:26:10-07:00","id":92671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=92623#post92623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly. Nothing prevents such exalted from coming about, but they're still rare (as far as I know), right?... Though, those may have been bad examples.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing about living in cities makes it an uncommon state for Lunars. They are barbarians in that they live in places that re culturally and politically not part of the dominant powers and they tend to have horrible fashion sense. Also writers while describing them might draw upon imagery reminiscent of Barbarian literature, like Conan.<br /> <br /> Unless we are talking Ex1, then using toilet paper causes your exaltation to fly off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/726-amine-hsu","name":"Amine Hsu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar726_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T23:43:16-07:00","id":92675,"title":"","content":"All Solars are virtuous in some way, by Exalted's virtue system. They all have at least one of their virtues at an above-average level. A regular human might well have all their virtues at 2. A Solar never does.<br /> It's also why (in 2nd ed) IIRC they're the only Exalts who can start with a virtue at 4 without spending freebies.<br /> <br /> But that's not at all the same as being good (and using the word &quot;righteous&quot; isn't a good description either, it just means the same thing). Valour 3 warrior guy who just loves fighting, and doesn't care if people get hurt, isn't good. Conviction 3 warrior-queen who's willing to plunge the Scavenger Lands into war to carve out her own glorious empire, isn't good.<br /> <br /> As to the Emperor from 40K, he was an intolerant, genocidal, xenophobic, megalomaniac. And would make an absolutely excellent Solar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 03-17-2014, 02:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-17T00:26:07-07:00","id":92678,"title":"","content":"Every Solar you will ever meet is either brave, honorable, caring, or stubborn as a mule.<br /> <br /> Some Solars with be two or three of those things. Some rare Solars will be all four. Few of them are what we might call &quot;good,&quot; though they might see themselves as heroes.<br /> <br /> The Sun will honor your bravery if you are a child who stands up to an armed man to defend an innocent slave, and he will honor your bravery if you ride out alone with a firewand and a whip to singlehandedly put down a slave rebellion. He does not care if you're good, for some modern definition of good. He cares if you are brave.<br /> <br /> The Sun will recognize your honor if you fast on a mountaintop and eschew life's temptations in search of enlightenment, only coming down to heal the sick and always refusing their attempts to repay you. The sun will recognize your honor if you give your word to your dark ninja master that you will slay an innocent man, and then you keep your word despite the obstacles in your way, because you have given your oath and it binds you. The Sun does not care if you are good, only that you have mastery over yourself.<br /> <br /> The Sun will grant you power if you are caring. When you spare a defeated enemy out of mercy, the Sun is with you. When you surrender instead of fighting, because you have fallen in love with the invading general, and you doom hundreds of your own people to suffering and oppression because you refuse to harm one who you love, the Sun is with you. He cares not the object of your compassion, but he sees his own love for the unworthy reflected in you and recognizes it for a strength, and he will give you the power to fight for it.<br /> <br /> The Sun will honor your conviction if you refuse to offer mercy to a murderer or a heretic or a blasphemer, even though they are your own child. The Sun will honor your conviction if you steadfastly refuse to betray your heretic child to the authorities even when starved and tortured. The Sun doesn't care if you're an absolute fanatic or a an unswerving juggernaut of justice: he only cares that you will move the world rather than give an inch.<br /> <br /> The Sun chooses great men and women: people who will reforge the world in their own image, people in whom he sees reflected back at him <i>his </i>own image. The Sun's perfection unopposed would scorch the earth and wipe out all life (that's the reason Night was invented), and the wise observer will note that the unimpeded rule of the Solars at their height was not dissimilar. The Solars are glorious and mighty and strong, and yes, some of them are even good. It is not a requirement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 03-17-2014, 03:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-17T02:54:50-07:00","id":92708,"title":"","content":"In order to get to the core of what heroic is meant to mean in Exalted's context, let's go back to the basics of what inspired Grabowski:<br /> <br /> Dinosaurs Rule The Earth!<br /> / \\<br /> / Eastern Epic +<br /> Western Epic Chinese Novels<br /> / \\ | \\<br /> / Classical | \\<br /> Lord Dunsany Histories | Floating World<br /> \\ / | Prints<br /> \\ / Wuxia |<br /> Pulp Fantasy \\ Anime<br /> / \\ \\ /<br /> Riverworld* Pulp Revival CRPGs<br /> \\ | /<br /> \\ v /<br /> +-----&gt; Exalted &lt;-----------------+<br /> <br /> <br /> So, yes, anything from classical Greek heroism to Shonen protagonists are valid. Also remember you can play Exalted in different ways going from 'Grand Theft Yeddim' to more serious styles. This means any individual Exalted campaign is going to be highlighting different themes and might even be in a different genre altogether. <br /> <br /> Now, what does this mean? It just means that the characters in your group have to be able to play together in the story created by the ST. There might, or there might not be room for paladins and/or villains in the party.<br /> <br /> That said, to focus more on classical Greek heroism vs modern heroism: the sacking of Troy came down to rape and enslave the women, kill the men, salt the earth. This was standard practice. These kind of heroes are obviously not for every table or campaign. Many players are not able to identify with such characters, even when they try. From what I have seen in games, completely abandoning the modern definition of heroism is pretty hard.<br /> In my experience, aiming for the middle ground instead of extremes, namely good guys with flaws or bad guys with redeeming features, seems to work best in the long term.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-17T08:39:57-07:00","id":92807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amine Hsu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=92671#post92671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nothing about living in cities makes it an uncommon state for Lunars. They are barbarians in that they live in places that re culturally and politically not part of the dominant powers and they tend to have horrible fashion sense. Also writers while describing them might draw upon imagery reminiscent of Barbarian literature, like Conan.<br /> <br /> Unless we are talking Ex1, then using toilet paper causes your exaltation to fly off.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I know about Exalted comes from KoC and a single game of 2e that died off fairly quickly. So yeah, probably thinking 1e... and the Sidereal one was just me being an idiot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=92650#post92650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Emperor is good by some of the things i consider good. Namely he seemed to be wanting to lead humanity into an age of technology and enlightenment when the Horus Heresy happened and now he's more or less a corpse with his soul stapled to it. He was decent. His cult not so much and he still had issues. Like you know, being an emperor.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Emperor was responsible for creating most of the practices in 40k that are evil just for the lulz (see: servitors) killing/exiling (it's not really made clear which) two of his own sons, their legions, and anyone who talks about those two legions, destroying entire planets at a time, and the protocol of slaughtering everyone who disagrees with him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sorta. I just think that it's so broad and post-hoc that making it a criterion is pointnless and more restricting than it seems at first. </div> </div> </div>I said 'personally', again, i'm not trying to make this a ruleset -_-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> it's a problem because you're adding to the pile of &quot;It should be this and not that' as what Solar Exaltation should be that this thread is full of. Even if it is not a rule, i think it is bad to even try and make it fanon or a regular bit to suggest for PCs. &quot;Solars should be these kind of good/virtueous/righteous/other arbitrary quality&quot; is not a position I think can be argued for without underming the setting. Especially when most terms are just as ambiguous as good, or so broad as to not have a point being there in the first place. </div> </div> </div>1) The idea that &quot;Solars can't be any kind of quality whatsoever or it breaks the setting&quot; is even more absurd than the idea that they're paladins &gt;.&gt; They are SOMETHING, else there's no point in having them be in the setting, least of all as main characters.<br /> <br /> 2) Oh joy, you think there's such a thing as right or wrong <i>fanon</i>. -_- This'll be fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-17T10:27:31-07:00","id":92858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Angwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=92708#post92708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, to focus more on classical Greek heroism vs modern heroism: the sacking of Troy came down to rape and enslave the women, kill the men, salt the earth. This was standard practice. These kind of heroes are obviously not for every table or campaign. Many players are not able to identify with such characters, even when they try. From what I have seen in games, completely abandoning the modern definition of heroism is pretty hard.<br /> In my experience, aiming for the middle ground instead of extremes, namely good guys with flaws or bad guys with redeeming features, seems to work best in the long term.</div> </div> </div> </div>I appreciate this for being a measured opinion that treats Exalted as an adaptible game system rather than an ideological battleground.<br /> <br /> It speaks to what I think was the original motive for this thread. Namely, that the prevailing community opinion was that Exalted is a game about corruption, and it seemed like if you wanted to play a straightforward Good Guys Right The World game using the setting, you were deemed unfaithful to the source material. And my contribution to this thread has largely (and very unfortunately) worked within the conceptual framework of Exalted as a story unto itself which you can be right or wrong about, rather than a toolkit for creating stories that are interesting to you and your group.<br /> <br /> I'm not proud of that. I'd like to affirm now that I am totally cool with anyone using Exalted's setting and rules to tell whatever story is compelling to them. I hope others will join me in that affirmation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2404-chant","name":"Chant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2404_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-17T10:46:47-07:00","id":92867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=92807#post92807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...The Emperor was responsible for creating most of the practices in 40k that are evil just for the lulz (see: servitors) killing/exiling (it's not really made clear which) two of his own sons, their legions, and anyone who talks about those two legions, destroying entire planets at a time, and the protocol of slaughtering everyone who disagrees with him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, scale of evilness. It's 40K. As far as I understand, the Tau are the ones with the least crimes against sapience on their docket, while Nids and Orks are not so much evil as just....antithetical to everyone else's existence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=92807#post92807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...<br /> 1) The idea that &quot;Solars can't be any kind of quality whatsoever or it breaks the setting&quot; is even more absurd than the idea that they're paladins &gt;.&gt; They are SOMETHING, else there's no point in having them be in the setting, least of all as main characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue is that people keep wanting to put some quality of &quot;People I think are good&quot; spun in various different ways. Which is what I'm against. So far I have yet to see presented a view of good or a word that's good-but-not that isn't in the end, &quot;I don't want this bad guy I don't like to count as a Solar.&quot; My response is that the moment you put such a qualifier in things, things go stupid fast. It's an unsustainable premise.<br /> <br /> The only thing I generally am for as a quality for Solars is greatness. And as I have defined it (besides more or less &quot;goodness or arbitrary mroalness&quot;) it is more on scope. Greatness isn't a quality of character, but a scale of act. And Solar Exalted are capable and gifted to be <i>great</i> people. People who do big things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=92807#post92807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Oh joy, you think there's such a thing as right or wrong <i>fanon</i>. -_- This'll be fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the context of Creation, the idea of some thing outside of what a character subjectively judges as right or wrong is fanon. The game is premised greatly on an idea that morality is not something that exists out in the world but what judges things is instead something that sapient entities in Creation do. Any attempt to say that an Exaltation should be that is fanon. Any attempt to say that the books should highlight folks who aren't some pre-conceived view of &quot;not good enough to be a Solar&quot; is trying ot elminate the subtext of the game by making them weird and aberrant, instead of the logical outgrowth of great people with power and no real check on things that the subtext was supposed to emphasize.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-17T13:50:50-07:00","id":92962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=92858#post92858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I appreciate this for being a measured opinion that treats Exalted as an adaptible game system rather than an ideological battleground.<br /> <br /> It speaks to what I think was the original motive for this thread. Namely, that the prevailing community opinion was that Exalted is a game about corruption, and it seemed like if you wanted to play a straightforward Good Guys Right The World game using the setting, you were deemed unfaithful to the source material. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>First off, that's not what folks arguing against you are for or support. I don't think the theme is corruption. Ith ink the game's theme is that humanity is a combination of all the good and bad, and that trying to take the &quot;heroes reborn are obviously good&quot; at face value actually breaks down as feasable when pressure is put to it. It also is against source material since &quot;Straight Guys Right the World&quot; is actually not what a lot of the source material actually is to much an extant.<br /> <br /> And much of the reactions have been against the OP's (apparently meant to only <i>appear </i>to be insinuating debate) to the idea of this above being a proscriptive. Heroes aren't this in her games or that the game shoudl support it. It's that heroes <i>are these things</i> and that things not that are aberrant to it. And that's what has been aruged against all thread in the simplest form: Heroes are good, Solars are heroes, ergo Solars are good. The issue is for me and a good chunk of everyone else mentioend (and yet to actually be argued against besides &quot;the feels&quot;) has been the first point. The game as it is doens't work on that definition of heroism. End of story. That I want a world that's corrupt or not is putting words in our mouths and not actually addressing our complaints of the poor framing of the entire OP.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=92858#post92858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... And my contribution to this thread has largely (and very unfortunately) worked within the conceptual framework of Exalted as a story unto itself which you can be right or wrong about, rather than a toolkit for creating stories that are interesting to you and your group.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exalted is a toolbox to give you the tools you want, sure. The issue is that the sort of stories it is meant to support in your telling are not out of the box the cliche, sappy, comicbook/kids movie &quot;good guys versus bad guys&quot; stories. The game is written to emulate more nuanced and generally less black and white source material where &quot;making the world better&quot; aren't necessarily clear cut, easy, or possible ethically. This is why source material is often noted as Howard's Conan, Tanith Lee's Flat Earth, <i>Ninja Scroll</i> or history.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=92858#post92858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not proud of that. I'd like to affirm now that I am totally cool with anyone using Exalted's setting and rules to tell whatever story is compelling to them. I hope others will join me in that affirmation.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fine. That doesn't address the OP more or less saying that her preferred style is objectively the right one. And which a lot of others in this thread seem to think Exalted <i>should</i> be to some extent, or should support. It can support that all day. It's just not going to support it explicitly. This was never the case in the past save in the most hackneyed styles. It isn't the case of the source material the game seeks to emulate. And it isn't the likely directly that the game line will go in the future.<br /> <br /> &quot;Do what you want and let's all just be happy feel good people who all do great&quot; is a cop out as far as fantasy goes. Exalted and really many RPGs are best when they have a strong thesis and view of what kind of games they are and worlds they emulate. If Exalted wanted to be a catch-all fanatsy game that does the spectrum from gritty shithole 40K to an the old GI Joe cartoon morality, that's one thing. But the game is written an dwill be written with a fairly solid idea of what it wants to be and emulate. Strong vision isntead &quot;Everyone's opinion is valid!&quot; leads to a better written game.<br /> <br /> So in short, no, I won't support the &quot;Exalted can do anything and that's fine!&quot; thing, becuase that' smore or less to me the, &quot;Everyone's opinion is valid and special.&quot; thing. I would rather have an ability to call out an idea as patently bad than be on self-appointed feel good high horse.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-17T15:06:01-07:00","id":92990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=92962#post92962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's fine. That doesn't address the OP more or less saying that her preferred style is objectively the right one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am by no means a paragon of reading comprehension, but I feel secure in saying that that is not anything approximating a charitable reading of the OP. It is, in fact, a pointlessly confrontational reading.<br /> <br /> It is eminently preferable that, in your quest to avoid any high horses, you not stoop to throwing shit while you talk. That tends to run the conversation downhill in a hurry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-17T15:14:27-07:00","id":92998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=92867#post92867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, scale of evilness. It's 40K. As far as I understand, the Tau are the ones with the least crimes against sapience on their docket, while Nids and Orks are not so much evil as just....antithetical to everyone else's existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's arguable that the Tau are only so low on the scale because they're fairly new to the 40k galaxy but even they have implied mass sterilization of human populations and mind control of their own race.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The issue is that people keep wanting to put some quality of &quot;People I think are good&quot; spun in various different ways. Which is what I'm against. So far I have yet to see presented a view of good or a word that's good-but-not that isn't in the end, &quot;I don't want this bad guy I don't like to count as a Solar.&quot; My response is that the moment you put such a qualifier in things, things go stupid fast. It's an unsustainable premise. </div> </div> </div>I would classify it as 'someone who does great things', but that's just me, let's move on.<br /> <br /> I'm talking about a general feel or idea for what a Solar is, not what ABSOLUTELY MUST BE OR FIRE RAINS FROM THE HEAVENS AND EATS YOUR GOLDFISH. My view isn't 'a solar must be good or he's not a solar', it's 'solars seem like good people because enough of them ARE good people'.<br /> <br /> Hence, 'righteous'. Usually seen as good, but plenty are just blood templars.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The only thing I generally am for as a quality for Solars is greatness. And as I have defined it (besides more or less &quot;goodness or arbitrary mroalness&quot;) it is more on scope. Greatness isn't a quality of character, but a scale of act. And Solar Exalted are capable and gifted to be <i>great</i> people. People who do big things. </div> </div> </div>The two are not mutually exclusive, and I would argue that one can flow from the other. People with great characters do great things, and people who can do great things become great people in the process. Especially in a world where you are so monumentally powerful that the only challenges for you are things big and bad enough to threaten all of existence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the context of Creation, the idea of some thing outside of what a character subjectively judges as right or wrong is fanon. The game is premised greatly on an idea that morality is not something that exists out in the world but what judges things is instead something that sapient entities in Creation do. Any attempt to say that an Exaltation should be that is fanon. Any attempt to say that the books should highlight folks who aren't some pre-conceived view of &quot;not good enough to be a Solar&quot; is trying ot elminate the subtext of the game by making them weird and aberrant, instead of the logical outgrowth of great people with power and no real check on things that the subtext was supposed to emphasize.<br /> <br /> And stuff. </div> </div> </div>When did I say any of that? When did I suggest an objective morality in the vein of DnD? The whole point of bringing 40k was to point out that being a good guy isn't the same thing as having a Good alignment. My first solar was a selfish, self-absorbed assassin who may or may not have been planning to murder one of his circle-mates and exalted because he shot a dragon-blood through the eye on one of his contracts.<br /> <br /> (also, someone mentioned earlier that Exaltations would not be making the choice in 3e, but the god of the respective exaltation. Which i find incredibly lame and head-scratching, but whatever)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-17T15:33:22-07:00","id":93013,"title":"","content":"I can't really endorse Blaque's position completely any longer (I would have been happy to take &quot;to each their own&quot; out presented earlier), nor can I speak for it, but for whatever it helps, I suspect &quot;Solars seem like good people because enough of them ARE&quot; is going to be troubling to some. The counterpoint being: &quot;there's no such thing as a &quot;good&quot; person in any absolute sense.&quot; So any Solar that seems like one is being looked at from the perspective of certain moral judgments that cannot be universalized to Creation (or perhaps even Earth). Rather, they're just people. Some of them do things we would consider &quot;good.&quot; Most if those things are, nevertheless, fucking up someone else's day, and it's likely they would not consider the Solar good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/926-yishten","name":"Yishten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar926_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-17T15:40:19-07:00","id":93016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=92998#post92998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's arguable that the Tau are only so low on the scale because they're fairly new to the 40k galaxy but even they have implied mass sterilization of human populations and mind control of their own race.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much. The assumption is that they're only decent because they're so young. It's implied that humanity wasn't nearly as viciously expansive and well... Imperialistic in it's infancy. Give them 40k years and psykers and they will put humanity to shame.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-17T16:34:39-07:00","id":93064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yishten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=93013#post93013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't really endorse Blaque's position completely any longer (I would have been happy to take &quot;to each their own&quot; out presented earlier), nor can I speak for it, but for whatever it helps, I suspect &quot;Solars seem like good people because enough of them ARE&quot; is going to be troubling to some. The counterpoint being: &quot;there's no such thing as a &quot;good&quot; person in any absolute sense.&quot; So any Solar that seems like one is being looked at from the perspective of certain moral judgments that cannot be universalized to Creation (or perhaps even Earth). Rather, they're just people. Some of them do things we would consider &quot;good.&quot; Most if those things are, nevertheless, fucking up someone else's day, and it's likely they would not consider the Solar good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much how I feel on the latter.<br /> <br /> I don't think in general there's such thing as a &quot;good person&quot;. I think their are people who as a sum of things did good stuff. But all that I can work on is someone's acts. Their inherent qualities really aren't something I have access to or measure for. Creation isn't much better in that regard as I see it. <br /> <br /> There's also a bit of earlier where the opposite of malice is not goodness. I <i>don't</i> think a lot of Exalted malicious, at least anymore than anyone else is. I don't as a result get to think they are good.<br /> <br /> As for live and let live, I generally admit it's not the position that will be the nice one, but I generally think that a position that in the end is &quot;Everyone is equally right&quot; means no one can be shown to be wrong and so I tend to reject them as a bit of feel good back-outs.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-17T17:16:27-07:00","id":93085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=92990#post92990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am by no means a paragon of reading comprehension, but I feel secure in saying that that is not anything approximating a charitable reading of the OP. It is, in fact, a pointlessly confrontational reading.</div> </div> </div> </div>The original post is presented as a statement of fact. It presents a statement, that as paraphrased about a few dozen times but I'll repeat a fucking 'gain, &quot;Solars are heroes, heroes are good people who do good things to make the world better, ergo Solars are good people who do good things to make the world better.&quot; It was presented as a normative statement. It was presented without anything else to say that it's opinion. And so folks went and debated it. This is in a context where Solars who don't fit her prescirption &quot;aren't heroes&quot; and are meant to be highlighted as exceptions. I also rejected this for various reasons. She argues that if Solars were amoral to start with, the First Age doesn't work (post #12). She repeatedly uses the term in her definiton of it in order to put words in other's mouths even after folks have rejected her definition as what hero means.<br /> <br /> I and a few others have shown how her definition is not logical in the context of things. It is not sound. It leads to absurdities in the setting as granted. It is a poor position and the burden of defending it shifted to her, in what again, had seemed like her debating and defending her case.<br /> <br /> This goes on for a while. Complete with her trying to justify her inclusion of exclusion of various figures as Exalts based on her ideals of Solar goodness and its need as a criterion of Solar Exalted. And then we get these nice quotes:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90294#post90294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your post comes from such an different viewpoint, I'm not sure how to react to it.<br /> <br /> 1) I have no interest in making or defending an argument.<br /> 2) People are under no obligation to 'refute' my non-argument.<br /> 3) I am rather satisfied with this thread and the discussions I've read/participated in, so I'm unlikely to change my communication style. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>The first point basically reads to me &quot;I get to say what I want and never will bother to defend it.&quot; Which when you just participated over the course of eight pages of a 40-page-for-me thread, means you pretty much never were going to engage people's comments with the same level of commitment as they assumed you were. This is being a dishonest debater. It's setting a trap of discussion.<br /> <br /> The second point is basically saying that her intial post and idea was a non-argument. Which is contrary to how she has reacted to cmmentary of it through the thread. This again, leads to her being dishonest in her participation in the thread or presentation in its initial argument (which if its a non-argument, she's got a froggy idea of how to express opinion).<br /> <br /> These combined with the third point more or less meant she insinuated a debate with no intention of actually doing anything but egging it on for her satisfaction. Her barbeque analogy later on more or less summarizes it: She wanted to see people dance. If I come accross as confrontational, it's because the idea that I was debating what amounted to a troll guised as an intellectual debate kind of leads one to not wanting to give that person ground to be anything but the false debater they have embraced being.<br /> <br /> Or in other words, if I come accross as confrontational, it's because the OP decided to build a debate and then pull the rug from the debaters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=92990#post92990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is eminently preferable that, in your quest to avoid any high horses, you not stoop to throwing shit while you talk. That tends to run the conversation downhill in a hurry.</div> </div> </div> </div>The OP's intial comments have been tainted by her conduct in this thread. I have my case why this is so above. I can expound on it with more quotes and contrasts if you like.<br /> <br /> As for high horses, I still hold that the hippy &quot;Every one wins in some way&quot; method of ending a discussion is something not to advocate for a few reasons:<br /> <br /> 1) It doesn't address the intial cause of this that some people, despite hippokrene's failure to debate on, do debate for. A criterion of &quot;goodness&quot; for Solars. Something that I still reject and have yet to see argued for.<br /> <br /> 2) It is often tried to be argued for by just changing the word form good to some other word that in the end, is that arguer's view of some good so it can exclude sorts of people they don't like being Solars. Which I again, think has failed since often the criteron used have rejected perfectly good Solars. See a denial that Solars are able to be Sinbad.<br /> <br /> Saying Exalted can be all of this asks too much of Exalted. As a gameline, it can't be all things from default. An ST or players can make it be those things. But that's YCMV. As far as I'm concenred, what's of any use beyond the &quot;That feels good to me because houserules&quot; is going to be what world we can look at and objectively (for us as rather omniscient observors of Creation compared to characters in it) can talk about. And to get a world that's not a morally absurd mess of undermining its own thesis, we need a means to call people's views as incompatable with that world.<br /> <br /> This combined with what I read as a snarky &quot;Aren't I so good for giving an olive leaf&quot; out tone of my high horse reaction lead to my rejection of this. It is simply a way to make everything work, without showing how that's contrary and absurd.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T10:38:17-07:00","id":93573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=92962#post92962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in short, no, I won't support the &quot;Exalted can do anything and that's fine!&quot; thing, becuase that' smore or less to me the, &quot;Everyone's opinion is valid and special.&quot; thing. I would rather have an ability to call out an idea as patently bad than be on self-appointed feel good high horse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you expect the 3e writers to omit the &quot;Game Styles&quot; section presented on p. 262 of the 2e core? I would have thought that, if there's one thing we could all agree on, it would be that the writers go out of their way to explicitly point out that their setting and rules can be used for a variety of purposes, and that storytellers are licensed and encouraged to change things to suit them better. Considering how much value has been placed on author intent in this thread, I'm surprised to see this particular aspect of author intent discarded.<br /> <br /> Can you explain the difference between your position and badwrongfun?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2404-chant","name":"Chant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2404_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T11:11:15-07:00","id":93594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=93573#post93573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you expect the 3e writers to omit the &quot;Game Styles&quot; section presented on p. 262 of the 2e core? I would have thought that, if there's one thing we could all agree on, it would be that the writers go out of their way to explicitly point out that their setting and rules can be used for a variety of purposes, and that storytellers are licensed and encouraged to change things to suit them better. Considering how much value has been placed on author intent in this thread, I'm surprised to see this particular aspect of author intent discarded.<br /> <br /> Can you explain the difference between your position and badwrongfun?</div> </div> </div> </div>He's not saying that you play the game wrong if you say &quot;Solars are good people&quot;, or that the game shouldn't allow for such deviations. He's saying that our conversation was started by hippokrene saying <i>&quot;The <u>default</u> way to play the game should be A&quot;</i> and that we're arguing about just that.<br /> <br /> Saying, <i>&quot;No, B should be the <u>default</u> game&quot;</i> isn't saying you can't play the game as A. Saying B should be the <u>default</u> is not saying A is not a good way to play the game around your table, it's not saying the book shouldn't have a sidebar or a page highligthing A, C, D, E other ways the game can be played.<br /> <br /> It's just that starting by giving out an opinion on what the <u>default</u> should be, and then saying <i>&quot;but you can play your game at home this way, how dare you accuse me of badwrongfun!&quot;</i> when people don't seem to agree is not finding common ground, it's <i>moving the goalposts</i>. And that's disingenuous.<br /> <br /> Everybody can play the game the way they want it to be. That has always been true, and nobody said the opposite (not even the writers). It's just that we're talking about THE game, not YOUR game, and both are very different things. In order to get away from what Lea (or was it Holden?) called high-attraction plots, THE game needs to have strong thematic decisions, even if no-one is forever bound by law to agree with those.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">(It's just like the Yozi not escaping thing. THE game is saying &quot;The Yozis will never escape&quot; because the devs know that some group will play that anyway, but they don't want all groups to play that scenario, and if you leave it open, a whole fucking lot of people will, to the point that not having the Reclamation in your game will become badwrongfun. You still can have the Reclamation in YOUR game. Same for Solars as Good People. A lot of groups will play that way anyway, but if you make it the canon, it will become inescapable, because it's just an easier narrative and a more simplistic thematic.)</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ultimate Jade-Screened Exalted Scholar, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304239-my-next-campaign-tdhr-peach\" target=\"_blank\">THDR : Future Dragon-Blooded campaign</a>, and other links.<br /> If you like Ex3, you can support <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/holdenshearer\" target=\"_blank\">Holden</a> on Patreon!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","name":"LeTipex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T11:38:25-07:00","id":93628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=90379#post90379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been debating with people who seem to think a lot more of your opinion than you are committed to being. Which shows a few things to me:<br /> 1) You're apparently ambivilant of those who share your ideas and seek to defend them, as you are not willing to do much besides le them do the work for them.<br /> 2) You're apparently wishy-washy on what ideas you will commit to, as it appears that even when you went to defend your points it was all for show.<br /> 3) You've wasted my time when I've attempted to directly debate you. Since a lot of this thread and my comments stem in the end from me calling out <i>your posts</i> and others who then latch onto them are mistaken since you, their source, are flawed. So yes, I have been debating you. You are apparently just willing to start a debate, let it roll on for a bit, and then tell people that you never were invested. Thanks for the heads up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand your frustration, but I also think I'm coming to understand the attitude from which hippokrene started the thread, and I hope I can alleviate your frustration by sharing that understanding.<br /> <br /> I don't think hippokrene ever meant to say &quot;the text of the source material supports this interpretation, and those who interpret otherwise are unfaithful to that source material&quot;. I think OP was a statement of personal interpretation, relying on a conceptual framework of fiction as an inherently adaptible and interpreted type of work. People can derive very different value from the same artistic expression, this forum seemed to hippokrene to be tightly focused on one particular interpretation, and wanted to present another interpretation.<br /> <br /> Like, if I encountered a discussion where people are praising Lady Gaga's Telephone because it efficiently sums up their feelings when their significant others call them while they're clubbing, and my contribution was &quot;I like it for a completely different reason: I find it to be a heartbreaking, self-aware narrative that expresses the frustration and despair of a neglected partner&quot;, I wouldn't be interested in defending that interpretation from a perspective of Lady Gaga's intent, because regardless of what she wanted to convey with the song, I derive value from my interpretation. And it would be absurd for anyone to try to convince me to like the song from the perspective of a clubber, because I don't go to clubs. All that can be accomplished by arguing about it is to sour my attitude toward something I like.<br /> <br /> So, the apparently assertive nature of hippokrene's original post may seem to &quot;obviously&quot; have been a statement of singular and unassailable truth, but that's only because hippokrene comes from a perspective where there cannot possibly <i>be</i> a singular and unassailable truth about a fictional fantasy world. It's not <i>necessary</i> to say &quot;but this is just my opinion and has no bearing on how you decide to play&quot;, because that's supposed to be a baseline assumption about a roleplaying setting. It's a little like saying &quot;cilantro is tasty&quot; and getting a response &quot;you're wrong, it tastes like soap&quot;. Why would anyone care to debate that? (Why indeed, coming from a guy who has spent altogether too much effort on doing exactly that in this thread.)<br /> <br /> Personally, my emotional reaction to hippokrene's original post was along the lines of &quot;connecting with someone else who sees Exalted like I do makes me feel a lot more comfortable enjoying the interpretation of the setting that appeals to me&quot;. I bet many of the 9 others who liked the OP felt something similar. So, with the very beginning of the thread, hippokrene succeeded in accomplishing something on which debate has no bearing. <i>That's</i> what is meant by &quot;I don't feel the need to argue my point&quot;.<br /> <br /> This is conjecture, so I'll ask: hippokrene, how did I do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2404-chant","name":"Chant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2404_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T11:41:59-07:00","id":93634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=93628#post93628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I understand your frustration, but I also think I'm coming to understand the attitude from which hippokrene started the thread, and I hope I can alleviate your frustration by sharing that understanding.<br /> <br /> I don't think hippokrene ever meant to say &quot;the text of the source material supports this interpretation, and those who interpret otherwise are unfaithful to that source material&quot;. I think OP was a statement of personal interpretation, relying on a conceptual framework of fiction as an inherently adaptible and interpreted type of work. People can derive very different value from the same artistic expression, this forum seemed to hippokrene to be tightly focused on one particular interpretation, and wanted to present another interpretation.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Hippokrene merely wanted to put forth her interpretation, why did she spend the following 10 pages arguing that she was correct and trying to quotemine the devs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T11:44:54-07:00","id":93637,"title":"","content":"@chant: I agree that was probably the case. But regretably she chose the wrong words to do it and in the process, nullified the opinions of countless other gamers that feel otherwise, many of whom jumped to defense their opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2245-quimeradc","name":"Quimeradc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T11:50:42-07:00","id":93644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=93634#post93634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If Hippokrene merely wanted to put forth her interpretation, why did she spend the following 10 pages arguing that she was correct and trying to quotemine the devs?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would try to answer this question if it weren't an abusive mischaracterisation of hippokrene's behavior in this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2404-chant","name":"Chant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2404_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T12:06:03-07:00","id":93662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=93644#post93644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would try to answer this question if it weren't an abusive mischaracterisation of hippokrene's behavior in this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>How would you characterize her behaviour in posts 131, 169, 173, 174, 176 and 179 and how do you reconcile it with your interpretation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T12:12:10-07:00","id":93669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=93662#post93662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How would you characterize her behaviour in posts 131, 169, 173, 174, 176 and 179 and how do you reconcile it with your interpretation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you explain your numbering system? As far as I can tell, <i>none</i> of those post indexes in this thread belonged to hippokrene. A couple were mine; I've since decided and declared that I'm not proud of taking an &quot;objective&quot; stance in this debate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2404-chant","name":"Chant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2404_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T12:27:41-07:00","id":93697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/87146-solars-are-heroes?p=93669#post93669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue an